        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "def-absolutely-continuous-with-respect-to-a-positive-measure",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Let $\\mu$ be a positive measure and let $\\nu$ be a signed measure or a complex measure on the same measurable space $(X,\\mathcal A)$. We say that $\\nu$ is **absolutely continuous with respect to $\\mu$**, and write\n$$\\nu\\ll\\mu,$$\nif every measurable $\\mu$-null set is also $\\nu$-null:\n$$\\mu(E)=0\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad \\nu(E)=0\\qquad(E\\in\\mathcal A).$$\nBecause every measurable subset of a $\\mu$-null set is again $\\mu$-null, this is equivalent to requiring $\\nu(F)=0$ for every measurable $F\\subseteq E$ whenever $\\mu(E)=0$.",
