          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "If $p_i>0=q_i$ for some $i$, [F1] gives $D(p\\|q)=+\\infty$, so nonnegativity holds and equality to zero is impossible. Otherwise $p_i=0$ whenever $q_i=0$; apply [F2] to $a_i=p_i$, $b_i=q_i$. Both sums equal $1$, and its left side is $D(p\\|q)$, so $D(p\\|q)\\ge0$.",
