          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume AC only for the interface to the published general definition [[def-kullback-leibler-divergence]]. Let $p,q$ be probability vectors on a finite set $S$, and let $P(A)=\\sum_{i\\in A}p_i$, $Q(A)=\\sum_{i\\in A}q_i$ on $\\mathcal P(S)$. Then the measurable-space divergence $D(P\\|Q)$ equals the finite KL sum $\\sum_{i:p_i>0}p_i\\ln(p_i/q_i)$, with value $+\\infty$ exactly when some $p_i>0=q_i$.",
