          "claim": "First suppose $P\\ll Q$ and $D(P\\|Q)<\\infty$. For bounded measurable $f$, let $Z_f=\\int e^f\\,dQ$ and define $Q_f$ by $dQ_f=e^f Z_f^{-1}dQ$. Then $Q_f$ is a probability equivalent to $Q$, and $dP/dQ_f=(dP/dQ)Z_fe^{-f}$. Taking logarithms and integrating under $P$ gives $D(P\\|Q_f)=D(P\\|Q)-\\Phi_{P,Q}(f)$. By [F2], $\\Phi_{P,Q}(f)\\le D(P\\|Q)$. If $D(P\\|Q)=+\\infty$ or $P\\not\\ll Q$, this upper bound is automatic.",
