          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume AC. Every standard-Borel space $(E,\\mathcal S)$ has a countable algebra $\\mathcal A$ which generates $\\mathcal S$, separates points, and determines finite measures: if finite measures $\\mu,\\nu$ agree on $\\mathcal A$, then $\\mu=\\nu$. In particular it determines probability measures.",
