          "quote": "Let $(Z,\\mathcal Z)$ and $(E,\\mathcal E)$ be standard-Borel spaces, let $\\mu$ be a probability measure on $Z$, and let $K,L:Z\\rightsquigarrow E$ be supplied probability kernels. Define their **conditional KL divergence with base $\\mu$** by\n$$D_\\mu(K\\|L):=\\int_Z D(K(z,\\cdot)\\|L(z,\\cdot))\\,\\mu(dz)\\in[0,+\\infty].$$\nThe integrand is measurable by [[thm-conditional-kl-is-measurable]], so this is a well-defined nonnegative extended integral. No absolute-continuity assumption is imposed on individual fibers; a singular fiber has divergence $+\\infty$. Changing supplied kernel versions on a $\\mu$-null set does not change the integral.",
