          "fact": "F4",
          "source": "def-polish-space",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "A topological space is **Polish** when it is separable ([[def-separable-space]]) and completely metrizable: its topology is induced by some complete metric ([[lem-complete-remetrisation]]). No particular compatible complete metric or countable dense subset is part of the structure.",
