          "source": "lem-it-n-type-approximation",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $\\mathcal A$ be a finite nonempty alphabet of size $k$, and let $q$ be any probability vector on $\\mathcal A$. For every $n\\ge1$, there is an $n$-type $q_n\\in\\mathcal P_n(\\mathcal A)$ such that\n$$\\|q_n-q\\|_1:=\\sum_{a\\in\\mathcal A}|q_n(a)-q(a)|\\le\\frac{k}{n}.$$",
