    "lem-finite-alphabet-iid-information-aep": {
      "citations": [
        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "def-finite-alphabet-iid-source",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Let $A$ be a nonempty finite alphabet identified with $[m]$, and let $p$ be\na probability vector in the sense of\n[[def-qa-35-finite-probability-entropy-and-stochastic-matrices]].\nA finite-alphabet IID source consists of random elements\n$X_i:(\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)\\to A$, $i\\ge1$, on one probability space,\nwhich are independent and identically distributed in the sense of\n[[def-identically-distributed-and-iid-random-variables]] and have common law\n$p$. For every $n\\ge1$, the finite vector $X^n=(X_1,\\ldots,X_n)$ then has\nprobability $\\mathbb P(X^n=x^n)=p^n(x^n)$ for each $x^n\\in A^n$, with $p^n$\nas in [[def-finite-law-self-information-and-entropy]].",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "3.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "def-finite-law-self-information-and-entropy",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Let $A$ be a nonempty finite alphabet identified with $[m]$, and let $p$ be a\nprobability vector as in\n[[def-qa-35-finite-probability-entropy-and-stochastic-matrices]]. Its support\nis $A_+:=\\{a\\in A:p(a)>0\\}$. On $A_+$ define self-information\n$\\imath_p(a):=-\\ln p(a)$; set $\\imath_p(a)=0$ when $p(a)=0$ only to make a\nfinite-valued function on all of $A$. Using the finite entropy $H(p)$ from\n[[def-qa-35-finite-probability-entropy-and-stochastic-matrices]] and the\nnatural-logarithm/nats convention from\n[[def-it-information-units-and-logarithm-base]], define the surprisal variance\n$$V(p):=\\sum_{a\\in A_+}p(a)(\\imath_p(a)-H(p))^2.$$\nFor $n\\ge1$ and $x^n=(x_1,\\ldots,x_n)\\in A^n$, define the product law\n$p^n(x^n):=\\prod_{i=1}^np(x_i)$. On its support $A_+^n$, define block\nself-information $\\imath_{p^n}(x^n):=-\\ln p^n(x^n)$. Logarithms use the\nnatural base, matching the entropy convention in\n[[def-qa-35-finite-probability-entropy-and-stochastic-matrices]].",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "def-it-information-units-and-logarithm-base",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Write $\\ln$ for the natural logarithm $\\log$ of [[def-natural-logarithm]]. Unless a base is displayed, every information quantity on this page uses $\\ln$ and is measured in **nats**. For a base $b>1$ and $t>0$, define\n$$\\log_b t:=\\frac{\\ln t}{\\ln b}.$$\nThe denominator is positive: $b>1$, $\\ln$ is strictly increasing, and $\\ln 1=0$ by [[thm-natural-logarithm-laws]]. A base-$b$ entropy or divergence is obtained by replacing each $\\ln$ in the finite formulas below by $\\log_b$; use $0\\log_b0:=0$ and assign $+\\infty$ to a positive numerator over a zero denominator. The case $b=2$ measures **bits**; $b=e$ gives nats.",
          "uses": [
