      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Every dictionary entry is an ordinary word over $\\mathcal A$. While unread text remains it ends in $\\#$, which no dictionary word contains; the root is a prefix and the finite dictionary therefore has a longest matching prefix with a following symbol. Each iteration removes at least one symbol, so from the finite input followed by $\\#$ the parser terminates after at most $n+1$ records, at a final marker record. If an ordinary phrase $wc$ were already in the dictionary, it would be a longer dictionary prefix than the selected $w$, contradicting the longest-prefix rule. Thus ordinary inserted phrases are distinct; the terminal phrase contains $\\#$ and is distinct from them.",
