          "id": "step-1-2",
          "claim": "For a parent index $i\\ge0$, put $m=i+1$, $b=\\lfloor\\log_2m\\rfloor+1$ and $d=\\lfloor\\log_2b\\rfloor+1$. The Elias-gamma code of $b$ consists of $d-1$ zeros followed by the $d$-bit binary expansion of $b$. Its first $1$ reveals $d$, after which exactly $d-1$ more bits complete $b$. Append the final $b-1$ bits of the binary expansion of $m$ to form its Elias-delta code; the decoder restores the leading $1$ of $m$ and then returns $i=m-1$. Thus the gamma header determines exactly how many suffix bits to read. No codeword can be a proper prefix of another, because identical headers determine the same suffix length. For $m=1,2,4$ the codes are respectively $1$, $0100$, and $01100$, so the case $b=1$ has an empty suffix but still a nonempty header. Appending a fixed-width $\\lceil\\log_2(q+1)\\rceil$-bit symbol field gives an unambiguously delimited nonempty record.",
