          "quote": "Assume AC. Let $X,Y$ be random elements with standard-Borel value spaces $(\\mathsf X,\\mathcal X)$ and $(\\mathsf Y,\\mathcal Y)$, and let $P_{XY}$, $P_X$, and $P_Y$ be their joint and marginal probability laws. The product law $P_X\\otimes P_Y$ exists by [[thm-sigma-finite-product-measure-exists-is-rectangular-and-is-unique]]. Define the mutual information in nats by\n\n$$I_{\\mathrm{nat}}(X;Y):=D(P_{XY}\\|P_X\\otimes P_Y)\\in[0,+\\infty],$$\n\nwhere $D$ is the directional Kullback–Leibler divergence of [[def-kullback-leibler-divergence]]. This definition remains meaningful when one or both laws have no Lebesgue density and does not subtract differential entropies that may be infinite.",
