          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Given an input law $P_X$, let $Q_{P_X}=P_XW$ be its output law. The **information density** is\n$$\\imath_{P_X}(x;y):=\\ln\\frac{W(y\\mid x)}{Q_{P_X}(y)}$$\nwhen $P_X(x)W(y\\mid x)>0$, and is $-\\infty$ otherwise. For block sequences define $\\imath_{P_X}(x^n;y^n):=\\sum_{i=1}^n\\imath_{P_X}(x_i;y_i)$, with any sum containing $-\\infty$ equal to $-\\infty$. On the support of the induced joint law, both numerator and denominator are positive, and the value is finite.",
