          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "A **finite discrete memoryless channel (DMC)** is the channel sequence [[def-channel-sequence]] with fixed finite nonempty input and output alphabets $\\mathcal X,\\mathcal Y$ (with every subset measurable) and one stochastic kernel $W(y\\mid x)$ from $\\mathcal X$ to $\\mathcal Y$ ([[def-finite-stochastic-kernel]]). At every blocklength its input and output alphabets are $\\mathcal X^n,\\mathcal Y^n$, and its block kernel is\n$$W^n(y^n\\mid x^n):=\\prod_{i=1}^n W(y_i\\mid x_i).$$\nThus the same single-use transition law is applied independently at each coordinate, conditional on the input word. This page imposes no feedback or input-cost constraint.",
