        },
        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "lem-parallel-awgn-information-density-convergence",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume AC. In orthogonal coordinates let the independent channel branches be $Y_j=X_j+Z_j$, where $X_j\\sim N(0,p_j)$, $Z_j\\sim N(0,\\lambda_j)$, all coordinates are independent, $p_j\\ge0$, and $\\lambda_j>0$. Across channel uses take independent copies. Define the information density on the joint support by\n$$\\imath(X;Y)=\\ln\\frac{f_{Y|X}(Y|X)}{f_Y(Y)}.$$\nThen\n$$\\frac1n\\sum_{t=1}^n\\imath(X_t;Y_t)\\longrightarrow\\frac12\\sum_{j=1}^d\\ln\\left(1+\\frac{p_j}{\\lambda_j}\\right)$$\nin probability.",
