    "lem-cost-constrained-dmc-achievability": {
      "risk": "medium",
      "kind": "lemma",
      "citations": [
        {
          "fact": "A1",
          "source": "def-discrete-memoryless-channel",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "A **finite discrete memoryless channel (DMC)** is the channel sequence [[def-channel-sequence]] with fixed finite nonempty input and output alphabets $\\mathcal X,\\mathcal Y$ (with every subset measurable) and one stochastic kernel $W(y\\mid x)$ from $\\mathcal X$ to $\\mathcal Y$ ([[def-finite-stochastic-kernel]]). At every blocklength its input and output alphabets are $\\mathcal X^n,\\mathcal Y^n$, and its block kernel is\n$$W^n(y^n\\mid x^n):=\\prod_{i=1}^n W(y_i\\mid x_i).$$\nThus the same single-use transition law is applied independently at each coordinate, conditional on the input word. This page imposes no feedback or input-cost constraint.",
          "uses": [
            "3.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "A1",
          "source": "def-finite-dmc-cost-model",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Let $W(y\\mid x)$ be a finite DMC with nonempty finite input alphabet $\\mathcal X$ ([[def-discrete-memoryless-channel]]). A **letter cost** is a supplied function $c:\\mathcal X\\to[0,\\infty)$ with finite real values. Define\n$$c_{\\min}:=\\min_{x\\in\\mathcal X}c(x),\\qquad c_{\\max}:=\\max_{x\\in\\mathcal X}c(x),\\qquad \\bar c(P_X):=\\sum_{x\\in\\mathcal X}P_X(x)c(x)$$\nfor each input probability vector $P_X$ ([[def-finite-probability-vector]]). A real number $\\Gamma$ is a **feasible cost budget** when $\\Gamma\\ge c_{\\min}$. Costs and budgets are per channel use; all logarithms and rates in this pair use natural units [[def-natural-logarithm]].",
          "uses": [
            "3.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "A1",
          "source": "def-cost-constrained-dmc-code-and-capacity",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Fix a finite DMC and cost model from [[def-finite-dmc-cost-model]], with feasible budget $\\Gamma$. A length-$n$, $M$-message code from [[def-fixed-length-channel-code]] is **average-cost feasible** if\n$$\\frac1{nM}\\sum_{m=1}^M\\sum_{t=1}^n c(x_t(m))\\le\\Gamma.$$\nA rate $R\\ge0$ is **average-error achievable under budget $\\Gamma$** if there is a sequence of such codes, for all sufficiently large $n$, whose average errors from [[def-fixed-length-channel-code-errors]] tend to zero and satisfy $\\liminf_{n\\to\\infty}n^{-1}\\ln M_n\\ge R$. The **operational cost-constrained capacity** $C(\\Gamma)$ is the supremum of these rates.\n\nFor an input probability vector $P_X$, define its expected cost $\\bar c(P_X)$ as in [[def-finite-dmc-cost-model]]. The **cost-constrained information capacity** is\n$$C_I(\\Gamma):=\\sup_{P_X:\\,\\bar c(P_X)\\le\\Gamma} I(P_X;W),$$\nwhere $I(P_X;W)$ and the unconstrained DMC information capacity use natural-log nats as in [[def-discrete-memoryless-channel-information-capacity]] and [[def-natural-logarithm]]. All rates use natural-log nats ([[def-natural-logarithm]]). This definition uses a supremum; attainment is proved separately.",
          "uses": [
            "3.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "A1",
          "source": "def-fixed-length-channel-code",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "For a finite DMC $W$, a **length-$n$ code with $M$ messages** is a pair of maps $e:[M]\\to\\mathcal X^n$ and $d:\\mathcal Y^n\\to[M]$, where $n,M\\ge1$ and $[M]:=\\{1,\\ldots,M\\}$. A message $m$ is encoded as $e(m)$, passed through the block kernel $W^n$ of [[def-discrete-memoryless-channel]], and decoded as $d(Y^n)$. The encoder and decoder are deterministic; there is no feedback, and no input-cost constraint is imposed.",
          "uses": [
            "3.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "A1",
          "source": "def-fixed-length-channel-code-errors",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "For a length-$n$ code $(e,d)$, let\n$$e_m:=W^n\\{y^n:d(y^n)\\ne m\\mid e(m)\\}.$$\nIts **average error** is $\\varepsilon_{\\rm av}:=M^{-1}\\sum_{m=1}^M e_m$, corresponding to a uniform message, and its **maximal error** is $\\varepsilon_{\\max}:=\\max_{1\\le m\\le M}e_m$.",
          "uses": [
            "3.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "lem-cost-constrained-dmc-information-capacity-properties",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $W$ be a finite DMC, $c:\\mathcal X\\to[0,\\infty)$ a finite letter cost, and $\\Gamma\\ge c_{\\min}$. The feasible set $\\{P_X:\\bar c(P_X)\\le\\Gamma\\}$ is nonempty and compact, and $C_I(\\Gamma)$ from [[def-cost-constrained-dmc-code-and-capacity]] is attained with $0\\le C_I(\\Gamma)\\le\\ln|\\mathcal X|$. The function $\\Gamma\\mapsto C_I(\\Gamma)$ is nondecreasing and concave on $[c_{\\min},\\infty)$. If $\\Gamma>c_{\\min}$, then for every maximizing law $P_X^*$ the laws\n$$P_{X,\\epsilon}:=(1-\\epsilon)P_X^*+\\epsilon\\delta_{x_{\\min}},\\qquad 0<\\epsilon<1,$$\nhave cost strictly below $\\Gamma$ whenever $P_X^*$ has cost $\\Gamma$, and $I(P_{X,\\epsilon};W)\\to C_I(\\Gamma)$ as $\\epsilon\\downarrow0$.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "lem-discrete-memoryless-channel-iid-information-density-converges",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Fix a finite DMC $W$ and input law $P_X$. If $(X_i,Y_i)_{i\\ge1}$ are IID with law $P_X(x)W(y\\mid x)$, then $n^{-1}\\imath_{P_X}(X^n;Y^n)\\to I(P_X;W)$ in probability.",
          "uses": [
            "2.1"
