          "quote": "Let $W(y\\mid x)$ be a finite DMC with nonempty finite input alphabet $\\mathcal X$ ([[def-discrete-memoryless-channel]]). A **letter cost** is a supplied function $c:\\mathcal X\\to[0,\\infty)$ with finite real values. Define\n$$c_{\\min}:=\\min_{x\\in\\mathcal X}c(x),\\qquad c_{\\max}:=\\max_{x\\in\\mathcal X}c(x),\\qquad \\bar c(P_X):=\\sum_{x\\in\\mathcal X}P_X(x)c(x)$$\nfor each input probability vector $P_X$ ([[def-finite-probability-vector]]). A real number $\\Gamma$ is a **feasible cost budget** when $\\Gamma\\ge c_{\\min}$. Costs and budgets are per channel use; all logarithms and rates in this pair use natural units [[def-natural-logarithm]].",
