          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "def-it-one-letter-gallager-exponent-functions",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Let $W$ be a finite DMC from finite nonempty $\\mathcal X$ to $\\mathcal Y$, with rates and logarithms in nats. For an input law $P$ and $\\rho\\ge0$, define\n$$E_0(\\rho,P):=-\\ln\\sum_{y\\in\\mathcal Y}\\left(\\sum_{x\\in\\mathcal X}P(x)W(y\\mid x)^{1/(1+\\rho)}\\right)^{1+\\rho}.$$\nSeparately, for $\\rho\\ge1$, define $B(x,x'):=\\sum_y\\sqrt{W(y\\mid x)W(y\\mid x')}$ and\n$$E_{0x}(\\rho,P):=-\\rho\\ln\\sum_{x,x'}P(x)P(x')B(x,x')^{1/\\rho}.$$\nFor every $a>0$, $0^a=0$; thus zero channel transitions and zero Bhattacharyya coefficients contribute zero to these sums. These are one-letter functions at a fixed $P$; the global maxima and rate-dependent exponent functions are separate definitions.",
          "uses": [
