          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Let $\\mathcal X,\\widehat{\\mathcal X}$ be nonempty finite alphabets, let $p$ be a pmf on $\\mathcal X$, and let $d:\\mathcal X\\times\\widehat{\\mathcal X}\\to[0,\\infty)$ be finite-valued. A test channel is a stochastic matrix $W(\\hat x\\mid x)$, and its expected single-letter distortion is $\\sum_{x,\\hat x}p(x)W(\\hat x\\mid x)d(x,\\hat x)$, with block distortion as in [[def-it-single-letter-distortion-and-block-distortion]]. Put $D_{\\min}=\\sum_xp(x)\\min_{\\hat x}d(x,\\hat x)$. Define, in bits,\n$$\nR_{p,d}(D):=\\begin{cases}\\displaystyle\\min_{W:\\,\\mathbb E d(X,\\hat X)\\le D} \\frac{I(X;\\hat X)}{\\ln2},&D\\ge D_{\\min},\\\\[4pt]+\\infty,&D<D_{\\min}. \\end{cases}\n$$\nThe minimum exists by [[lem-it-finite-rate-distortion-minimum-attained]]. Values are not operational code rates; the finite memoryless coding theorem is a separate claim.",
