    "thm-it-point-to-point-lossless-source-channel-separation": {
      "citations": [
        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "def-it-point-to-point-joint-source-channel-code",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Let $\\mathcal S,\\mathcal X,\\mathcal Y,\\widehat{\\mathcal S}$ be nonempty finite alphabets, let $P_S$ be a probability vector on $\\mathcal S$, and let $W$ be a finite discrete memoryless channel from $\\mathcal X$ to $\\mathcal Y$ as in [[def-discrete-memoryless-channel]]. For positive integers $k,n$, a deterministic **$(k,n)$ joint source-channel code** is a pair of maps\n$$f_k:\\mathcal S^k\\to\\mathcal X^n,\\qquad g_k:\\mathcal Y^n\\to\\widehat{\\mathcal S}^{\\,k}.$$\nThe source block has law $P_S^{\\otimes k}$, the channel output conditional on input $x^n$ has law $W^n(\\cdot\\mid x^n)$, and the reproduction is $\\widehat S^k=g_k(Y^n)$. The code has no feedback.\n\nA **code sequence at channel-use ratio $\\rho$** consists of such codes with source lengths $k\\to\\infty$, channel lengths $n_k$, and $n_k/k\\to\\rho\\in(0,\\infty)$. In the lossless case $\\widehat{\\mathcal S}=\\mathcal S$, its block error is $\\Pr[\\widehat S^k\\ne S^k]$. In the lossy case, for finite nonnegative single-letter distortion $d$, its normalized block distortion is $d_k$ from [[def-it-single-letter-distortion-and-block-distortion]]; expected distortion and the positive-slack excess-distortion probabilities $\\Pr[d_k>D+\\varepsilon]$ for every $\\varepsilon>0$ are distinct criteria.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "2.1",
            "3.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "def-discrete-memoryless-channel-information-capacity",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "For an input probability vector $P_X$ on $\\mathcal X$ ([[def-finite-probability-vector]]), let $P_{XY}(x,y):=P_X(x)W(y\\mid x)$ and $Q_{P_X}(y):=\\sum_xP_X(x)W(y\\mid x)$. Write $I(P_X;W):=I(X;Y)$ for this joint law, using [[def-it-finite-mutual-information]]. The **single-letter information capacity** is\n$$C(W):=\\sup_{P_X} I(P_X;W),$$\nmeasured in nats per channel use. The finite-dimensional maximum is attained, as proved in [[lem-discrete-memoryless-channel-capacity-is-attained]].",
          "uses": [
            "1.3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "def-discrete-memoryless-channel-operational-capacity",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "A rate $R\\ge0$ is **average-error achievable** for $W$ if there are length-$n$ codes for all sufficiently large $n$ with\n$$\\liminf_{n\\to\\infty}\\frac{\\ln M_n}{n}\\ge R,\\qquad \\varepsilon_{\\rm av}(n)\\longrightarrow0.$$\nIt is **maximal-error achievable** if the same condition holds with $\\varepsilon_{\\max}(n)\\to0$. Define $C_{\\rm av}(W)$ and $C_{\\max}(W)$ as the suprema of the respective achievable-rate sets. Rates use nats per channel use.",
          "uses": [
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "thm-discrete-memoryless-channel-capacity-formula",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For every finite DMC $W$ with no input-cost constraint,\n$$C_{\\rm av}(W)=C_{\\max}(W)=C(W)=\\max_{P_X}I(P_X;W),$$\nwith rates and mutual information measured in nats per channel use.",
          "uses": [
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F4",
          "source": "lem-it-finite-iid-source-lossless-code-achievability",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $P_S$ be a probability vector on a finite nonempty alphabet $\\mathcal S$, and define its entropy in nats by\n\n$$H(P_S):=-\\sum_{s:P_S(s)>0}P_S(s)\\ln P_S(s).$$\n\nFor every $R>H(P_S)$, there are deterministic fixed-length codes $f_k:\\mathcal S^k\\to[M_k]$, $g_k:[M_k]\\to\\mathcal S^k$ for the IID source $P_S^{\\otimes k}$ such that $\\Pr[g_k(f_k(S^k))\\ne S^k]\\to0$ and $\\limsup_{k\\to\\infty}k^{-1}\\ln M_k<R$.",
          "uses": [
            "1.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F5",
          "source": "lem-discrete-memoryless-channel-n-letter-information-bound",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For every input probability vector on $\\mathcal X^n$ and output $Y^n$ generated by a finite DMC $W^n$, one has $I(X^n;Y^n)\\le nC(W)$.",
          "uses": [
            "1.3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F6",
          "source": "thm-it-fano-inequality",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $X$ take values in an alphabet $\\mathcal X$ of size $m\\ge2$, let $Y$ be finite, and let $\\widehat X$ be an estimator in the same alphabet generated from $Y$, so the joint pmf factors as $p_{XY\\widehat X}=p_{XY}p_{\\widehat X|Y}$. Put $P_e=\\mathbb P[\\widehat X\\ne X]$ and define\n\n$$h_2(t):=-t\\ln t-(1-t)\\ln(1-t),\\qquad 0\\ln0:=0.$$\n\nThen\n\n$$H(X|Y)\\le h_2(P_e)+P_e\\ln(m-1)\\le \\ln2+P_e\\ln m.$$\n\nFor $m=1$, $X$ is constant and $H(X|Y)=0$.",
