          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Remove all zero-probability values of $U$. For each remaining $u$, set $\\pi_u=P_U(u)>0$, $q_u(x)=P(X=x|U=u)$, $a_u=\\mathbb E[d(X,g(Y,u))|U=u]$, and $h_u=H(X|Y,U=u)$. Because $U-X-Y$, the conditional law of $Y$ given $(X,U)$ is $P_{Y|X}$, so $a_u$ is determined by $q_u$ and the fixed decoder map $g(\\cdot,u)$. Also, $P_X(x)=\\sum_u\\pi_uq_u(x),\\quad \\mathbb E d(X,g(Y,U))=\\sum_u\\pi_ua_u,\\quad H(X|Y,U)=\\sum_u\\pi_uh_u.$ These are finite sums.",
