        {
          "id": "step-2-1",
          "claim": "Define $U'$ to have the remaining positive weights $\\pi'_u$, conditional posterior $P(X=x|U'=u)=q_u(x)$, and conditional side-information law $P_{Y|X}$. Equivalently set $P_{XYU'}(x,y,u)=P_{XY}(x,y)P(U'=u|X=x)$ with $P(U'=u|X=x):=\\pi'_uq_u(x)/P_X(x)$ for $P_X(x)>0$, and choose any row on zero-mass $x$. The source marginal is preserved by step 1.2, and $\\sum_u\\pi'_uq_u(x)=P_X(x)$ makes each conditional row sum to one. Use the same reconstruction map $g(y,u)$. The distortion is unchanged by step 1.2, and [F2] gives $I(X;U'|Y)=H(X|Y)-\\sum_u\\pi'_uh_u\\le H(X|Y)-\\sum_u\\pi_uh_u=I(X;U|Y).$ At least one positive auxiliary value was removed. Repeating finitely many times leaves at most $m+1$ values and never increases the objective.",
