          "source": "def-it-finite-iid-multisource",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Fix an integer $k\\ge2$ and finite nonempty alphabets $\\mathcal X_1,\\ldots,\\mathcal X_k$. Let $\\mathcal X:=\\prod_{i=1}^k\\mathcal X_i$, identified with a finite alphabet as in [[def-finite-alphabet-iid-source]]. A **finite-alphabet IID $k$-source** is an IID sequence of vectors\n$$Z_t=(X_{1,t},\\ldots,X_{k,t})\\in\\mathcal X,\\qquad t\\ge1,$$\nwith common joint probability vector $P$ on $\\mathcal X$. Thus for every $n\\ge1$ its block law is $P^{\\otimes n}$, and terminal $i$ observes $X_i^n=(X_{i,1},\\ldots,X_{i,n})$. For $S\\subseteq[k]:=\\{1,\\ldots,k\\}$ write $X_S=(X_i)_{i\\in S}$, let $S^c=[k]\\setminus S$, and define $H_P(X_S\\mid X_{S^c})$ by [[def-it-finite-conditional-entropy]] for the induced finite joint law. When $S=[k]$, $X_{S^c}$ takes values in the singleton empty product, so $H_P(X_S\\mid X_{S^c})=H(P)$ under [[def-qa-35-finite-probability-entropy-and-stochastic-matrices]]. Unmarked logarithms and information rates use nats by [[def-it-information-units-and-logarithm-base]].",
