          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $P_{XY}$ be a finite joint law, let $d:\\mathcal X\\times\\widehat{\\mathcal X}\\to[0,d_{\\max}]$, and let $(U,P_{U|X},g)$ be any finite Wyner-Ziv test channel from [[def-it-finite-wyner-ziv-code]] with expected distortion at most $D$. There is another finite test channel $(U',P_{U'|X},g')$ such that\n$$|\\mathcal U'|\\le|\\mathcal X|+1,\\qquad \\mathbb E[d(X,g'(Y,U'))]=\\mathbb E[d(X,g(Y,U))],\\qquad I(X;U'|Y)\\le I(X;U|Y).$$\nConsequently the infimum $R_{\\rm WZ}(D)$ in [[def-it-finite-wyner-ziv-code]] is a minimum and it suffices to optimize over $|\\mathcal U|\\le|\\mathcal X|+1$.",
