          "fact": "F8",
          "source": "lem-it-finite-codebook-covering-selection-law",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $P_{XU}=P_XP_{U|X}$ be a joint law on finite nonempty alphabets, with marginal $P_U$. Fix $\\eta>0$ and a target joint-typicality tolerance $\\epsilon>0$. There are a source-typicality tolerance $\\delta>0$ and an integer $n_0$ such that, for every $n\\ge n_0$, every $x^n\\in T_\\delta^{(n)}(P_X)$, and every $R>I(X;U)+\\eta$, an iid codebook of $M_n=\\lceil e^{nR}\\rceil$ independent $P_U^{\\otimes n}$ words contains a word in $T_\\epsilon^{(n)}(P_{XU}|x^n)$ with probability tending to one uniformly in $x^n$. If the encoder selects the least index with a jointly typical word, then, conditional on a match, its selected word has law $P_U^{\\otimes n}$ conditioned on $T_\\epsilon^{(n)}(P_{XU}|x^n)$; conditional on any particular joint type, this law is uniform on the associated conditional type class.",
