          "source": "lem-it-finite-selected-codeword-markov-typicality",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $P_{XYZ}(x,y,z)=P_{XY}(x,y)P_{Z|X}(z|x)$ be a finite-alphabet Markov law. For every $\\epsilon>0$ there are $\\delta>0$ and $n_0$ such that the following holds for $n\\ge n_0$: if $(x^n,y^n)\\in T_\\delta^{(n)}(P_{XY})$ and a random $Z^n$ is supported on $T_\\delta^{(n)}(P_{Z|X}\\mid x^n)$ and, conditional on each joint type of $(x^n,Z^n)$, is uniform on that conditional type class, then\n$$\\Pr\\{(x^n,y^n,Z^n)\\in T_\\epsilon^{(n)}(P_{XYZ})\\}\\ge1-\\frac{C}{n},$$\nwhere $C<\\infty$ depends only on the fixed finite law, alphabets, and $\\epsilon$, not on the particular typical source block or conditional type.",
