          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Fix $k\\ge1$, finite alphabets $\\mathcal U_1,\\ldots,\\mathcal U_k,\\mathcal S$, and a joint law $P_{U_1\\cdots U_kS}$. Let the source-selection data $Z^n$ and decoder side-information block $S^n$ have any joint law. Independently of $(Z^n,S^n)$, generate mutually independent codebooks whose $M_i$ codewords each have law $P_{U_i}^{\\otimes n}$. Generate independent uniform bin labels from $[B_i]$ for every codeword, independently of the source and codebooks. Let the selected true indices $L_i$ be functions of $Z^n$ and codebooks but not the bin labels. In addition, for every nonempty proper $J\\subset[k]$, require the complementary selected codewords at indices in $J^c$ to be determined by $Z^n$ and codebooks indexed by $J^c$ alone; this condition is automatic when each terminal selects using its own codebook, and is vacuous for $k=1$. For a fixed positive typicality tolerance, a joint-typicality decoder looks for the unique tuple in the received bins whose codewords and $S^n$ are jointly typical for $P_{U_1\\cdots U_kS}$. Suppose there is a common $\\eta>0$ such that for every nonempty $J\\subseteq[k],$\n$$\\sum_{i\\in J}\\frac1n\\ln\\frac{M_i}{B_i}<\\sum_{i\\in J}H(U_i)-H(U_J\\mid U_{J^c},S)-\\eta.$$\nThen there is $\\epsilon_0>0$ such that, for every fixed typicality tolerance $0<\\epsilon\\le\\epsilon_0$, writing $E_n$ for the event that the selected true tuple and $S^n$ are jointly typical, the expected number of wrong jointly typical tuples in its received bins, multiplied by $\\mathbf1_{E_n}$, tends to zero as $n\\to\\infty$. Consequently the probability that $E_n$ holds and a wrong jointly typical tuple exists tends to zero. The case of no side information is represented by a singleton $\\mathcal S$.",
