          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "A two-user finite discrete memoryless multiple-access channel (DM-MAC) consists of finite nonempty input alphabets $\\mathcal X_1,\\mathcal X_2$, a finite nonempty output alphabet $\\mathcal Y$, and a stochastic kernel $W(y\\mid x_1,x_2)$ from $\\mathcal X_1\\times\\mathcal X_2$ to $\\mathcal Y$ in the convention of [[def-finite-stochastic-kernel]]. Its length-$n$ conditional law is $W^n(y^n\\mid x_1^n,x_2^n)=\\prod_{i=1}^nW(y_i\\mid x_{1i},x_{2i})$.",
