          "source": "lem-it-awgn-feedback-estimation-covariance-update",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $(X_1,X_2)$ be centered jointly Gaussian with variances $P_1,P_2>0$, correlation $\\rho\\in[0,1)$, and let $Z\\sim N(0,N)$ be independent, $N>0$. Put $X=(X_1,X_2)^T$, $a=(1,1)^T$, $K=\\begin{pmatrix}P_1&\\rho\\sqrt{P_1P_2}\\\\\\rho\\sqrt{P_1P_2}&P_2\\end{pmatrix}$, $Y=a^TX+Z$, and $D=N+a^TKa$. The residual $X-\\mathbb E[X\\mid Y]$ is independent of $Y$ and has covariance $K-Kaa^TK/D$. In particular,\n$$\\operatorname{Var}(X_1\\mid Y)=\\frac{P_1[N+P_2(1-\\rho^2)]}{D},\\quad \\operatorname{Var}(X_2\\mid Y)=\\frac{P_2[N+P_1(1-\\rho^2)]}{D},$$\n$$\\operatorname{Cov}(X_1-\\mathbb E[X_1\\mid Y],X_2-\\mathbb E[X_2\\mid Y])=\\frac{\\rho\\sqrt{P_1P_2}N-P_1P_2(1-\\rho^2)}{D}.$$\nAfter scaling the two errors to variances $P_1,P_2$ and reversing the sign of the second, their correlation is\n$$\\rho_{\\rm new}=\\frac{\\sqrt{P_1P_2}(1-\\rho^2)-\\rho N}{\\sqrt{[N+P_1(1-\\rho^2)][N+P_2(1-\\rho^2)]}}.$$",
