          "quote": "For the finite DM-MAC of [[def-it-two-user-discrete-memoryless-mac]], a perfect-feedback length-$n$ code has independent uniform messages $M_j\\in[M_j]$, deterministic encoders $f_{ji}:[M_j]\\times\\mathcal Y^{i-1}\\to\\mathcal X_j$ and a joint decoder from $\\mathcal Y^n$ to the message pair. Both users see the same noiseless past output $Y^{i-1}$ before use $i$; neither sees the other user's message. Rates are $R_j=n^{-1}\\ln M_j$ nats/use and error is average joint message error. Achievability means a sequence with vanishing error and limiting lower rates at least the specified pair; capacity is the closure.",
