          "quote": "Use the channel, independent messages, noise law, average joint error, powers $P_1,P_2$ and nats/use convention of [[def-it-two-user-real-awgn-mac-code]]. A length-$n$ perfect-feedback code has a Borel-measurable joint decoder $g:\\mathbb R^n\\to[M_1]\\times[M_2]$. Its user-$j$ encoder is a deterministic Borel-measurable family $f_{ji}:[M_j]\\times\\mathbb R^{i-1}\\to\\mathbb R$, $1\\le i\\le n$, with $X_{ji}=f_{ji}(M_j,Y^{i-1})$; at $i=1$ the history is the singleton empty tuple. Both senders receive the same noiseless past output, and there is no message sharing or preshared common randomness. The same expected block-power constraint is imposed.",
