          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $X=(X_1,\\ldots,X_d)$ be a real random vector with $\\mathbb E\\|X\\|^2<\\infty$, and let $Z$ be independent of $X$ with density $(2\\pi N)^{-d/2}e^{-\\|z\\|^2/(2N)}$, $N>0$. Then $Y=X+Z$ has a positive density and finite differential entropy. Each coordinate satisfies $h(Y_k)\\le\\frac12\\ln(2\\pi e\\,\\operatorname{Var}Y_k)$, while $h(Y)\\le\\sum_kh(Y_k)$ and $h(Y)\\ge h(Z)=\\frac d2\\ln(2\\pi eN)$. If a side variable $S$ admits a conditional law $P_{X|S=s}$ with finite second moment almost surely and $Z$ is independent of the pair $(X,S)$, then each conditional Gaussian convolution has finite entropy and\n$$h(Y\\mid S)\\le\\sum_{k=1}^d\\frac12\\ln\\!\\left(2\\pi e\\left[N+\\mathbb E\\operatorname{Var}(X_k\\mid S)\\right]\\right).$$",
