          "quote": "Let $M$ be uniform on a finite message set $\\mathcal M$ of size $m\\ge2$, let $S$ take values in a finite set $\\mathcal S$, and let $Y$ take values in $\\mathbb R^d$; a complex observation space $\\mathbb C^k$ is identified with $\\mathbb R^{2k}$. Suppose $Y\\mid(M,S)$ has a Lebesgue density. For every measurable estimator $\\widehat M=\\phi(Y,S)$ with $\\phi:\\mathbb R^d\\times\\mathcal S\\to\\mathcal M$ and error probability $\\epsilon$, define $H(M\\mid Y,S):=\\int H(p_{M|y,s})\\,dP_{Y,S}(y,s)$ using its finite posterior vector. Then\n$$H(M\\mid Y,S)\\le h_b(\\epsilon)+\\epsilon\\ln(m-1)\\le\\ln2+\\epsilon\\ln m,$$\nwhere $h_b(t)=-t\\ln t-(1-t)\\ln(1-t)$ and $0\\ln0=0$. For $m=1$, the conditional entropy is zero.",
