          "source": "def-it-two-correlated-iid-sources-over-dm-mac-code",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Let $(S_{1t},S_{2t})_{t\\ge1}$ be the $k=2$ case of the finite IID multisource in [[def-it-finite-iid-multisource]], with finite nonempty component alphabets and common joint law $P_{S_1S_2}$. A length-$n$ lossless source-channel code over a DM-MAC as in [[def-it-two-user-discrete-memoryless-mac]] has separate deterministic encoders $f_j:\\mathcal S_j^n\\to\\mathcal X_j^n$ and one decoder $g:\\mathcal Y^n\\to\\mathcal S_1^n\\times\\mathcal S_2^n$. Its error is $\\Pr[g(Y^n)\\ne(S_1^n,S_2^n)]$. Reliable transmission means a sequence of such codes with error tending to zero. All source entropies are in nats and use [[def-it-finite-conditional-entropy]].",
