          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "def-it-finite-dmc-feedback-code",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "For a finite DMC $W:\\mathcal X\\to\\mathcal Y$ as in [[def-discrete-memoryless-channel]], a length-$n$ feedback code has a uniform message $M\\in[M]$, deterministic causal encoders $f_i:[M]\\times\\mathcal Y^{i-1}\\to\\mathcal X$ and a decoder $g:\\mathcal Y^n\\to[M]$. The encoder at time $i$ sees only $Y^{i-1}$, sets $X_i=f_i(M,Y^{i-1})$, and the causal joint law is\n$$\\Pr(M=m,Y^n=y^n)=\\frac1M\\prod_{i=1}^n W(y_i\\mid f_i(m,y^{i-1})).$$\nEquivalently, at each positive-probability message-and-past-output history, $Y_i$ has conditional law $W(\\cdot\\mid f_i(m,y^{i-1}))$. Its average error is $\\Pr[g(Y^n)\\ne M]$, rate is $n^{-1}\\ln M$ nats/use, and the feedback capacity is the closure of rates achievable with error tending to zero. There is no input-cost constraint.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "1.2",
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "def-discrete-memoryless-channel-information-capacity",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "For an input probability vector $P_X$ on $\\mathcal X$ ([[def-finite-probability-vector]]), let $P_{XY}(x,y):=P_X(x)W(y\\mid x)$ and $Q_{P_X}(y):=\\sum_xP_X(x)W(y\\mid x)$. Write $I(P_X;W):=I(X;Y)$ for this joint law, using [[def-it-finite-mutual-information]]. The **single-letter information capacity** is\n$$C(W):=\\sup_{P_X} I(P_X;W),$$\nmeasured in nats per channel use. The finite-dimensional maximum is attained, as proved in [[lem-discrete-memoryless-channel-capacity-is-attained]].",
          "uses": [
            "2.1",
            "3.1"
          ]
        },
        {
