          "source": "thm-it-fano-inequality",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $X$ take values in an alphabet $\\mathcal X$ of size $m\\ge2$, let $Y$ be finite, and let $\\widehat X$ be an estimator in the same alphabet generated from $Y$, so the joint pmf factors as $p_{XY\\widehat X}=p_{XY}p_{\\widehat X|Y}$. Put $P_e=\\mathbb P[\\widehat X\\ne X]$ and define\n\n$$h_2(t):=-t\\ln t-(1-t)\\ln(1-t),\\qquad 0\\ln0:=0.$$\n\nThen\n\n$$H(X|Y)\\le h_2(P_e)+P_e\\ln(m-1)\\le \\ln2+P_e\\ln m.$$\n\nFor $m=1$, $X$ is constant and $H(X|Y)=0$.",
