          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Let $p_{XY}$ be a joint probability vector on finite alphabets $\\mathcal X\\times\\mathcal Y$. It is the weight function of the canonical finite probability space from [[def-finite-probability-space-and-event]]; its coordinate maps are finite random elements in the sense of [[def-random-element-and-real-random-variable]]. Write $p_Y(y)=\\sum_xp_{XY}(x,y)$. For each $y$ with $p_Y(y)>0$, set $p_{X|y}(x)=p_{XY}(x,y)/p_Y(y)$; this is a probability vector by [[lem-it-finite-marginals-and-conditionals-are-pmfs]]. Define the conditional entropy in nats by\n\n$$H(X|Y):=\\sum_{y:p_Y(y)>0}p_Y(y)H(p_{X|y}),$$\n\nwhere $H(p)=-\\sum_xp(x)\\ln p(x)$ is the finite entropy of [[def-qa-35-finite-probability-entropy-and-stochastic-matrices]]. Terms for zero-mass $y$ are omitted. The base-$b$ version replaces $\\ln$ by $\\log_b$.",
