        {
          "id": "step-2-1",
          "claim": "For any finite time-sharing variable, the sum bound is $I(X_1,X_2;Y\\mid Q)=H(Y\\mid Q)\\le\\ln2$, because each conditional output is binary. With $Q$ constant and $p=q=1/2$, both individual informations and the sum information equal $\\ln2$. Hence every nonnegative pair with sum at most $\\ln2$ is in the closed region, and no pair with larger sum is.",
