      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Fix $a\\in\\mathcal A$ with $P(a)>0$, and set $B_i=\\mathbf1_{\\{X_i=a\\}}$. The variables $B_i$ are IID Bernoulli with mean $P(a)$ and variance $P(a)(1-P(a))\\le1/4$. Thus $\\widehat P_{X^n}(a)=n^{-1}\\sum_iB_i$ has mean $P(a)$ and variance at most $1/(4n)$. If $Z=\\widehat P_{X^n}(a)-P(a)$, then pointwise $\\mathbf1_{\\{|Z|>\\delta P(a)\\}}\\le Z^2/(\\delta^2P(a)^2)$. Taking expectations bounds the deviation probability by $1/(4n\\delta^2P(a)^2)$.",
