        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "lem-standard-borel-conditional-mutual-information-chain-rule-and-data-processing",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume AC. Let $U,V,Y,S$ take values in standard-Borel spaces. Then\n$$I((U,V);Y|S)=I(U;Y|S)+I(V;Y|U,S)$$\nand also\n$$I((U,V);Y|S)=I(V;Y|S)+I(U;Y|V,S),$$\nwhere these are equalities of extended nonnegative quantities. In particular, if the conditional law of $Y$ given $(U,V,S)$ depends only on $(V,S)$, then\n$$I(U;Y|S)\\le I(V;Y|S).$$",
          "uses": [
            "6.1"
