          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Initially choose $0<P_i'<P_i$ when $P_i>0$, and set $X_i=0$ when $P_i=0$. On positive-power nodes take independent $X_i\\sim N(0,P_i')$. Use the stated reconstruction kernels. Remove constant coordinates when writing densities. The remaining joint coordinates $(X,Y,\\hat Y_{\\mathcal Q})$ are an invertible linear image of the independent nonconstant inputs, channel noises and quantization noises: recover inputs first, channel noises from $Y-GX$, and quantization noises from $\\hat Y_{\\mathcal Q}-Y_{\\mathcal Q}$. They therefore have a strictly positive nonsingular Gaussian density. Its needed marginal and conditional densities are likewise Gaussian with positive conditional covariance, so all local and reference likelihood ratios in [F2] exist measurably. Every log ratio is a constant plus a quadratic polynomial in Gaussian variables.",
