          "claim": "Increase $P_i'$ to $P_i$ simultaneously at positive-power nodes. Each mutual information in these finitely many cuts is a continuous function of the variances: its Gaussian entropy formula is a log determinant of a positive-definite conditional noise covariance plus a positive-semidefinite signal covariance. One may derive the formula directly from the Gaussian density: for positive-definite $K$, integration of its log density gives $h(N(0,K))=\\tfrac12\\ln((2\\pi e)^m\\det K)$ because the expected quadratic form is $m$. Conditional noise covariance is positive definite even at the limiting input variances. Therefore any tuple satisfying all strict inequalities at $P_i$ satisfies them at $P_i'$ sufficiently close to $P_i$. Use the codes from step 3.1, already satisfying the original power constraints. This proves the full chosen-$\\mathcal Q$ achievability assertion, including arbitrary zero-power nodes.",
