          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Fix $(v^n,x^n)\\in T_{\\delta_{\\rm in}}^{(n)}(P_{VX})$. For this concentration calculation, draw an auxiliary word under $Q_n:=P_{U|X,V}^{\\otimes n}(\\cdot|x^n,v^n)$, rather than under the codebook law $C_n:=P_{U|V}^{\\otimes n}(\\cdot|v^n)$. For each positive-mass triple $(v,x,u)$, its empirical frequency under $Q_n$ has mean $\\widehat P_{v^nx^n}(v,x)P_{U|X,V}(u|x,v)$, which differs from $P(v,x,u)$ by at most $\\delta_{\\rm in}P(v,x,u)$. Its variance is at most $1/(4n)$ because its indicator summands are independent across positions. Chebyshev's inequality with deviation threshold $(\\delta_{\\rm out}-\\delta_{\\rm in})P(v,x,u)$ and a finite union bound show that all positive-mass triple frequencies meet the $\\delta_{\\rm out}$ conditions with probability tending to one uniformly over the fixed input pairs. Zero-mass input pairs are absent and zero conditional-probability outputs are never generated.",
