    "lem-finite-directed-information-feedback-decomposition": {
      "completion_status": "ready",
      "citations": [
        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "def-finite-directed-information-and-causal-conditioning",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "For finite random sequences $X^n=(X_1,\\ldots,X_n)$ and $Y^n=(Y_1,\\ldots,Y_n)$, define the **directed information** from $X^n$ to $Y^n$ by\n$$I(X^n\\to Y^n):=\\sum_{i=1}^n I(X^i;Y_i\\mid Y^{i-1}),$$\nwhere $X^i=(X_1,\\ldots,X_i)$ and $Y^0$ is the empty tuple. For a third finite sequence $Z^n$, define the causally conditioned version\n$$I(X^n\\to Y^n\\Vert Z^n):=\\sum_{i=1}^n I(X^i;Y_i\\mid Y^{i-1},Z^i).$$\nAll conditional mutual information terms use the finite nats convention of [[def-it-finite-conditional-mutual-information]]. The conditioning includes $Z_i$ because it is the current side-information symbol available at the receiving end of the directed-information term; $Y^{i-1}$ and $Z^{i-1}$ are the past.",
