nder a zero budget. Unconstrained nodes and constant coordinates are permitted.\n\nEvery nonnegative rate tuple satisfying\n$$\\sum_{k\\in A\\cap\\mathcal S}r_k<F_d(A)$$\nfor every $d\\in\\mathcal D$ and nonempty $A$ with $d\\notin A$ and $A\\cap\\mathcal S\\ne\\varnothing$ is achievable by deterministic measurable causal codes. Each constrained node can satisfy $\\sum_{t=1}^m c_k(X_{k,t})\\le m\\Gamma_k$ on every realized transmitted input sequence of code length $m$, and hence also its expected average-cost constraint. The closure of the union of these regions over admissible laws is achievable. Constant reconstructions are permitted. The separate all-zero tuple is achievable whenever one can choose fixed inputs obeying any imposed costs, regardless of negative cut expressions.",
