        {
          "fact": "F6",
          "source": "thm-general-kl-chain-rule-for-standard-borel-kernels",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $E,F$ be standard-Borel spaces, let $\\mu,\\nu$ be probability measures on E, and let $K,L:E\\rightsquigarrow F$ be probability kernels. Let $P=\\mu\\ltimes K$ and $Q=\\nu\\ltimes L$ be the joint probability laws defined by\n$$P(C)=\\int_E K(x,C_x)\\,\\mu(dx),\\qquad Q(C)=\\int_E L(x,C_x)\\,\\nu(dx)$$\nfor product-measurable $C\\subseteq E\\times F$. Then\n$$D(P\\|Q)=D(\\mu\\|\\nu)+\\int_E D(K(x,\\cdot)\\|L(x,\\cdot))\\,\\mu(dx)=D(\\mu\\|\\nu)+D_\\mu(K\\|L),$$\nas an equality in $[0,+\\infty]$. In particular, when $\\mu=\\nu$, the joint KL is the conditional KL from [[def-conditional-kl-for-probability-kernels]].",
          "uses": [
            "1.2"
          ]
        }
