          "claim": "By [F2], successively adjoining $Y_i$ to $Y^{i-1}$ gives $$I(X^n;Y^n)=I(Y^n;X^n)=\\sum_{i=1}^n I(Y_i;X^n|Y^{i-1})=\\sum_{i=1}^n I(X^n;Y_i|Y^{i-1}).$$ The first equality and the last equality use the coordinate swap in [F5]; the initial term for the empty tuple $Y^0$ is zero. Every term is an extended nonnegative quantity, so no subtraction of infinities is involved.",
