      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "For any length-$n$ code, independence of the messages makes the induced vectors $X_1^n,X_2^n$ independent. Fano at receiver 1 and the fact that revealing $M_2$ cannot reduce mutual information give $nR_1\\le I(X_1^n;Y_1^n|X_2^n)+o(n)$. The analogous receiver-2 bound is $nR_2\\le I(X_2^n;Y_2^n|X_1^n)+o(n)$.",
