          "quote": "Let $X$ have a finite alphabet $\\mathcal X$ of size $m\\ge1$, let $Y$ be finite, and let $\\widehat X$ be any finite estimate output generated from $Y$, with an output alphabet that may contain symbols outside $\\mathcal X$. Assume $X\\to Y\\to\\widehat X$, and set $P_e=\\mathbb P[\\widehat X\\ne X]$. Use $h_2$ as defined in [[thm-it-fano-inequality]]. Then\n\n$$H(X|Y)\\le h_2(P_e)+P_e\\ln m.$$\n\nIf $X$ is uniform on $\\mathcal X$, then\n\n$$ (1-P_e)\\ln m\\le I(X;Y)+h_2(P_e).$$",
