          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For every finite joint law $P_{UX}$ on a finite wiretap channel with input alphabet $\\mathcal X$, where $U-X-(Y,Z)$ means $P_{UXYZ}(u,x,y,z)=P_{UX}(u,x)W(y,z\\mid x)$, there is another finite auxiliary $\\widetilde U$ with $|\\widetilde{\\mathcal U}|\\le|\\mathcal X|$ whose value of $I(\\widetilde U;Y)-I(\\widetilde U;Z)$ is at least $I(U;Y)-I(U;Z)$. Consequently\n\n$$\\sup_{P_{U,X}:\\,U-X-(Y,Z)}[I(U;Y)-I(U;Z)]$$\n\nis a maximum and may be restricted to $|\\mathcal U|\\le|\\mathcal X|$. For each input law $q$, the single-letter objective $q\\mapsto I_q(X;Y)-I_q(X;Z)$ is continuous on the finite probability simplex.",
