          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "For finite random variables $M,Z$, information leakage is the finite mutual information $I(M;Z)$ in nats, as defined in [[def-it-finite-mutual-information]], and equivocation is the finite conditional entropy $H(M\\mid Z)$, as defined in [[def-it-finite-conditional-entropy]]. For an $n$-use code with Eve's observation $Z^n$, its normalized leakage is $n^{-1}I(M;Z^n)$. When $M$ is uniform on a finite message set $\\mathcal M$, its entropy is $H(M)=\\ln|\\mathcal M|$. Zero-probability symbols are handled by the finite entropy and KL conventions cited above.",
