          "quote": "Let $H$ be a nonzero finite-dimensional complex inner-product space; the pairing is linear in its first argument ([[def-dimension]], [[def-real-and-complex-inner-product-space]]). Write $\\mathcal L(H)$ for its complex-linear endomorphisms ([[def-vector-space-of-linear-maps]]) and let $\\Omega$ be a finite nonempty outcome set. A **finite POVM** on $H$ with outcomes $\\Omega$ is a family $E=(E_a)_{a\\in\\Omega}$ with each $E_a$ nonnegative and $\\sum_{a\\in\\Omega}E_a=I_H$; after any enumeration of $\\Omega$, these operators form the finite complete positive family of [[def-qc-finite-positive-effect-family]]. Reordering does not alter the finite sum. The complete-family lemma [[lem-qc-complete-effect-family-members-are-effects]] shows that every $E_a$ also has nonnegative complement $I_H-E_a$, so each is an effect.\n\nFor a density operator $\\rho$ on $H$ (a nonnegative operator of trace one, [[def-qc-density-operator]]), its **POVM outcome weights** are\n\n$$p_\\rho(a):=\\operatorname{tr}(\\rho E_a),\\qquad a\\in\\Omega.$$\n\nHere $\\operatorname{tr}$ is the finite-dimensional endomorphism trace ([[def-trace-of-an-endomorphism]]).\n\nThe positivity and normalization of these weights are proved in [[thm-qc-povm-probabilities-normalize]]. A POVM specifies this outcome law; it does not by itself prescribe a conditional output state.",
