          "source": "thm-it-quantum-relative-entropy-joint-convexity",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $H$ be a finite-dimensional complex inner-product space, let $n\\ge1$, let $A_i,B_i:H\\to H$ be non-negative for $1\\le i\\le n$, and let $\\lambda_i\\ge0$ with $\\sum_i\\lambda_i=1$. Then, in the extended-real order,\n\n$$D\\!\\left(\\sum_i\\lambda_iA_i\\,\\middle\\|\\,\\sum_i\\lambda_iB_i\\right)\\le\\sum_i\\lambda_iD(A_i\\|B_i),$$\n\nwhere zero-weight terms are omitted from the right side, and the order is that on the extended real line.",
