          "source": "def-qc-tensor-register-and-permutation",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "An **ordered tensor register** consists of a finite ordered list of\nfinite-dimensional complex inner-product spaces $H_0,\\ldots,H_{n-1}$, each\nequipped with a specified ordered orthonormal basis. Its space is\n$H_0\\otimes\\cdots\\otimes H_{n-1}$, with factors retained in the displayed\norder. The product basis is ordered lexicographically by its tuple of factor\nindices. The empty tensor product is $\\mathbb C$ with basis $\\{1\\}$. A\nzero-dimensional factor is allowed in this mathematical construction and makes\nthe tensor space zero; it is not a register under\n[[def-qc-register-and-computational-basis]].\n\nThe inner product is linear in the first argument and conjugate-linear in the\nsecond, and on elementary tensors it is\n\n$$\\left\\langle\\bigotimes_{k<n}x_k,\\bigotimes_{k<n}y_k\\right\\rangle_{\\otimes}:=\\prod_{k<n}\\langle x_k,y_k\\rangle_{{\\rm root},k}.$$ \n\nFor the empty tensor, the right side is the empty product $1$, giving the\nstandard inner product on $\\mathbb C$.\n\nFor a permutation $\\sigma$ of the $n$ factor positions, the **wire permutation**\n$P_\\sigma$ maps the product basis vector indexed by\n$(i_0,\\ldots,i_{n-1})$ to the product basis vector whose output factor order is\n$(\\sigma(0),\\ldots,\\sigma(n-1))$. It is extended linearly; for $n=0$ it is the\nidentity on $\\mathbb C$. The extension is a linear map in the sense of\n[[def-linear-map]].",
