          "excerpt": "Every density operator $\\rho$ on a nonzero finite-dimensional complex-inner-product space $H$ has a purification on some finite-dimensional auxiliary space. More precisely, if $r=\\operatorname{rank}(\\rho)$, it has one on an auxiliary space of dimension $r$. If $\\Psi_i\\in H\\otimes K_i$ ($i=1,2$) are any two purifications of the same $\\rho$, then for every integer $m\\ge\\max(\\dim K_1,\\dim K_2)$ and every pair of linear isometric embeddings $\\iota_i:K_i\\to\\mathbb C^m$, where $\\mathbb C^m$ has its standard complex inner product, there is a unitary $U$ on $\\mathbb C^m$ such that\n\n$$ (I_H\\otimes U)(I_H\\otimes\\iota_2)\\Psi_2=(I_H\\otimes\\iota_1)\\Psi_1. $$",
