      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Let $E=A\\oplus\\mathbb C e_E$ with $e_E$ a unit vector orthogonal to the data summand, and write $J_B,J_E$ for the data inclusions. Define $V_\\epsilon x:=\\sqrt{1-\\epsilon}\\,J_Bx\\otimes e_E+\\sqrt\\epsilon\\,e\\otimes J_Ex$. The summands lie in orthogonal subspaces of $B\\otimes E$, so for all $x,y\\in A$, $\\langle V_\\epsilon x,V_\\epsilon y\\rangle=(1-\\epsilon)\\langle x,y\\rangle+\\epsilon\\langle x,y\\rangle=\\langle x,y\\rangle$. Thus $V_\\epsilon$ is a linear isometry, including at $\\epsilon=0$ and $\\epsilon=1$.",
