          "id": "step-2-1",
          "claim": "Expanding $V_\\epsilon X V_\\epsilon^*$ gives two diagonal terms and two cross terms. The first diagonal term is $(1-\\epsilon)J_BXJ_B^*\\otimes|e_E\\rangle\\langle e_E|$, whose partial trace over $E$ is $(1-\\epsilon)J_BXJ_B^*$. The second is $\\epsilon|e\\rangle\\langle e|\\otimes J_EXJ_E^*$, whose partial trace is $\\epsilon\\operatorname{tr}(X)|e\\rangle\\langle e|$. Each cross term has a partial-trace coefficient equal to the inner product of the orthogonal erasure flag with the data subspace, hence vanishes. Therefore $\\operatorname{Tr}_E(V_\\epsilon X V_\\epsilon^*)=\\mathcal E_{d,\\epsilon}(X)$ for every $X$.",
