        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "def-qc-ensemble-and-purification",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Let $H$ be a nonzero finite-dimensional complex-inner-product space. A **finite ensemble of density operators** on $H$ is a positive integer $n$, weights $p_1,\\ldots,p_n\\ge0$ with $\\sum_{a=1}^np_a=1$, and density operators $\\rho_1,\\ldots,\\rho_n$ on $H$. Its **barycenter** is $\\bar\\rho=\\sum_{a=1}^np_a\\rho_a$. A zero-weight component still names a density operator but contributes zero to the barycenter.\n\nLet $K$ be any finite-dimensional complex-inner-product space. A **purification** of a density operator $\\rho$ on $H$ is a unit vector $\\Psi\\in H\\otimes K$ such that\n\n$$\\operatorname{Tr}_K(|\\Psi\\rangle\\langle\\Psi|)=\\rho.$$\n\nThe tensor factors are ordered $H$ then $K$. Tensor products, outer products and partial trace have the conventions of [[def-qc-tensor-register-and-permutation]], [[def-qc-dirac-notation-conversion]] and [[def-qc-partial-trace]]. The auxiliary space may be any finite dimension that supports such a unit vector.",
          "uses": [
