          "source": "lem-it-dimension-dependent-quantum-entropy-continuity",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Write $h(t)=-t\\ln t-(1-t)\\ln(1-t)$ with continuous endpoints. Let $g(t)=(1+t)\\ln(1+t)-t\\ln t$ for $t\\in[0,1]$, with $g(0)=0$. For states $\\rho,\\sigma$ on dimension $d\\ge1$ and $t=\\frac12\\|\\rho-\\sigma\\|_1$, $$|S(\\rho)-S(\\sigma)|\\le t\\ln d+g(t).$$ Moreover, if $\\sigma_1,\\ldots,\\sigma_M$ are states on that space and $a=M^{-1}\\sum_m\\frac12\\|\\sigma_m-\\sigma\\|_1$, their uniform Holevo information is at most $2a\\ln d+2g(a)$. In particular on dimension $d_E^n$, exponential decay of $a$ makes unnormalized Holevo information tend to zero.",
