          "source": "def-it-classical-quantum-state-and-holevo-information",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Let $X$ be a finite nonempty classical label set, represented by a register $H_X$ with computational orthonormal basis $(\\xi_x)_{x\\in X}$ ([[def-qc-register-and-computational-basis]]). For each $x$, write $\\Pi_xz:=\\langle z,\\xi_x\\rangle\\xi_x$, the rank-one orthogonal projection using the root linear-first convention, as in [[lem-it-finite-cq-block-sum-is-a-state]]. Let $H_B$ be a nonzero finite-dimensional complex inner-product space. A finite **classical-quantum state** is\n\n$$\\rho_{XB}:=\\sum_{x\\in X}p_x\\Pi_x\\otimes\\rho_x,$$\n\nwhere $p_x\\ge0$, $\\sum_xp_x=1$, and each $\\rho_x$ is a density operator on $H_B$. It is a density operator by [[lem-it-finite-cq-block-sum-is-a-state]]. Its quantum marginal is $\\bar\\rho_B:=\\sum_xp_x\\rho_x=\\operatorname{Tr}_X\\rho_{XB}$ by the second-factor partial-trace formula in [[def-qc-partial-trace]], and it is a density operator by [[lem-it-partial-traces-of-a-state-are-states]]. The **Holevo information** of this ensemble is\n\n$$\\chi(\\{p_x,\\rho_x\\}_{x\\in X}):=S(\\bar\\rho_B)-\\sum_{x:p_x>0}p_xS(\\rho_x),$$\n\nwhere zero-probability branches contribute nothing. This is measured in nats under [[def-it-von-neumann-entropy]].",
