    "lem-finite-trellis-prefix-score-recurrence": {
      "citations": [
        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "def-finite-layered-trellis",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "A **finite weighted trellis** has an integer length $T\\ge0$. If $T=0$, it is\nthe empty structure, with no vertex layers, edges, or endpoint weights. If\n$T\\ge1$, it consists of finite vertex sets $V_1,\\ldots,V_T$, edge sets\n$E_t\\subseteq V_{t-1}\\times V_t$ for $2\\le t\\le T$, positive edge weights\n$w_t:E_t\\to(0,\\infty)$, and initial and terminal weights\n$\\alpha:V_1\\to[0,\\infty)$ and $\\beta:V_T\\to[0,\\infty)$. The sets $V_t$ may\nbe empty. A zero initial or terminal weight disables that endpoint; every edge\nin $E_t$ is allowed and has positive weight.\n\nA **path** for $T\\ge1$ is a tuple $(v_1,\\ldots,v_T)$ with $v_t\\in V_t$,\n$\\alpha(v_1)>0$, $\\beta(v_T)>0$, and $(v_{t-1},v_t)\\in E_t$ for every\n$2\\le t\\le T$. Its **score** is\n$$\\alpha(v_1)\\left(\\prod_{t=2}^{T}w_t(v_{t-1},v_t)\\right)\\beta(v_T),$$\nwhere the empty product for $T=1$ is $1$. For $T=0$, the unique path is the\nempty tuple, with score $1$ (the empty product).\n\nA **prefix path through layer $t$**, for $1\\le t\\le T$, satisfies the same\nconditions through $v_t$, without a terminal-weight condition. For $T=0$,\nthe empty tuple is the unique prefix path through no layers, with score $1$.\nA vertex $v\\in V_t$ is **reachable** if some prefix path ends at $v$;\notherwise it is **unreachable**. There are finitely many paths. If at least\none path exists, its maximum score is attained; if none exists, the trellis\nhas no admissible path.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "1.2"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "If $T=0$, the unique prefix path through no layers is empty and has score $1$. For $T\\ge1$, at layer $1$ the only prefix ending at $v$ is the one-vertex prefix. It exists exactly when $\\alpha(v)>0$, and then has score $\\alpha(v)=D_1(v)$; when $\\alpha(v)=0$ there is no prefix and $D_1(v)=0$.",
          "step": "1.1",
          "inputs": [
            "given",
            "F1",
            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-1-2",
          "claim": "Fix $t\\ge2$ and $v\\in V_t$. Every prefix ending at $v$ has a predecessor $u$ with $(u,v)\\in E_t$ and is obtained by appending that edge to a prefix ending at $u$. Its score is the predecessor-prefix score multiplied by the positive weight $w_t(u,v)$. By [A1], the best such extension through each $u$ has score $D_{t-1}(u)w_t(u,v)$; if no predecessor prefix exists this value is zero. Taking the maximum over the finite predecessor set, with zero when it is empty, gives exactly the stated recurrence.",
          "step": "1.2",
          "inputs": [
            "given",
