        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "lem-finite-trellis-prefix-score-recurrence",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For a finite weighted trellis with $T=0$, the unique prefix path through no\nlayers is empty and has score $1$. For $T\\ge1$, define $D_1(v)=\\alpha(v)$ and,\nfor $2\\le t\\le T$,\n$$D_t(v)=\\max\\bigl(\\{D_{t-1}(u)w_t(u,v):(u,v)\\in E_t\\}\\cup\\{0\\}\\bigr).$$\nThen $D_t(v)$ is the maximum score of a prefix path ending at $v$; if no such\nprefix exists, $D_t(v)=0$.",
          "uses": [
