          "quote": "Let $\\mathcal C$ be a unitary fusion category, let $\\operatorname{Irr}(\\mathcal C)$\nbe the representative set fixed in [[def-qc-tqc-fusion-tree-basis]], and take\n$a_1,\\ldots,a_n,d\\in\\operatorname{Irr}(\\mathcal C)$. Fix any parenthesized\nbinary tree $T$ on the ordered input list. The fusion-tree vectors of\n[[def-qc-tqc-fusion-tree-basis]] form an orthonormal basis of\n$\\operatorname{Hom}(T,d)$. For $n\\ge2$, their number is\n\n$$m_T(d)=\\sum_{\\substack{\\ell\\text{ admissible, with every internal label in }\\operatorname{Irr}(\\mathcal C)}}\\;\\prod_{v\\,\\mathrm{internal}}N_{\\ell(v_L)\\,\\ell(v_R)}^{\\ell(v)},$$\n\nwhere the sum runs over charge labelings only (the product counts the\nvertex multiplicity indices), the leaves carry the inputs, the root carries\n$d$, and each internal edge is labeled by a representative simple charge.\nFor the empty tree, $m_0(d)=1$ if $d=\\mathbf1$ and $0$ otherwise; for one\ninput, $m_1(d)=1$ if $a_1=d$ and $0$ otherwise. The left-associated tree on\n$n\\ge2$ inputs satisfies\n\n$$m_n(d)=\\sum_e m_{n-1}(e)N_{e a_n}^d\\qquad(n\\ge2).$$",
