        {
          "id": "step-1-2",
          "claim": "A projective class of $\\operatorname{diag}(x,y)$ has the same order as $r=y/x$. In the Fibonacci case $r=e^{2\\pi i(-3/10)}$ has exact order $10$ because $\\gcd(3,10)=1$. In the Ising case $r=i$ has exact order $4$. These orders ignore only the common scalar $x$.",
          "step": "1.2",
