          "id": "step-2-1",
          "claim": "In the Fibonacci case put $r=y/x=e^{-3\\pi i/5}$ and $D=\\operatorname{diag}(1,r)$. Then $B_1=xD$ and $B_2=xC$, where $C=FDF$. Put $s=r^2+ur+1$. Direct multiplication gives $$DCD-C DC= \\begin{pmatrix} u^3(1-r)s&-u^3v(1-r)s\\\\ -u^3v(1-r)s&u^3(r-1)s \\end{pmatrix}.$$ Here $u^2+u=1$, $v^2=u$, and $r+r^{-1}=2\\cos(3\\pi/5)=-u$, so $s=0$. Thus $DCD=CDC$ and $B_1B_2B_1=x^3DCD=x^3CDC=B_2B_1B_2$.",
          "step": "2.1",
