        {
          "fact": "F4",
          "source": "def-qc-tensor-map",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "For a finite ordered family of finite-dimensional complex vector spaces\n$H_k,K_k$ and complex-linear maps $T_k:H_k\\to K_k$, the **tensor map**\n$\\bigotimes_{k<n}T_k:H_0\\otimes\\cdots\\otimes H_{n-1}\\to\nK_0\\otimes\\cdots\\otimes K_{n-1}$ is the unique linear map satisfying\n\n$$\\left(\\bigotimes_{k<n}T_k\\right)(x_0\\otimes\\cdots\\otimes x_{n-1})=T_0x_0\\otimes\\cdots\\otimes T_{n-1}x_{n-1}.$$\n\nFor $n=0$, the tensor map is the identity map $z\\mapsto z$ on the empty tensor\nproduct $\\mathbb C$.",
