          "source": "lem-qc-tqc-toric-incidence-ranks",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For $L\\ge3$, the $L^2$ star-support vectors in $\\mathbb F_2^E$ have span\ndimension $L^2-1$, and their only relation is their total sum. The $L^2$\nface-boundary vectors have the same span dimension and their only relation\nis their total sum. The dual-face incidence statement has the same rank.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "def-qc-stabilizer-code-space",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Let $n\\ge1$ and let $S$ be an abelian subgroup of the Hermitian elements of\nthe phase-aware Pauli group $\\mathcal P_n$ on the ordered $n$-qubit register.\nAssume $-I\\notin S$. The **stabilizer code space** is the common $+1$\neigenspace\n\n$$\\mathcal C(S):=\\{\\psi\\in(\\mathbb C^2)^{\\otimes n}:g\\psi=\\psi\\text{ for every }g\\in S\\}.$$\n\nIf $g_1,\\ldots,g_r$ are independent generators of $S$, the associated\nstabilizer rank is $r$; independence means no nonempty product of distinct\ngenerators is $I$. The code-space projector and its nonzero dimension are\nestablished by [[thm-qc-stabilizer-projector-and-dimension]].",
          "uses": [
            "2.1",
            "3.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F4",
          "source": "def-qc-stabilizer-syndrome-and-logical-operators",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Let $n\\ge1$ and let $S$ be a stabilizer subgroup generated by an ordered independent\nHermitian list $g_1,\\ldots,g_r$. For a phase-aware Pauli error $E$, its\n**syndrome** is the bit string $s(E)\\in\\mathbb F_2^r$ defined by\n\n$$E g_j=(-1)^{s_j(E)}g_jE,\\qquad s_j(E):=\\omega(\\lambda(E),\\lambda(g_j)).$$\n\nHere $\\lambda(P(k,x,z))=(x,z)$ is the binary Pauli label and\n$\\omega((x,z),(x',z'))=x\\cdot z'+z\\cdot x'$. The scalar center of\n$\\mathcal P_n$ is $Z_n=\\{i^kI:k\\in\\mathbb Z/4\\mathbb Z\\}$, and the\n**normalizer** is $N(S)=\\{P\\in\\mathcal P_n:Pg=gP\\text{ for every }g\\in S\\}$.\nThe **logical Pauli classes** form the quotient group\n\n$$N(S)/(Z_nS).$$\n\nA normalizer element is logically nontrivial exactly when it lies in\n$N(S)\\setminus Z_nS$. Multiplication by a scalar phase does not change a\nsyndrome or logical class.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F5",
          "source": "thm-qc-stabilizer-projector-and-dimension",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $n\\ge1$ and let $S$ be an abelian group of Hermitian $n$-qubit Pauli operators with\n$-I\\notin S$, generated by $r$ independent checks. Then\n\n$$P_S:=|S|^{-1}\\sum_{g\\in S}g$$\n\nis the orthogonal projector onto the stabilizer code space and has rank\n$2^{n-r}$. In particular, the code space is nonzero, including when $r=n$.",
          "uses": [
            "3.1"
