      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "d1_1",
          "claim": "By [F1], $\\bar Z_1$ and $\\bar X_1$ share only $h_{0,0}$, while $\\bar Z_2$ and $\\bar X_2$ share only $v_{0,0}$. [F6] gives anticommutation for these equal-index pairs. The cross pairs $(\\bar Z_1,\\bar X_2)$ and $(\\bar Z_2,\\bar X_1)$ have disjoint physical-edge supports, so [F2] gives commutation for unequal indices. Two Z strings commute with one another and two X strings commute with one another because their factors have the same Pauli type.",
