    "thm-qc-tqc-toric-constant-barrier": {
      "risk": "high",
      "kind": "theorem",
      "citations": [
        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "def-qc-tqc-toric-energy-barrier",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Fix $L\\ge3$, $J_e,J_m>0$, a unit vector $\\psi$ in the toric code space, and\na specified nontrivial logical Pauli representative $Q$. An **elementary\nPauli path to $Q$** is a finite sequence $E_0,\\ldots,E_T$ with $E_0=I$,\n$E_T$ a scalar-phase multiple of $Q$, and\n$E_{r+1}=P_rE_r$, where each $P_r$ is $X$, $Y$, or $Z$ on a single edge and\nthe identity on every other edge.\n\nFor any prefix Pauli $E$, define its energy excess\n$\\varepsilon(E):=\\langle E\\psi,H_LE\\psi\\rangle-E_{\\rm code}$, where\n$E_{\\rm code}:=-L^2(J_e+J_m)$ is the energy of every code vector. The\n**Pauli-path energy barrier** of $Q$ is\n\n$$\\mathcal B_L(Q):=\\min_{(E_0,\\ldots,E_T)}\\max_{0\\le r\\le T}\\varepsilon(E_r),$$\n\nwhere the minimum ranges over elementary Pauli paths to $Q$. This is a\nfinite-code energy quantity; it is not a thermal lifetime.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "1.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "thm-qc-tqc-toric-gap",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For the finite toric-code Hamiltonian\n$H_L=-J_e\\sum_q A_q-J_m\\sum_f B_f$ with $J_e,J_m>0$, the ground space is\nthe four-dimensional toric code space and the ground energy is\n$E_g=-L^2(J_e+J_m)$. The exact spectral gap above it is\n$\\Delta_L=4\\min(J_e,J_m)$.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "1.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "lem-qc-tqc-toric-string-syndrome",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $P$ be a primal edge trail with no repeated edge and distinct endpoints\n$q_0,q_1$. The Pauli string $Z(P)$ has commutation syndrome $1$ at exactly\nthe two endpoint stars and $0$ at every other star or plaquette. Let $Q$ be\na dual edge trail with no repeated edge and distinct endpoint faces\n$f_0,f_1$. The string $X(Q)$ has commutation syndrome $1$ at exactly those\ntwo endpoint plaquettes and $0$ at every other plaquette or star.\n\nIf either kind of edge-simple trail is closed, its corresponding string has\nzero syndrome at every check.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "1.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F4",
