          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $\\rho,\\sigma$ be density operators on a finite-dimensional complex Hilbert space and let $\\{E_a\\}_{a\\in\\mathcal A}$ be any finite POVM. If $p_a=\\operatorname{tr}(\\rho E_a)$ and $q_a=\\operatorname{tr}(\\sigma E_a)$, then\n$$\\frac12\\sum_{a\\in\\mathcal A}|p_a-q_a|\\le D(\\rho,\\sigma).$$\nThe two-effect projective measurement from the Holevo–Helstrom theorem attains equality.",
          "uses": [
