          "quote": "Let $A=A^0\\oplus A^1$ be a $\\mathbb Z/2$-graded unital associative algebra over a field, and suppose it contains an invertible homogeneous element $u\\in A^1$. For left modules, the rule $M\\mapsto M^0$ gives a bijection between isomorphism classes of graded-simple $A$-modules (with even isomorphisms) and isomorphism classes of simple $A^0$-modules. An inverse sends a left $A^0$-module $N$ to the induced graded module $A\\otimes_{A^0}N$.",
