          "source": "lem-lichnerowicz-formula-for-geometric-dirac-operators",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume full AC. Let $M$ be a Riemannian manifold and $V$ a graded Hermitian Clifford module with compatible connection as in [[def-graded-hermitian-clifford-module-and-geometric-dirac]]. Use $R(X,Y)=[\\nabla^{LC}_X,\\nabla^{LC}_Y]-\\nabla^{LC}_{[X,Y]}$ and $\\operatorname{Rm}(X,Y,Z,W)=g(R(X,Y)Z,W)$. In a local oriented orthonormal frame define\n$$F^S_{ij}=\\frac14\\sum_{a,b}\\operatorname{Rm}(e_i,e_j,e_a,e_b)c(e^a)c(e^b),\\qquad F^{V/S}_{ij}=F^V_{ij}-F^S_{ij}.$$\nThen $F^{V/S}_{ij}$ commutes with Clifford multiplication and\n$$D_V^2=(\\nabla^V)^*\\nabla^V+\\frac{\\operatorname{scal}_g}{4}I+\\sum_{i<j}c(e^i)c(e^j)F^{V/S}_{ij}.$$\nIts positive-frequency principal symbol is $|\\xi|^2I$ in every dimension. When $M$ is compact and boundaryless and $n\\ge2$, $D_V^2$ is formally symmetric Laplace type in the sense of [[def-second-order-laplace-type-operators-on-vector-bundles]]. In dimension zero, $D_V=0$ and the displayed identity holds directly; no Laplace-type classification is asserted there.",
