th-manifold-and-oriented-chart]]). The reference zero-dimensional Clifford module $S_{0,x}$ is the complex line with grading operator $\\Gamma_{S_{0,x}}=\\varepsilon_x I$: it is even at a positive point and odd at a negative point. The zero-dimensional Clifford algebra is $\\mathbb C$, acting by scalars. Set $W_x=\\operatorname{Hom}_{\\mathbb C}(S_{0,x},V_x)$ with the grading for which evaluation $S_{0,x}\\widehat\\otimes W_x\\to V_x$ is even. Identifying a map with its value at $1$ gives $\\Gamma_{W_x}=\\varepsilon_x\\Gamma_{V_x}$. All curvature two-forms vanish, so $\\widehat A_0=1$, $F^{V/S}=0$, and\n$$\\operatorname{ch}(V/S)_0(x)=\\operatorname{str}_{W_x}I=\\varepsilon_x\\bigl(\\dim V_x^+-\\dim V_x^-\\bigr).$$\nThis formula is independent of any basis of $V_x$ and leaves its arbitrary given grading unrestricted. For $V=S_0\\widehat\\otimes E$ with $E$ in even degree, evaluation identifies $W=E$ in even degree, so the relative character is the ordinary rank, consistently with the product formula above. This reference-line convention makes no assertion about a Spin$(0)$ lift or its isomorphism classes.",
