          "claim": "Write $\\phi\\circ_i\\psi$ for insertion of a $q$-cochain into slot $i$ of a $p$-cochain, with slots numbered from $0$, so $\\phi\\circ\\psi=\\sum_{i=0}^{p-1}(-1)^{i(q-1)}\\phi\\circ_i\\psi$. In $(\\phi\\circ\\psi)\\circ\\chi-\\phi\\circ(\\psi\\circ\\chi)$, terms where $\\chi$ is inserted into the block occupied by $\\psi$ cancel. If that block starts at slot $i$ and $\\chi$ is inserted into its local slot $s$, the first expression has coefficient $(-1)^{i(q-1)+(i+s)(r-1)}$, while the second has coefficient $(-1)^{i(q+r-2)+s(r-1)}$; these exponents agree. Every remaining term is a pair of insertions into distinct original slots of $\\phi$. For original slots $i<j$, the coefficient with $\\psi$ inserted first and $\\chi$ second is $(-1)^{i(q-1)+(j+q-1)(r-1)}$; with the insertion order swapped it is $(-1)^{j(r-1)+i(q-1)}$. Their ratio is $(-1)^{(q-1)(r-1)}$. The same comparison for $j<i$ puts the earlier insertion first and gives that same ratio. Thus, with $|\\psi|=q-1$ and $|\\chi|=r-1$, $$\\operatorname{as}(\\phi,\\psi,\\chi) =(-1)^{|\\psi||\\chi|}\\operatorname{as}(\\phi,\\chi,\\psi), \\qquad \\operatorname{as}(u,v,w):=(u\\circ v)\\circ w-u\\circ(v\\circ w).$$",
