          "quote": "Let $\\mathfrak g$ be a cohomologically graded Lie algebra over a characteristic-zero field: its degree-zero bracket is graded skew, satisfies graded Jacobi, and a degree-one map $d$ satisfies $d^2=0$ and $d[x,y]=[dx,y]+(-1)^{|x|}[x,dy]$. Suppose its degreewise separated complete positive filtration is preserved by $d$ and satisfies $[F^r\\mathfrak g,F^s\\mathfrak g]\\subseteq F^{r+s}\\mathfrak g$. With $s:\\mathfrak g\\to\\mathfrak g[1]$ of degree $-1$, set\n\n$$q_1(sx)=-s(dx),\\qquad q_2(sx,sy)=(-1)^{|x|}s[x,y],\\qquad q_n=0\\ (n\\ge3).$$\n\nThese operations define a complete filtered shifted L∞-algebra. Its degree-zero Maurer–Cartan elements are exactly $sR$, where $R\\in F^1\\mathfrak g^1$ satisfies $dR+[R,R]/2=0$. Its elementary gauge paths are exactly $R'=-d\\xi+[\\xi,R]$ with $\\xi\\in F^1\\mathfrak g^0[t]^{\\wedge}$, under $w=sR$, $a=s\\xi$.",
