          "claim": "Put $V_B=\\varprojlim_n(A[1]\\otimes_k B/I^n)$ and $V_B^{\\widehat\\otimes r}=\\varprojlim_n((A[1])^{\\otimes r}\\otimes_k B/I^n)$. A continuous homogeneous positive-arity Taylor map $f:V_B^{\\widehat\\otimes r}\\to V_B$ of degree $u$ extends by inserting $f$ in every consecutive block of a word, with sign $(-1)^{u(|v_1|+\\cdots+|v_{i-1}|)}$ for a block starting at $i$. Each word has only finitely many such blocks. Splitting the output word shows the coderivation equation: the replaced block lies entirely on one side of a coproduct split, and its insertion sign agrees with that side's graded tensor action. Thus these formulas define the coderivation and extend continuously through coefficient completion. Conversely, applying the iterated reduced coproduct and projecting every factor to length one expresses the length-$j$ component of a coderivation as the sum with its length-one projection on one of the $j$ input factors. Its other components are the untouched factors. This follows by iterating the coderivation equation. It determines every length component uniquely, and proves there is no output of length greater than the input length because all $j$ factors must be nonempty. The argument holds at each coefficient quotient and then in the limit. Thus these Taylor maps give every coaugmented counital coderivation uniquely.",
