          "quote": "Assume Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]), and let $H$ be a complex Hilbert space. For each $k\\ge0$, let $\\Lambda^kH$ be the Hilbert exterior power with the Gram-determinant inner product and wedge convention of [[def-hilbert-exterior-power-and-induced-operator]], with $\\Lambda^0H=\\mathbb C$. The algebraic direct sum $X_0=\\bigoplus_{k\\ge0}^{\\mathrm{alg}}\\Lambda^kH$, where distinct particle-number summands are orthogonal and the inner product on a finite sum is the sum of the component inner products, is an inner-product space. Its norm completion exists under Countable Choice by [[thm-metric-completion-exists]] and has its compatible Banach-space and Hilbert-space structures by [[thm-metric-completion-carries-a-unique-banach-space-structure]] and [[thm-completion-of-an-inner-product-space-is-hilbert]]. The **fermionic Fock space** over $H$ is this Hilbert completion. The **vacuum vector** $\\Omega$ is the image of $1\\in\\Lambda^0H$ in the completion.\n\nOn finite sums of decomposable wedges define the creation rule $C(f)\\xi=f\\wedge\\xi$ for $f\\in H$. This rule is initially defined on a dense subspace. Its bounded extension and the CAR relations for $C(f)$ and its Hilbert-space adjoint are proved in [[lem-fock-creation-annihilation-satisfy-car]].",
