          "source": "def-finite-dimensional-gapped-free-hamiltonian-and-stable-equivalence",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "A finite-dimensional free-fermion Hamiltonian is a self-adjoint matrix on a finite-dimensional complex Hilbert space. It is gapped at zero if 0 is not in its spectrum. A symmetry class is specified by named unitary and antiunitary operators and exact commutation, anticommutation and square relations with H. Stable equivalence means gap-preserving homotopy after direct sum with fixed reference trivial bands; phases are differences of stabilized systems, not absolute modules.\n\nClass A has no additional antiunitary constraint. A symmetry is unitary or antiunitary and its relation is recorded as S H S^{-1}=σH, σ∈{+1,−1}; any additional square relation is part of the declared model data.",
