        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "lem-finite-cw-relative-ko-triples-and-homotopy-invariance",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume AC. For a finite CW pair $(X,A)$, $KO^0(X,A)$ is naturally the group of triples $(E,F,g)$, with $E,F$ real bundles on $X$ and $g:E|_A\\to F|_A$ an isomorphism. Relations are bundle isomorphism, direct-sum additivity, homotopy of $g$, and deletion of a triple whose $g$ extends to an isomorphism on $X$. Equivalently, use stable homotopy of triples, allowing addition of such elementary triples. Pullback along homotopic maps of pairs induces equal maps. In degree zero over $X$, equality of virtual bundles is equality after common trivial stabilization. Every real bundle on $X$ has a finite trivial complement. The analogous complement, stable-isomorphism, homotopy and triple statements hold for right-$\\mathbb H$ bundles. All these conclusions also hold for compact Hausdorff pairs with closed subspace; this includes disk, sphere and Thom bundle spaces over compact finite CW bases.",
