          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "def-reduced-relative-ko-and-ko-compact-support",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "For a based compact Hausdorff space $(Y,*)$, set $\\widetilde {KO}^0(Y)=\\ker(KO^0(Y)\\to KO^0(*))$. For a compact pair with closed subspace $A\\subset X$, set $KO^0(X,A)=\\widetilde {KO}^0(X/A)$, where all of $A$ is collapsed to one basepoint. If $A=\\varnothing$, use $X_+=X\\amalg\\{*\\}$ instead. Set $KO^{-j}(X,A)=\\widetilde {KO}^0(S^j\\wedge(X/A))$ for $j\\geq0$, and $KO^{-j}(X)=KO^{-j}(X,\\varnothing)$. The same conventions define reduced, relative and negative-degree $KSp$.\n\nFor a finite-rank metric real bundle $V\\to X$ over compact $X$, write $\\operatorname{Th}(V)=D(V)/S(V)$ and $KO_c^{-j}(V)=\\widetilde {KO}^0(S^j\\wedge\\operatorname{Th}(V))$. At rank zero use $\\operatorname{Th}(0)=X_+$. These definitions do not assert any periodicity or an isomorphism between successive degrees.",
