          "quote": "Assume AC. Let $\\beta\\in\\widetilde{KO}^0(S^8)=KO^{-8}(\\mathrm{pt})$ be the volume-positive rank-eight real spinor symbol of the trivial bundle, with the source-minus-target relative-triple convention. For every finite CW pair $(X,A)$, multiplication by this same class is a natural isomorphism $KO^j(X,A)\\to KO^{j-8}(X,A)$ in every integer degree. In particular it gives $KO^0(X)\\cong\\widetilde{KO}^0(X_+\\wedge S^8)$. These maps respect external products; positive degrees are defined by the resulting periodic continuation of the bundle theory. No complexification or coefficient table is used.",
