          "claim": "Transport $H_0$ by $w$ so that both masses act on the same fixed representation. Define first an auxiliary comparison $\\Phi_q$ with the positive-rank convention, and finally set $\\Psi_q=-\\Phi_q$ in EVERY degree. For $q=0$ put $\\Phi_0=\\dim W_H^+-\\dim W_{H_0}^+$. Equal total dimensions give $-\\Phi_0=\\dim W_H^--\\dim W_{H_0}^-$. The uniform negation is part of the comparison convention; it will also negate integer-valued Hopf classes in degrees divisible by four.",
