          "claim": "If $A=A_0$, the clutching map factors through the closed upper hemisphere by $t\\mapsto|t|$. That disk contracts to the chosen equatorial basepoint while fixing the point, so its clutching map is based nullhomotopic. Common reference blocks contribute zero. Mass homotopies give homotopies of clutching maps; simultaneous coordinate changes conjugate the clutching map and give isomorphic bundles; direct sums give block sums and hence sums of reduced classes. These conclusions hold also in step 1.1 and step 1.2. Reversing the two masses reflects the clutching sphere and negates its class by the reflection/block-rotation proof in [F2]. Thus $\\Phi_q$, and consequently $\\Psi_q$, respect stable difference relations and inverses.",
