          "quote": "For a finite-dimensional complex simple Lie algebra $\\mathfrak g$ as in [[def-loop-algebra-of-a-simple-lie-algebra]], use the invariant form $B$ normalized by long roots of square $2$ in [[def-residue-two-cocycle-on-a-loop-algebra]]. The local trace calculation below shows that the Casimir $\\Omega_B$ from [[def-casimir-operator-relative-to-an-invariant-form]] acts in the adjoint representation as $\\gamma_B I$ for a unique positive real scalar $\\gamma_B$. Define the **dual Coxeter number** by $h^\\vee=\\gamma_B/2$. If a compact real form $\\mathfrak k$ from [[def-compact-real-form-of-a-complex-semisimple-lie-algebra]] is additionally supplied, then for every $Q=-B|_{\\mathfrak k}$-orthonormal basis $(X_i)$ one has $-\\sum_i\\operatorname{ad}(X_i)^2=2h^\\vee I$. This is the normalization used in the affine central term and every Sugawara denominator below; existence of a compact real form is not needed to define $h^\\vee$.",
