          "quote": "Let $\\mathfrak g$ be a finite-dimensional complex simple Lie algebra with the invariant form used in [[def-untwisted-affine-central-extension]]. A representation $\\rho$ of the loop central extension $\\overline{L\\mathfrak g}$ is a **restricted affine-current module of level $k\\in\\mathbb C$** if the central generator acts as $k\\operatorname{id}$ and, for every vector $v$ and current $x\\in\\mathfrak g$, there is an integer $N(v,x)$ such that $\\rho(x\\otimes t^n)v=0$ for all $n\\ge N(v,x)$.\n\nThe algebra in this definition is the central extension only; it does not contain the degree derivation. Restrictedness is a mode-truncation condition and does not itself supply an energy grading. A compatible positive-energy grading is extra structure on this current algebra.",
