          "source": "thm-universal-affine-vertex-algebra",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $\\mathfrak g$ be a finite-dimensional complex simple Lie algebra, let $B$ be the normalized invariant form of [[def-untwisted-affine-central-extension]], and let $k\\in\\mathbb C$. The induced module $V^k(\\mathfrak g)$ of [[def-universal-affine-vacuum-module]] has a unique vertex-algebra structure in the convention of [[def-vertex-algebra-state-field]] for which $\\mathbf1$ is the vacuum and\n$$Y(x_{-1}\\mathbf1,z)=J^x(z)=\\sum_{n\\in\\mathbb Z}x_nz^{-n-1}\\qquad(x\\in\\mathfrak g).$$\nThis construction is valid for every complex level, including values at which a normalized Sugawara denominator vanishes. It asserts no conformal vector, simple quotient, unitarity, or integrability.",
