          "quote": "Let $U_q^-=\\bigoplus_{\\nu\\in Q_+}U_q^-[-\\nu]$ be the negative half of the\nDrinfeld-Jimbo algebra of a finite symmetrizable Cartan datum with $a_{ii}=2$\n([[def-drinfeld-jimbo-quantized-enveloping-algebra]],\n[[def-positive-negative-and-toral-quantum-subalgebras]]), with skew derivations\n$e_i',e_i''$ ([[def-kashiwara-skew-derivations-on-the-negative-quantum-half]]),\nand let $(\\ ,\\ )$ be a bilinear form on $U_q^-$.\n\n(i) **Existence and symmetry.** A bilinear form with $(1,1)=1$ and\n$(F_iP,Q)=(P,e_i'(Q))$ for all $i,P,Q$ exists on $U_q^-$; every normalized\nhomogeneous form satisfying these conditions is symmetric; and by the\nuniqueness of [[def-the-lusztig-kashiwara-bilinear-form-on-the-negative-quantum-half]]\nthere is exactly one such form. No separate right-adjunction formula for\n$(P,QF_i)$ is asserted: in the rank-one subalgebra a formula\n$(P,QF_i)=c\\,(e_i''P,Q)$ with constant $c$ is false, as the explicit values in\n(iv) show.\n\n(ii) **Orthogonality.** $(U_q^-[-\\nu],U_q^-[-\\mu])=0$ whenever $\\nu\\ne\\mu$.\n\n(iii) **Nondegeneracy.** For every $0\\ne x\\in U_q^-$ there is $y\\in U_q^-$ with\n$(x,y)\\ne0$; equivalently, the restriction of the form to each\nfinite-dimensional graded piece $U_q^-[-\\nu]$ is nondegenerate.\n\n(iv) **Integrality on the word lattice.** Let $A=\\mathbb Z[q,q^{-1}]$\n([[def-the-laurent-polynomial-ring]]) and let $W\\subseteq U_A^-$ be the\n$A$-span of the monomials $F_{i_1}\\cdots F_{i_k}$ ($k\\ge0$). Then\n$W\\subseteq U_A^-$ (because $F_i^k=[k]_i!F_i^{(k)}$ and $[k]_i!\\in A$), and\n$(W,W)\\subseteq A$. On the larger divided-power lattice $U_A^-$ the form is\n*not* $A$-valued: in the rank-one subalgebra generated by a single $F_i$ one\nhas, for all $a,b\\ge0$,\n$$(F_i^{(a)},F_i^{(b)})=\\delta_{ab}\\frac{q_i^{-a(a-1)/2}}{[a]_i!}=\\delta_{ab}\\frac{1}{[a]_{q_i^2}!},$$\nin particular $(F_i^{(2)},F_i^{(2)})=1/(1+q_i^2)\\notin A$; here\n$[a]_{q_i^2}!=\\prod_{m=1}^a(1+q_i^2+\\cdots+q_i^{2(m-1)})$. Globally, with\n$A_{\\mathrm{loc}}=A[s^{-1}:s\\in S]$, the localization of $A$ inverting the\nmultiplicative set $S$ generated by $\\{[r]_i!:i\\in I,r\\ge1\\}$ (equivalently inverting the\nGaussian factorials $[r]_{q_i^2}!$), one has\n$(U_A^-,U_A^-)\\subseteq A_{\\mathrm{loc}}$: divided-power words are word\nvectors divided by finite products of these factorials. This is an exact\ndenominator bound, not an $A$-integrality assertion on $U_A^-$ in this\nnormalization.",
