          "quote": "Let $\\psi$ (the bar involution) and $\\tau$ (the contravariant anti-involution) be\nthe semilinear maps of\n[[lem-quantum-serre-relations-are-stable-under-the-chevalley-involutions]], so\nthat $\\psi(q)=q^{-1}$, $\\psi(E_i)=E_i$, $\\psi(F_i)=F_i$, $\\psi(K_h)=K_h^{-1}$\nand $\\tau(q)=q^{-1}$, $\\tau(E_i)=F_i$, $\\tau(F_i)=E_i$, $\\tau(K_h)=K_h^{-1}$,\nwith $\\tau$ anti-multiplicative. Let $A=\\mathbb Z[q,q^{-1}]$ and let $U_A$ be\nthe Lusztig divided-power integral form with its generators $E_i^{(r)}$,\n$F_i^{(r)}$, $K_h^{\\pm1}$ and toral binomials $T_{i,c,t}$\n([[def-lusztig-divided-power-integral-form]]). Then $\\psi(U_A)=U_A$ and\n$\\tau(U_A)=U_A$. Explicitly, on the generators,\n\n$$\\psi(E_i^{(r)})=E_i^{(r)},\\quad \\psi(F_i^{(r)})=F_i^{(r)},\\quad \\psi(K_h)=K_h^{-1},\\quad \\psi(T_{i,c,t})=T_{i,c,t},$$\n\n$$\\tau(E_i^{(r)})=F_i^{(r)},\\quad \\tau(F_i^{(r)})=E_i^{(r)},\\quad \\tau(K_h)=K_h^{-1},\\quad \\tau(T_{i,c,t})=T_{i,c,t}.$$\n\nIn particular both maps restrict to bijections of $U_A$: $\\psi$ to a semilinear\nalgebra involution of $U_A$ and $\\tau$ to a semilinear anti-involution of\n$U_A$, while $q^{\\pm1}\\in A$ keeps all coefficients in $A$. These are the two\ninvolutions under which the bar lattice and the contravariant duality of the\nlater constructions are taken; neither formula is the Chevalley involution\n$\\omega$, which changes signs, exchanges the two halves and is treated in\n[[lem-quantum-serre-relations-are-stable-under-the-chevalley-involutions]].\nNo choice is used.",
