          "claim": "The loop space at $f$ of the restricted arrow core over the fixed target $z$ is the homotopy fiber over $f$ of postcomposition $f\\circ-:\\operatorname{Map}(x,x)^{\\simeq}\\to\\operatorname{Map}(x,z)$, based at $\\mathrm{id}_x$. Here the source is the union of components represented by isomorphisms, since this is a core; using all of $\\operatorname{Map}(x,x)$ would include noninvertible endomorphisms. Its positive homotopy groups at $\\mathrm{id}_x$ are $\\operatorname{Ext}^{-i}(x,x)$, and those of $\\operatorname{Map}(x,z)$ are $\\operatorname{Ext}^{-i}(x,z)$. The long exact sequence gives, for each $i\\ge1$, $\\operatorname{Ext}^{-i-1}(x,x)\\to\\operatorname{Ext}^{-i-1}(x,z)\\to\\pi_{i+1}(C_f)\\to\\operatorname{Ext}^{-i}(x,x)\\to\\operatorname{Ext}^{-i}(x,z)$. Its low-degree tail is $\\operatorname{Ext}^{-1}(x,x)\\to\\operatorname{Ext}^{-1}(x,z)\\to\\pi_1(C_f)\\to\\operatorname{Aut}(x)\\to\\operatorname{Hom}_{\\mathcal D(\\mathcal T)}(x,z)$; the kernel of the last map is $\\operatorname{Aut}(f/z)$, the image of $\\pi_1(C_f)$ in $\\operatorname{Aut}(x)$, and the induced map onto that image is surjective.",
