          "claim": "For composable chain maps $x\\xrightarrow{f}y\\xrightarrow{g}z$, put $h=gf$. With the mapping-cone convention $\\operatorname{Cone}(f)^n=y^n\\oplus x^{n+1}$ and $d(y,x)=(d_y y+fx,-d_xx)$, the induced map is $k(y,x)=(gy,x)$. The cone $\\operatorname{Cone}(k)$ has degree-$n$ elements $(z,u,y',x')$ and differential $(d_z z+gf u+gy',-d_xu+x',-d_y y'-fx',d_xx')$. The invertible change $\\widetilde y=y'+fu$, $\\widetilde x=x'-d_xu$ decomposes it as $\\operatorname{Cone}(g)$ plus a contractible identity pair. The homotopy pullback of source and target maps on arrow cores is the core of composable pairs: its data are two arrows and an equivalence of middle objects, which can be strictified by transport. The extra cofiber coordinate is an object with an equivalence to $\\operatorname{Cone}(g)$; these equipped objects form a contractible space over $g$, and the cone calculation supplies its comparison with $\\operatorname{Cone}(k)$. Thus the first square is homotopy cartesian.",
