          "source": "def-canonical-t-structure-on-a-derived-category",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "For a triangulated category $T$ with shift $[1]$, a **t-structure** is a pair of strictly full subcategories $(T^{\\leq0},T^{\\geq0})$ such that $T^{\\leq0}[1]\\subseteq T^{\\leq0}$, $T^{\\geq0}[-1]\\subseteq T^{\\geq0}$, $\\operatorname{Hom}_T(T^{\\leq0},T^{\\geq1})=0$, and every $X$ has a distinguished triangle $A\\to X\\to B\\to A[1]$ with $A\\in T^{\\leq0}$ and $B\\in T^{\\geq1}$. Here $T^{\\geq1}=T^{\\geq0}[-1]$ and $T^{\\leq n}=T^{\\leq0}[-n]$, $T^{\\geq n}=T^{\\geq0}[-n]$. Its **heart** is $T^{\\leq0}\\cap T^{\\geq0}$.\n\nFor the triangulation of [[thm-the-derived-category-inherits-a-triangulated-structure]], the canonical candidate is $D^{\\leq0}=\\{X:H^i(X)=0\\text{ for }i>0\\}$ and $D^{\\geq0}=\\{X:H^i(X)=0\\text{ for }i<0\\}$, using [[prop-cohomology-factors-through-the-derived-category]].",
