n the extension stack calculation. Let $q:\\mathfrak E_{\\mathbf d,\\mathbf e}\\to\\mathfrak M_{\\mathbf d}$ send a sequence to its quotient, $s:\\mathfrak E_{\\mathbf d,\\mathbf e}\\to \\mathfrak M_{\\mathbf e}$ send it to its subrepresentation, and $m:\\mathfrak E_{\\mathbf d,\\mathbf e}\\to\\mathfrak M_{\\mathbf d+\\mathbf e}$ send it to its middle representation. The Hall correspondence is ~~~ tikzcd & \\mathfrak E_{\\mathbf d,\\mathbf e}(Q) \\ar[dl,\"(q,s)\"'] \\ar[dr,\"m\"] & \\\\ \\mathfrak M_{\\mathbf d}(Q)\\times\\mathfrak M_{\\mathbf e}(Q) && \\mathfrak M_{\\mathbf d+\\mathbf e}(Q) ~~~ Its arrows record the ordered quotient, subrepresentation, and middle object of the displayed short exact sequence; the diagram fixes the convolution convention. Define$$H_Q:=\\bigoplus_{\\mathbf d\\in\\mathbb N^{Q_0}} \\mathscr K(\\mathfrak M_{\\mathbf d}(Q)).$$For $\\alpha\\in\\mathscr K(\\mathfrak M_{\\mathbf d})$ and $\\beta\\in\\mathscr K(\\mathfrak M_{\\mathbf e})$, define$$\\alpha*\\beta :=m_!\\big((q,s)^*(\\alpha\\boxtimes\\beta)\\big) \\in\\mathscr K(\\mathfrak M_{\\mathbf d+\\mathbf e}).$$\nThus the first factor is the quotient and the second factor is the\nsubrepresentation, so the sequence is\n$0\\to B\\to E\\to A\\to0$. Each homogeneous product is defined by one\nfinite-type stack correspondence; no completion or finiteness of a sum over\nisomorphism classes is required. This is the stack-function product without\na potential or a vanishing-cycle weight.",
