          "source": "def-intrinsic-quotient-stack-borel-moore-grading",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Assume AC as inherited from [[def-equivariant-borel-moore-homology-and-correspondence-convolution]]. For a separated finite-type complex variety $X$ with an algebraic action of a finite product $G$ of general linear groups, put $g=\\dim_{\\mathbb C}G$. The **intrinsic quotient-stack Borel–Moore grading** of this presentation is\n$$\\mathbb H_i([X/G];\\mathbb Q)=H_{i+2g}^{\\mathrm{BM},G}(X;\\mathbb Q).$$\nThe group on the right has exactly the variety dualizing normalization of the cited supplier, $\\omega_X^G|_X=\\omega_X$. Equivalently, for a sufficiently acyclic free general linear frame space $U$ of dimension $t$, the group is the stable value $H_{i+2t}^{\\mathrm{BM}}(X\\times_GU;\\mathbb Q)$ in each fixed degree. There is no one finite approximation asserted to compute all degrees.\n\nFor representation stacks use $X=\\operatorname{Rep}_Q(\\mathbf d)$ and $G=G_{\\mathbf d}$ from [[def-quiver-representation-stacks-and-exact-sequence-correspondences]]. For an extension or flag presentation $[Y/P]$ with total-dimension group $G$ and block parabolic $P$, use the induced variety $S=G\\times_PY$ and set $\\mathbb H_i([Y/P])=H_{i+2\\dim G}^{\\mathrm{BM},G}(S)$. The induction and frame comparisons for these presentations are proved in [[lem-quiver-parabolic-levi-borel-model-comparisons]]; this formula does not assert presentation independence for arbitrary Artin stacks.\n\nIf $X$ is smooth of dimension $x$, write $D=x-g$. Then $\\mathbb H_i([X/G])=H_G^{2D-i}(X;\\mathbb Q)$. The complex orientation, rational coefficients and the intrinsic shift are part of this convention. No Tate enrichment is included. Rank-zero general linear factors are omitted and the empty product is the trivial group.",
