          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume AC. Let $G=G_{\\mathbf d}$, let $P\\subset G$ be a block upper parabolic associated to a finite ordered dimension-vector decomposition, and let $L$ be its block-diagonal Levi. Let $Y$ be the variety of arrow matrices preserving that block flag. The induced spaces $S=G\\times_PY$ and $T=G\\times_LY$ are separated quasi-projective finite-type complex varieties, with quotient equivalences $[S/G]\\simeq[Y/P]$ and $[T/G]\\simeq[Y/L]$. With the intrinsic grading of [[def-intrinsic-quotient-stack-borel-moore-grading]], the latter equivalence gives a canonical degree-preserving comparison\n$$\\mathbb H_*([T/G])\\cong\\mathbb H_*([Y/L]).$$\nIt is natural for proper and smooth maps of these induced presentations, compatible with external products, and its comparisons on common product frame models satisfy the cocycle. All assertions include zero block ranks and empty products.",
