          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume AC and use the intrinsic rational Borel–Moore grading of [[def-intrinsic-quotient-stack-borel-moore-grading]]. For any finite quiver over $\\mathbb C$, the representation, extension and finite block-flag stacks admit the following operations: representable proper invariant-flag-forgetting maps have degree-zero proper pushforward; diagonal-block-forgetting maps have smooth pullback of degree twice their relative stack dimension. For the exact-sequence map $q$ this degree is $2(e-u)=-2\\chi_Q(\\mathbf b,\\mathbf a)$, where $e=\\sum_{h:i\\to j}b_i a_j$ and $u=\\sum_i a_i b_i$.\n\nThese operations are independent of the indicated induced-variety and frame presentations, commute with external products, compose with the positive complex orientation, and satisfy proper/smooth base change and Cartesian pasting for the representation/extension/flag diagrams. This includes the two 2-Cartesian squares of three-step quiver flags. Loops, multiple arrows, zero coordinates and the empty quiver are allowed. This statement concerns these particular quotient stacks and maps; it is not a six-functor assertion for arbitrary Artin stacks.",
