      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "derive-1-1",
          "claim": "We first construct the original, sum-skein version over $F=\\mathbb Q(b,t)$. Set $h=(b+b^{-1})/t-1$. Its desired normalization is $L(\\bigcirc)=1$, positive and negative curls have factors $b,b^{-1}$, an extra trivial circle has factor $h$, and its skein equation is $L(D)+L(S_cD)=tC_c(D)$, where $S_c$ switches crossing $c$ and $C_c(D)=L(E_cD)+L(e_cD)$ is the sum over its two smoothings. All constructions are by induction on the crossing number $N$. At a given $N$, first define single-component diagrams; then define diagrams with increasing numbers of components. The crossing-free value on $r\\ge1$ circles is $h^{r-1}$. Throughout the induction the lower-crossing functions satisfy the stated equations and invariance under moves whose diagrams have fewer than $N$ crossings.",
