          "claim": "Extend the field by $i^2=-1$, replace $b$ by $ia$ and $t$ by $-is$, and for a nonempty unoriented diagram $D$ temporarily choose orientations and put $D^\\flat(D)=-i^{-w(D)}(-1)^{c(D)}L(D;ia,-is)$, where $c(D)$ is its number of components. This does not depend on orientations. Reversing one whole component changes writhe by minus twice its mutual crossing-sign sum with all the other components, hence by a multiple of four by [F2]. The phase is unchanged. The same formula is unchanged by moves II and III because writhe and component number are unchanged by these moves and $L$ is invariant. A positive curl multiplies the phase by $i^{-1}$ and $L$ by $ia$, giving factor $a$; a negative curl gives $i(ia)^{-1}=a^{-1}$. Its value on one trivial circle is $1$.",
