      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "derive-1-1",
          "claim": "Work first over $\\Lambda_0$ and write $s=-z_0$, so $s(\\delta-1)=\\lambda-\\lambda^{-1}$, where $z_0$ denotes the skein variable called $z_0$ in the statement. The coefficient ring is the domain $A$ of [F3], under $a=\\lambda,s=-z_0,d=\\delta$; the coefficient injection and its factorization arguments were proved in that supplier. The scalar evaluation of [[lem-framed-kauffman-link-evaluation]], with $a=\\lambda$, $s=-z_0$ and $d=\\delta$, identifies the closed-diagram skein module with $\\Lambda_0$. Its positive crossing is the usual positive braid crossing, with identity smoothing first. A positive braid closed as a two-strand braid gives a positive self-curl with factor $\\lambda$; if the same crossing is followed by a cup-cap, the cup forces opposite strand directions, giving a negative self-curl with factor $\\lambda^{-1}$. Thus the helper's framing rules give exactly $G_iE_i=\\lambda^{-1}E_i$ and the displayed source convention.",
          "step": "1.1",
