        },
        {
          "id": "derive-3-1",
          "claim": "For a fixed connector, draw simple arcs in separate height layers ordered by their initial endpoints and join them to the fixed boundary intervals. This gives a descending, loop-free, self-crossing-free representative $T_c$. Any two such representatives can be put in those same layers: each earlier strand is over every later strand, so changing its height introduces no intersection. Within its layer, a simple arc with specified endpoints in a disk deforms to any other such arc, while other arcs are in different layers. Its framing has no self-curl. These deformations give framed isotopy, equivalently regular isotopy of the diagrams. Thus the class $T_c$ is unique. Step 2.1 proves that these classes span.",
