        {
          "id": "derive-5-1",
          "claim": "The tangle quotient over any $\\Lambda_0$-algebra $S$ is the base change of its universal quotient. Indeed it is a cokernel of the map from the free module on all defining regular-isotopy, skein, curl and loop relations to the free module on all diagrams, and [F4] says tensor product preserves this cokernel. Thus $KT_n(S)=KT_n(\\Lambda_0)\\otimes_{\\Lambda_0}S$ and the classes $T_c$ form an $S$-basis. The same base-change argument applies to the generators-and-relations presentation of BMW. It suffices to prove the universal BMW-to-tangle map injective. In the rest of the proof write $W_j$ for the universal BMW algebra, with $g_i-g_i^{-1}=s(1-e_i)$, $g_ie_i=\\lambda^{-1}e_i$, $e_ig_{i\\pm1}e_i=\\lambda e_i$, and write $\\phi(g_i)=G_i$, $\\phi(e_i)=E_i$. The tangle generators obey these relations: inverse crossings cancel by II, three crossings give III, disjoint disks commute, a cup and cap satisfy the snake move, and the remaining cup slides and curls give the mixed and untwisting relations. This defines $\\phi$.",
