        {
          "id": "derive-7-2",
          "claim": "Let $\\alpha$ reverse words and let $S$ shift all indices by one; reflection $r_{2k}$ sends an index $i$ to $2k-i$. These preserve the relations. Moving distant generators and applying braid gives $g_i^{\\pm1}(g_m\\cdots g_1)=(g_m\\cdots g_1)g_{i+1}^{\\pm1}$ for $i<m$, and the analogous cup slide $e_i(g_m\\cdots g_1)=(g_m\\cdots g_1)e_{i+1}$. The latter uses $e_i g_{i+1}g_i=e_ie_{i+1}=g_{i+1}g_ie_{i+1}$ at the only adjacent positions. Reversing words gives the corresponding identities for $g_1\\cdots g_m$. Another useful identity is $g_ig_{i+1}e_ie_{i+2}=g_{i+2}g_{i+1}e_ie_{i+2}$: both equal $e_{i+1}e_ie_{i+2}$ by the defining mixed relations and distant commutation.",
