        {
          "id": "derive-11-1",
          "claim": "For $r=n-2k\\ge0$, let $I_n^{(r)}$ be the two-sided ideal generated by $e_1e_3\\cdots e_{2k-1}$; set $I_n^{(-1)}=I_n^{(-2)}=0$ as required by parity. They give the increasing parity filtration ending at $I_n^{(n)}=W_n$. The recursion for $f_k$ expresses it as an invertible braid on each side of $e_1e_3\\cdots e_{2k-1}$, so it generates the same ideal. If $n>2k$, its shift generates the same ideal, since shifting these cups is conjugation by $g_{n-1}\\cdots g_1$ using step 7.2. Therefore step 10.1 gives $I_{2k}^{(0)}=W_kf_kW_k$ and $I_{2k+1}^{(1)}=W_{k+1}S(f_k)W_{k+1}$. The image of $I_n^{(r)}$ consists of tangles factoring through $r$ intermediate strands. Descending reduction separately in the two factors expresses them using representatives whose connectors have at most $r$ through pairs.",
