          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $F$ be a field, $\\delta\\in F$, and $n\\ge0$. Put $D_{n,t}=W_{n,t}(F,\\delta)/\\operatorname{rad}(\\phi_{n,t})$ for each allowed $t$. Then the nonzero $D_{n,t}$ are absolutely simple and form a complete set of pairwise nonisomorphic simple right $\\mathrm{TL}_n(F,\\delta)$-modules. Moreover, $D_{n,t}\\ne0$ exactly when $\\phi_{n,t}$ is not identically zero; in that case $\\operatorname{rad}(\\phi_{n,t})$ is the unique maximal proper submodule and $D_{n,t}$ is the simple head of $W_{n,t}$. If $\\phi_{n,t}$ is identically zero, then $D_{n,t}=0$, but no conclusion about the actual head of $W_{n,t}$ follows.",
