          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "thm-temperley-lieb-diagram-generators-span",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For every $n\\ge0$, each basis diagram in $\\mathcal D(n,n)$ is a finite product of the elementary diagrams $d_1,\\ldots,d_{n-1}$ from [[def-temperley-lieb-diagram-category]]. The product can be chosen so that no intermediate stack creates a closed cycle. Therefore the set of diagrams lies in the unital subalgebra of $\\mathrm{TL}_n(R,\\delta)$ generated by these diagrams.",
