          "source": "lem-temperley-lieb-link-state-restriction-filtration",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $R$ be a commutative ring with unit, $\\delta\\in R$, $n\\ge1$, and let $t$ be allowed for $W_{n,t}(R,\\delta)$. Include $\\mathrm{TL}_{n-1}(R,\\delta)$ into $\\mathrm{TL}_n(R,\\delta)$ by adding a rightmost vertical strand, and restrict the right action along this inclusion. Set $W_{m,s}=0$ when $s<0$, $s>m$, or $m-s$ is odd. Then there is a short exact sequence of right $\\mathrm{TL}_{n-1}(R,\\delta)$-modules\n\n$$0\\longrightarrow W_{n-1,t-1}\\longrightarrow \\operatorname{Res}^{TL_n}_{TL_{n-1}}W_{n,t}\\longrightarrow W_{n-1,t+1}\\longrightarrow0.$$\n\nThe sequence gives a two-step filtration; it is not asserted to split.",
