          "id": "derivation-2.1",
          "step": "2.1",
          "claim": "The contragredient action $(x\\varphi)(u)=\\varphi(S(x)u)$ defines $\\nabla(a)$; its weights are the negatives of the original weights and its toral character at weight $m$ is the full character at $m$, by substituting $K^{-1}$ in the generic toral product. Double duality is identified by $K$, since $S^2=\\operatorname{Ad}K$. A map $\\Delta(a)\\to\\nabla(b)$ vanishes for $a>b$ because the generating weight-$a$ vector has nowhere to go. For $a<b$, dualizing gives a map $\\Delta(b)\\to\\nabla(a)$, also zero. For $a=b$, step 1.1 maps onto the one-dimensional highest line of $\\nabla(a)$, and every map is determined by that line. This proves the Hom formula.",
