          "claim": "By [F1], the genuine full-algebra intertwiners $w,b$ satisfy both snakes, $b(w)=-\\delta$ and $KB^t=-B$ for their bilinear form. Thus the self-duality sign is $-1$, independently of rescaling. Put $e=wb$ and $U=-e=\\delta P_0$. The snakes give $U_i^2=\\delta U_i$, $U_iU_{i+1}U_i=U_i$ and distant commutation, so they give every $\\rho_n$. The two channels and their twists/crossings are exactly [F1]. In particular $T=qU-1=-s c^{-1}$, so $q^2$ belongs to the trivial channel, not to the highest-weight-$2$ channel.",
