          "claim": "The rigid tensor functor from $\\mathrm{TL}(-\\delta)$ sends cup to $w$, cap to $b$, and $e_i$ to $w_ib_i$. The two snakes and negative loop verify its defining matching relations. The algebra identification $U_i\\mapsto-e_i$ preserves the JW projectors: the recursion quantum integers for loop $-\\delta$ are $(-1)^{j-1}[j]$, and these signs cancel against the generator sign in each recursive correction. Thus the evaluated projector $p_a$ is annihilated by the matrices $U_i$. For $a\\le\\ell-1$, their common kernel in each weight space is one-dimensional: $U_i$ imposes that the coefficient of $-+$ is $q$ times that of $+-$, so adjacent swaps determine every coefficient from one word. The vectors $F^{(j)}v_+^{\\otimes a}$, $0\\le j\\le a$, belong to this kernel and are nonzero: the divided coproduct has one Laurent-monomial coefficient for every specified subset of $j$ changed positions. The projector acts as identity on its common kernel, since its nonidentity generator words kill that kernel. Its image is therefore precisely this $(a+1)$-dimensional highest-weight string, equal to $\\Delta(a)$ by [F4]. In particular $p_{\\ell-1}$ has a nonzero image of zero pivotal dimension, and cannot lie in the kernel of the unreduced map.",
