          "source": "lem-temperley-lieb-quantum-binomial-digit-criterion",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For $0\\le k\\le n$, let $G_{n,k}(Q)$ be the polynomial $\\sum_w Q^{\\operatorname{inv}(w)}$, summed over binary words with $k$ ones and $n-k$ zeros, where $\\operatorname{inv}(w)$ counts pairs with a one to the left of a zero. There is a unique polynomial $B_{n,k}(T)\\in\\mathbb Z[T]$ such that\n\n$$B_{n,k}(q+q^{-1})=q^{-k(n-k)}G_{n,k}(q^2).$$\n\nFor a formal indeterminate $q$, write $[r]_q=[r]_{q+q^{-1}}$ and $[m]!_q=\\prod_{r=1}^m[r]_q$, with $[0]!_q=1$. Then $B_{n,k}(q+q^{-1})$ agrees as a rational-function identity with $[n]!_q/([k]!_q[n-k]!_q)$; its value at a specialized loop parameter is the polynomial value, without division by vanishing factorials.\n\nFor a field $K$, $\\delta\\in K$, recurrence quantum characteristic $\\ell$, and $p=\\operatorname{char}K$, every $B_{n,k}(\\delta)$ for $0\\le k\\le n$ is nonzero exactly as follows: if $\\ell=\\infty$, at every finite $n$; if $\\ell<\\infty$ and $p>0$, when $n<\\ell$ or $n=a\\ell p^{i-1}-1$ with $i\\ge1$ and $1\\le a<p$; if $\\ell<\\infty$ and $p=0$, when $n<\\ell$ or $n=a\\ell-1$ for a positive integer $a$.",
