          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "The hook quotient is a polynomial by induction on its forest. Removing the root of a tree cancels its factor $[|F|]_T$, leaving the quotient for its subforest. For a disjoint union of forests of sizes $u,v$, the quotient is $B_{u+v,u}(T)$ times their two quotients, a polynomial by [F2]. The empty forest has weight $1$. For a chain, numerator and denominator cancel completely, so its weight is $1$. All further calculations may therefore be proved in $\\mathbb Q(T)$ and then interpreted as identities in $\\mathbb Z[T]$, before making any field specialization.",
