          "claim": "We first use loop value $-T$. Consider matchings with a fixed finite number $d$ of cups on a half-infinite ordered row, with all sufficiently far-left sites propagating. A diagram is encoded by the $d$ right cup endpoints, numbered from the right starting at $1$: scanning from right to left, a listed site opens a cup and the next unpaired unlisted site closes the most recent cup; unlisted sites with no open cup propagate. Thus every $d$-element subset of the positive integers encodes exactly one matching. Hook weights are unchanged by adding more leftmost propagating strands, because bending one more such strand adds a root above the entire old forest and cancels its new numerator factor. We may consequently form the formal series $V_d$ of these matchings with their hook weights. Every fixed output coefficient after a local generator or cup attachment involves finitely many terms: only its finitely many cups and the nearest exposed propagating strand can be reconnected. All operations below are defined coefficient by coefficient.",
