          "quote": "Fix a finite-dimensional complex semisimple Lie algebra $\\mathfrak g$, a Cartan subalgebra $\\mathfrak h$, and a positive Borel $\\mathfrak b=\\mathfrak h\\oplus\\mathfrak n^+$. Let $\\{\\alpha_i\\}_{i\\in I}$ be the simple roots of the chosen positive system and write $Q^+=\\sum_{i\\in I}\\mathbb Z_{\\geq0}\\alpha_i$ and $\\mu\\leq\\lambda$ when $\\lambda-\\mu\\in Q^+$. Let $W$ be the Weyl group of [[def-root-reflections-and-the-weyl-group-action]] and let $\\rho$ be the Weyl vector of [[def-weyl-vector-rho-for-a-chosen-positive-system]]; for $w\\in W$ set $w\\cdot\\lambda=w(\\lambda+\\rho)-\\rho$.\n\nThe **BGG category $\\mathcal O$** is the full subcategory of left $U(\\mathfrak g)$-modules $M$ satisfying all three conditions: $M$ is finitely generated; $M=\\bigoplus_{\\mu\\in\\mathfrak h^*}M_\\mu$ where $M_\\mu=\\{v:hv=\\mu(h)v\\text{ for all }h\\in\\mathfrak h\\}$; and $U(\\mathfrak n^+)v$ is finite dimensional for each $v\\in M$. Its morphisms are all $\\mathfrak g$-linear maps. The zero module is included, generated by the empty set. The enveloping and triangular conventions are those of [[thm-pbw-ordered-monomial-basis-for-the-enveloping-algebra]] and [[thm-triangular-decomposition-from-a-chosen-positive-root-system]].",
