          "quote": "Work over the field $\\mathbb C$ and fix an integer $d\\ge 0$\n([[def-algebra-over-a-commutative-ring]], [[def-commutative-ring]]). Let\n$\\mathcal F_d$ be the free associative unital $\\mathbb C$-algebra on the\n$d+\\max(d-1,0)$ symbols $x_1,\\dots,x_d,s_1,\\dots,s_{d-1}$ (for $d=0$ there is only\nthe unit; for $d=1$ only $x_1$), with its word basis and universal property\n([[lem-hh-free-associative-ring-and-relations-descent]]), and let\n$I_d\\mathrel{\\trianglelefteq}\\mathcal F_d$ be the two-sided ideal\n([[def-left-right-and-two-sided-ideal]], [[def-generated-and-principal-ideals]])\ngenerated by the following elements:\n\n- $x_ix_j-x_jx_i$ for all $1\\le i,j\\le d$;\n- $s_i^2-1$ for $1\\le i\\le d-1$;\n- $s_is_{i+1}s_i-s_{i+1}s_is_{i+1}$ for $1\\le i\\le d-2$;\n- $s_is_j-s_js_i$ for $1\\le i,j\\le d-1$ with $|i-j|>1$;\n- $s_ix_j-x_js_i$ for $j\\notin\\{i,i+1\\}$, $s_ix_{i+1}-x_is_i-1$, and\n  $x_{i+1}s_i-s_ix_i-1$, for $1\\le i\\le d-1$ and $1\\le j\\le d$.\n\nThe **degenerate affine Hecke algebra** is the quotient $\\mathbb C$-algebra\n$$H_d:=\\mathcal F_d/I_d$$\nwith unit element written $1$ ([[thm-quotient-ring-laws]]). We keep the symbols\n$x_1,\\dots,x_d,s_1,\\dots,s_{d-1}$ for their images, and for $w\\in S_d$ we write\n$w$ for the image in $H_d$ of any word in the $s_i$ representing $w$; this is\nindependent of the chosen word once the basis theorem below is proved. For\n$d\\ge1$ and $a\\in\\mathbb C$, the notation $H_d/(x_1-a)$ means the quotient by the two-sided\nideal generated by $x_1-a$.\n\nThe verification below establishes exactly the structure of $H_d$ used\nthroughout this page: the ordered monomials\n$$x_1^{r_1}\\cdots x_d^{r_d}w,\\qquad r_1,\\dots,r_d\\ge0,\\ w\\in S_d,$$\nform a $\\mathbb C$-basis, so that\n$H_d\\cong\\mathbb C[x_1,\\dots,x_d]\\otimes_{\\mathbb C}\\mathbb C[S_d]$ as a vector\nspace with polynomial and group-algebra subalgebras\n([[def-polynomial-ring-on-a-family-of-indeterminates]], [[def-group-ring]]);\n$H_0=\\mathbb C$ and $H_1=\\mathbb C[x_1]$; for $d\\ge1$ and every $a$ there is a unique\nalgebra isomorphism\n$$H_d/(x_1-a)\\cong\\mathbb C[S_d],\\qquad x_j\\longmapsto a+\\sum_{k<j}(k\\ j),\\qquad s_i\\longmapsto(i\\ i+1);$$\nand total polynomial degree is an algebra filtration whose associated graded is\nthe semidirect product $\\mathbb C[x_1,\\dots,x_d]\\rtimes\\mathbb C[S_d]$ in which\n$s_i$ acts by swapping $x_i$ and $x_{i+1}$. For $d\\ge2$, the cross relation is\ninhomogeneous, so it does not turn $H_d$ into a graded algebra with\n$\\deg x_i=1$ and $\\deg s_i=0$. For $d=0$ the algebra $\\mathbb C$ has its\ndegree-zero grading, and for $d=1$ the algebra $\\mathbb C[x_1]$ has its\nnatural polynomial grading.",
