          "source": "def-cyclotomic-klr-quotient-at-a-dominant-weight",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Fix a symmetrizable Cartan datum with finite color set $I$ and no imaginary\nsimple roots, a KLR datum $Q=(Q_{ij})_{i\\ne j}$ satisfying (Q1)-(Q4), and a\nfield $k$ placed in degree zero\n([[def-quiver-hecke-klr-algebra-for-a-symmetrizable-cartan-datum]],\n[[def-symmetrizable-cartan-datum-for-a-quantum-group]]); let\n$R=\\bigoplus_{\\beta\\in Q_+}R(\\beta)$ be the resulting graded KLR algebra, with\nits idempotents $e(\\nu)$, dots $x_a$, crossings $\\tau_a$ and degrees\n$\\deg x_a=2d_{\\nu_a}$, $\\deg\\tau_a=-b_{\\nu_a\\nu_{a+1}}$\n([[def-klr-grading-and-diagrammatic-composition]]). Let $\\Lambda$ be a\ndominant integral weight and put $\\lambda_i:=\\langle h_i,\\Lambda\\rangle\\ge0$\n([[def-kac-moody-integral-and-dominant-integral-weights]]).\n\n**Cyclotomic data.** For every color $i$ choose a monic polynomial\n$a_i(u)\\in k[u]$ of degree exactly $\\lambda_i$\n([[def-polynomial-ring-over-a-commutative-ring]]); the standard choice made\nbelow is $a_i(u)=u^{\\lambda_i}$. For $n\\ge1$ write\n$$a(x_s)=\\sum_{\\nu\\in I^n}a_{\\nu_s}(x_s)e(\\nu)\\qquad(1\\le s\\le n),$$\nthe element of $R_n(Q)$ that acts on the $\\nu$-component by the monic\npolynomial $a_{\\nu_s}$ in the dot at position $s$.\n\n**The cyclotomic quotient.** For $\\beta\\in Q_+$ define $J_a(\\beta)$ to be the\ntwo-sided ideal of $R(\\beta)$ generated by the first-strand elements\n$a_{\\nu_1}(x_1)e(\\nu)$, $\\nu\\in I^\\beta$; equivalently\n$$J_a(\\beta)=\\sum_{\\nu\\in I^\\beta}R(\\beta)\\,a_{\\nu_1}(x_1)e(\\nu)\\,R(\\beta),$$\nand put\n$$R_a^\\Lambda(\\beta):=R(\\beta)/J_a(\\beta),\\qquad R_a^\\Lambda(0):=k .$$\nThe **cyclotomic KLR algebra** is the direct sum\n$R_a^\\Lambda:=\\bigoplus_{\\beta\\in Q_+}R_a^\\Lambda(\\beta)$; it carries the\nlocal units $e(\\beta)=\\sum_{\\nu\\in I^\\beta}e(\\nu)$, which act as the identity\non $R_a^\\Lambda(\\beta)$ and annihilate the other summands, and it is a\n$k$-algebra with these orthogonal idempotents.\n\n**Standard choice and grading.** The STANDARD choice $a_i(u)=u^{\\lambda_i}$ is\nused throughout the graded categorification, duality-normalization and based\nstatements below; for it we write $R^\\Lambda:=R^\\Lambda_a$. Under the standard\nchoice each individual first-strand generator\n$x_1^{\\lambda_{\\nu_1}}e(\\nu)$ is homogeneous of degree\n$2d_{\\nu_1}\\lambda_{\\nu_1}$ in the grading of\n[[def-klr-grading-and-diagrammatic-composition]], so the ideal $J_a(\\beta)$\nand the quotient $R^\\Lambda(\\beta)$ are graded, and $R^\\Lambda$ is a\n$\\mathbb Z$-graded algebra with local units. The sum $a(x_1)$ itself need not\nhave one common degree across different colors, and no single degree is\nassigned to it.\n\n**Boundary of the definition.** Arbitrary monic polynomials with lower\ncoefficients in degree-zero $k$ give an UNGRADED deformation $R_a^\\Lambda$;\nnilpotent dots, homogeneous trace degree and the highest-weight graded $K_0$\nidentification are not asserted for that branch, and the ungraded branch is\nused only where a statement explicitly says so. Finite dimension, finite root\nstrings, ordinary projectivity and symmetry of the standard quotient have the\nseparately stated monic conclusions below. The cyclotomic relation is imposed\non the FIRST strand, and cyclotomic induction appends strands on the RIGHT\n([[def-cyclotomic-klr-induction-and-restriction-functors]]); this convention\nfixes the side on which the quotient map acts throughout the page.\n\nThis definition uses no choice.",
