          "quote": "Let $Q$ be a KLR datum as in [[def-quiver-hecke-klr-algebra-for-a-symmetrizable-cartan-datum]]. Assign degrees $\\deg e(\\nu):=0$, $\\deg(x_ae(\\nu)):=(\\alpha_{\\nu_a}\\mid\\alpha_{\\nu_a})=2d_{\\nu_a}$ and $\\deg(\\tau_ae(\\nu)):=-(\\alpha_{\\nu_a}\\mid\\alpha_{\\nu_{a+1}})=-b_{\\nu_a\\nu_{a+1}}$ in the presentation; then every relation (1)-(7) is homogeneous (## Verification), so $R_n(Q)=\\bigoplus_{m\\in\\mathbb Z}R_n(Q)_m$ is a $\\mathbb Z$-graded unital associative $k$-algebra with $R_n(Q)_m=\\bigoplus_{\\nu,\\eta\\in I^n}e(\\nu)R_n(Q)_me(\\eta)$, and each $R(\\beta)=\\bigoplus_mR(\\beta)_m$ is a graded subalgebra ([[def-graded-ring-module-bimodule-and-internal-shift]]). The global sums $x_a=\\sum_\\nu x_ae(\\nu)$ and $\\tau_a=\\sum_\\nu\\tau_ae(\\nu)$ need not be homogeneous; displayed generator degrees always refer to their word components. Equivalently, the weight refinement by $Q_+$ is available: the idempotent $e(\\nu)$ carries weight $\\sum_a\\alpha_{\\nu_a}$, and $x_a$ and $\\tau_a$ are weight-preserving operators of the displayed scalar degrees.\n\n**Diagram dictionary.** Read a planar diagram bottom to top. A local dot on strand $a$ is $x_a$, a crossing of strands $a,a+1$ is $\\tau_a$, the identity is the collection of straight diagrams $e(\\nu)$, and vertical concatenation of diagrams with matching bottom labels $\\nu$ and top labels $s_{a_r}\\cdots s_{a_1}\\nu$ is the algebra product: in $ab$ the diagram for $b$ is placed below the diagram for $a$, matching operator composition. Isotopies of the plane that do not change the combinatorial type act as the identity, and the local relations (2.3)-(2.8) of Khovanov–Lauda I (quadratic relation, dot-sliding over a crossing, and the braid relation) in the simply-laced Khovanov–Lauda parameter specialization are relations (4), (6) and (7); for general $Q$ the local diagram relations are defined by the full presentation of [[def-quiver-hecke-klr-algebra-for-a-symmetrizable-cartan-datum]]. 