          "quote": "Every $W$-orbit in $E$ has exactly one point in $\\overline{\\mathcal C}$. For $\\eta\\in\\overline{\\mathcal C}$, its stabilizer is generated by those simple reflections $s_i$ with $(\\eta,\\alpha_i)=0$. The group acts simply transitively on open chambers. There is a unique longest element $w_0$, characterized by $w_0\\Phi^+=\\Phi^-$; it has length $|\\Phi^+|$ and satisfies $w_0^2=1$. In particular every weight orbit has a unique dominant weight. These assertions include rank zero and singular wall points, without AC.",
