          "source": "def-pa36-flag-tdo-and-module",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice as inherited from the published group and sheaf\nsuppliers. Let $G$ be a connected simply connected complex semisimple affine\nalgebraic group, $B\\supseteq T$ a Borel subgroup and maximal torus,\n$X=G/B$, $\\mathfrak g=\\operatorname{Lie}G$,\n$\\mathfrak h=\\operatorname{Lie}T$, and $\\Phi^+$ the positive roots selected by\n$B$. Write $\\rho=\\frac12\\sum_{\\alpha\\in\\Phi^+}\\alpha$. All schemes are over\n$\\mathbb C$. For an integral weight $\\eta$, $\\mathcal O_X(\\eta)$ denotes the\n$G$-equivariant line bundle $G\\times^B\\mathbb C_\\eta$ with fiber character\n$\\eta$ at $eB$.\n\nThe infinitesimal $G$-action gives an anchor\n$$a_X:\\mathcal L_X:=\\mathcal O_X\\otimes_{\\mathbb C}\\mathfrak g\\longrightarrow T_X,\\qquad f\\otimes x\\longmapsto f x_X.$$\nGive $\\mathcal L_X$ the action-algebroid bracket\n$$[f\\otimes x,g\\otimes y]=fg\\otimes[x,y]+f x_X(g)\\otimes y-g y_X(f)\\otimes x.$$\nIts kernel $\\mathfrak b_X=\\ker a_X$ is the isotropy Lie-algebra bundle; at\n$gB$ its fiber is $\\operatorname{Ad}(g)\\mathfrak b$.\n\nFor any $\\kappa\\in\\mathfrak h^*$, the character $\\kappa+\\rho$ of\n$\\mathfrak b$ (zero on $\\mathfrak n^+$) transports to an\n$\\mathcal O_X$-linear map $\\chi^X_{\\kappa+\\rho}:\\mathfrak b_X\\to\\mathcal O_X$.\nThe transport is independent of the representative $g$ of $gB$, since a\ncharacter is invariant under the adjoint action of $B$. The action-algebroid\nenveloping sheaf $\\mathcal U_X(\\mathfrak g)$ is generated by $\\mathcal O_X$\nand $\\mathcal L_X$ with the displayed bracket and\n$$[x,f]=x_X(f),\\qquad x\\in\\mathcal L_X,\\ f\\in\\mathcal O_X.$$\nDefine the sheaf of twisted differential operators\n$$\\mathcal D_\\kappa:=\\mathcal U_X(\\mathfrak g)/\\bigl(\\xi-\\chi^X_{\\kappa+\\rho}(\\xi):\\xi\\in\\mathfrak b_X\\bigr).$$\nIts order filtration assigns order zero to $\\mathcal O_X$ and order at most\none to the image of $\\mathcal L_X$. A TDO means a filtered\n$\\mathcal O_X$-ring with $F_0=\\mathcal O_X$, associated graded\n$\\operatorname{Sym}_{\\mathcal O_X}T_X$, and first-order commutator equal to\nthe anchor; the well-definedness and PBW properties of $\\mathcal D_\\kappa$\nare proved in [[lem-pa36-flag-tdo-pbw-and-twist]]. A left\n$\\mathcal D_\\kappa$-module below is required to be quasi-coherent as an\n$\\mathcal O_X$-module.\n\nFor $z\\in Z(U(\\mathfrak g))$, let $\\operatorname{pr}(z)\\in U(\\mathfrak h)$ be\nthe Harish–Chandra projection along the chosen triangular decomposition, and\nput\n$$\\chi_\\kappa(z)=\\operatorname{pr}(z)(\\kappa-\\rho).$$\nThis is the shifted central character: the Harish–Chandra isomorphism makes it\n$W$-invariant in $\\kappa$. Define\n$$A_\\kappa=U(\\mathfrak g)/U(\\mathfrak g)\\ker\\chi_\\kappa.$$\nThe regularity convention is **antidominant** when\n$\\langle\\kappa,\\alpha^\\vee\\rangle\\notin\\mathbb Z_{>0}$ for each positive\nroot $\\alpha$, and **regular** when\n$\\langle\\kappa,\\alpha^\\vee\\rangle\\ne0$ for every root. For complex weights,\n$\\mathbb Z_{>0}$ means the positive real integers; no order on arbitrary\ncomplex numbers is used.",
