          "source": "lem-pa36-complex-weight-central-character-separation",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $E$ be the real span of a finite reduced crystallographic root system\n$\\Phi$, with chosen positive roots $\\Phi^+$, simple roots\n$\\Delta=\\{\\alpha_1,\\ldots,\\alpha_r\\}$, Weyl group $W$ and root lattice\n$Q=\\sum_i\\mathbb Z\\alpha_i$. Extend the pairing complex linearly to\n$E_\\mathbb C$. For $\\kappa\\in E_\\mathbb C$, call $\\kappa$ antidominant if\n$\\langle\\kappa,\\alpha^\\vee\\rangle\\notin\\mathbb Z_{>0}$ for every\n$\\alpha\\in\\Phi^+$, and regular if\n$\\langle\\kappa,\\alpha^\\vee\\rangle\\ne0$ for every root. Then\n$$\\kappa-w\\kappa\\notin Q_+\\setminus\\{0\\}\\qquad(w\\in W)$$\nfor antidominant $\\kappa$, and\n$$\\kappa-w\\kappa\\notin Q_+\\qquad(w\\ne1)$$\nwhen $\\kappa$ is also regular. Here\n$Q_+=\\sum_i\\mathbb Z_{\\ge0}\\alpha_i$.",
          "uses": [
            "3.1",
            "3.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F4",
          "source": "thm-pa36-global-twisted-differential-operators",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the setup of [[def-pa36-flag-tdo-and-module]] and the Axiom of\nChoice. For every complex $\\kappa$, the infinitesimal action on\n$\\mathcal D_\\kappa$ induces a filtered algebra isomorphism\n$$A_\\kappa=U(\\mathfrak g)/U(\\mathfrak g)\\ker\\chi_\\kappa \\xrightarrow{\\sim}\\Gamma(X,\\mathcal D_\\kappa),$$\nwhere $\\chi_\\kappa(z)=\\operatorname{pr}(z)(\\kappa-\\rho)$. No dominance,\nregularity, or integrality condition is imposed on $\\kappa$.",
