        {
          "fact": "F5",
          "source": "thm-chinese-remainder-theorem-for-comaximal-ideals",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $R$ be a commutative ring and let $I_1,\\ldots,I_r$ be pairwise comaximal ideals, where $r\\ge1$. Then the canonical map\n$$ R\\longrightarrow \\prod_{i=1}^r R/I_i,\\qquad x\\longmapsto(x+I_1,\\ldots,x+I_r) $$\nis surjective, its kernel is $\\bigcap_{i=1}^r I_i$, and\n$$ \\bigcap_{i=1}^r I_i=\\prod_{i=1}^r I_i. $$\nEquivalently,\n$$ R/\\prod_{i=1}^r I_i\\cong\\prod_{i=1}^r R/I_i. $$",
          "uses": [
            "3.3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F6",
          "source": "thm-harish-chandra-isomorphism-for-the-center",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice. Let $\\mathfrak g$ be a finite-dimensional complex\nsemisimple Lie algebra, let $\\mathfrak h$ be any Cartan subalgebra in the\nnilpotent self-normalizing sense, and fix a positive root system with Weyl\ngroup $W$ and half-sum $\\rho$ of its positive roots. The shifted Harish-Chandra map\n\n$$ \\operatorname{HC}_\\rho\\colon Z(U(\\mathfrak g))\\to S(\\mathfrak h)^W, \\qquad \\operatorname{HC}_\\rho(z)(\\lambda)=\\operatorname{pr}(z)(\\lambda-\\rho), $$\n\nis an algebra isomorphism.",
