          "id": "d1_1",
          "claim": "Form the finite $G$-equivariant bundle $E(V_\\eta)=G\\times^B V_\\eta$. The map $[g,v]\\mapsto(gB,gv)$ identifies it with the trivial bundle $X\\times V_\\eta$ with its diagonal $G$-action. Choose a weight basis in each weight space and order the weights with higher weights first. Positive root operators raise weights, so the resulting complete filtration is $B$-stable and its successive quotient lines have characters $\\eta_j$ as in [F2]. Association to $G\\to X$ is exact on this finite filtration: on every torsor chart it is tensoring a sequence of complex vector spaces with $\\mathcal O_X$. Its quotient line bundles are $\\mathcal O_X(\\eta_j)$, with highest line $\\mathcal O_X(\\eta)$. Tensoring this bundle filtration with arbitrary $M$ remains exact, since each quotient is locally free.",
