        {
          "id": "d2_1",
          "claim": "The coevaluation $\\mathcal O_X\\to L_\\eta\\otimes E(V_\\eta)$ is the highest line in this filtration; dually the evaluation $E(V_\\eta)^*\\to L_\\eta$ is the quotient of weight $-\\eta$. These are the duals of evaluation of the globally generated line bundle [F1], so they are respectively injective and surjective, locally split as vector-bundle maps. After tensoring with $M$ they give the maps in the Statement, with the same exact filtration positions. Each associated quotient of the first target is $M\\otimes\\mathcal O_X(-\\eta+\\eta_j)$, with central character $\\chi_{\\kappa-\\eta+\\eta_j}$ by [F4]. The evaluation source has quotients $M\\otimes\\mathcal O_X(-\\eta_j)$ with characters $\\chi_{\\kappa-\\eta_j}$; its target has character $\\chi_{\\kappa-\\eta}$. All these filtrations are preserved by the diagonal $\\mathfrak g$-action because their finite bundle factors are $G$-equivariant.",
          "step": "2.1",
