          "claim": "For the evaluation, if $\\eta_j\\ne\\eta$ had $\\chi_{\\kappa-\\eta_j}=\\chi_{\\kappa-\\eta}$, then $\\kappa-\\eta_j=w(\\kappa-\\eta)$ for some $w$. Rearranging gives $\\kappa-w^{-1}\\kappa=\\eta-w^{-1}\\eta_j\\in Q_+$, since $w^{-1}\\eta_j$ is again a weight of $V_\\eta$. If the right side is nonzero, antidominance [F3] rules it out; if it is zero, regularity [F3] forces $w=1$ and hence $\\eta_j=\\eta$, a contradiction. Thus its target is the sole quotient with the distinguished character.",
          "step": "3.2",
