        {
          "id": "d3_3",
          "claim": "For a sheaf of complex vector spaces with a finite filtration of exact central-character quotients, a product of powers of their finitely many maximal ideals in $Z(U(\\mathfrak g))$ annihilates the sheaf. Powers of distinct maximal ideals are comaximal: expand $1=(u+v)^{a+b-1}$ with $u+v=1$, $u$ in the first ideal and $v$ in the second. Thus [F5] gives central polynomial projectors onto the corresponding generalized-character summands. These polynomials act on sections by the diagonal differential $U(\\mathfrak g)$-action, commute with restrictions and with $U(\\mathfrak g)$, and hence are morphisms of sheaves of complex vector spaces. They are natural in $M$. They are generally differential operators rather than $\\mathcal O_X$-linear maps; that stronger linearity is neither asserted nor needed.",
