,C'\\in W_a\\cdot A$ share a facet $F$, its type computed from either alcove is the same. Every alcove in $W_a\\cdot A$ has exactly one facet of each type in $J$. The reflection in the wall of a facet of type $a$ of $g(A)$ is $g\\,s_a\\,g^{-1}$.\n\nThese statements include reducible systems: there is one affine label $0_i$ for each nonempty component, not one global highest-root wall. In dimension zero the statements reduce to the single alcove $\\{0\\}$ and the empty type set. No axiom of choice is used.",
