          "quote": "Let $U_q(\\mathfrak g)$ be the Drinfeld–Jimbo algebra of [[def-drinfeld-jimbo-quantized-enveloping-algebra]] with its root-lattice grading $U_q(\\mathfrak g)=\\bigoplus_{\\beta\\in Q}U_q(\\mathfrak g)[\\beta]$. Define\n\n$$U_q^+:=\\langle E_i\\ :\\ i\\in I\\rangle,\\qquad U_q^-:=\\langle F_i\\ :\\ i\\in I\\rangle,\\qquad U_q^0:=\\langle K_h\\ :\\ h\\in P^{\\vee}\\rangle,$$\n\nthe $\\mathbb Q(q)$-subalgebras generated by the indicated images, and let $Q_+=\\bigoplus_i\\mathbb Z_{\\ge0}\\alpha_i$. Then\n\n$$U_q^\\pm=\\bigoplus_{\\beta\\in Q_+}U_q^\\pm[\\pm\\beta],\\qquad U_q^+[\\beta]:=U_q(\\mathfrak g)[\\beta]\\cap U_q^+,\\quad U_q^-[ -\\beta]:=U_q(\\mathfrak g)[-\\beta]\\cap U_q^-.$$\n\nThe degree-zero component $U_q(\\mathfrak g)[0]$ contains $U_q^0$, and for every $x\\in U_q(\\mathfrak g)[\\beta]$ and $h\\in P^{\\vee}$,\n\n$$K_hxK_h^{-1}=q^{\\beta(h)}x.$$\n\nThus each $K_h\\in U_q^0$ acts by conjugation on the degree-$\\beta$ component as the scalar $q^{\\beta(h)}$. The elements $K_h$ span $U_q^0$ and satisfy $K_hK_{h'}=K_{h+h'}$ with $K_0=1$; hence $U_q^0$ is a quotient of the group algebra $\\mathbb Q(q)[P^{\\vee}]$. The subalgebras $U_q^\\pm$ are spanned by finite monomials in the $E_i$ and $F_i$, respectively. Define the nonnegative and nonpositive product spans by\n\n$$U_q^{\\ge0}:=\\operatorname{span}_{\\mathbb Q(q)}(U_q^0U_q^+),\\qquad U_q^{\\le0}:=\\operatorname{span}_{\\mathbb Q(q)}(U_q^-U_q^0).$$\n\nThis definition asserts no linear independence of these spanning families and no injectivity of the natural maps; those claims belong to [[thm-triangular-decomposition-of-a-quantized-enveloping-algebra]].",
