          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Let $(I,A,D,P,P^{\\vee},q)$ be a symmetrizable Cartan datum for a quantum\ngroup with $a_{ii}=2$ for all $i$\n([[def-symmetrizable-cartan-datum-for-a-quantum-group]]), let\n$U_q(\\mathfrak g)$ be its Drinfeld–Jimbo algebra\n([[def-drinfeld-jimbo-quantized-enveloping-algebra]]) with $q_i=q^{d_i}$ and\n$K_i=K_{d_ih_i}$, and set\n\n$$A:=\\mathbb Z[q,q^{-1}]\\ \\subseteq\\ \\mathbb Q(q),$$\n\nthe image of the Laurent polynomial ring $\\Lambda_1=\\mathbb Z[t]_{S}$ of\n[[def-the-laurent-polynomial-ring]] under the unital ring homomorphism sending\n$t$ to the indeterminate $q$; this homomorphism is injective and $A$ is a\nsubring of $\\mathbb Q(q)$ (Verification, step 1.1). We work over this\ncommutative domain $A$ inside the field $\\mathbb Q(q)$.\n\nFor $i\\in I$, $c\\in\\mathbb Z$ and $t\\ge0$ define the **toral quantum binomial**\n\n$$T_{i,c,t}:=\\begin{bmatrix}K_i;c\\\\ t\\end{bmatrix}:=\\prod_{s=1}^{t}\\frac{K_iq_i^{\\,c-s+1}-K_i^{-1}q_i^{\\,-c+s-1}}{q_i^{\\,s}-q_i^{\\,-s}}\\in U_q(\\mathfrak g),$$\n\nthe empty product being $T_{i,c,0}:=1$. Each factor is defined in\n$U_q(\\mathfrak g)$ because $q_i^{\\,s}-q_i^{\\,-s}\\ne0$ for $s\\ge1$\n([[def-quantum-integers-factorials-and-divided-powers-at-q-i]]), so\n$T_{i,c,t}$ is a polynomial in $K_i^{\\pm1}$ with coefficients in $\\mathbb Q(q)$;\nin particular all $T_{i,c,t}$ commute with the $K_h$ and with one another\n(Verification, step 2.1).\n\nThe **Lusztig divided-power integral form** is the $A$-subalgebra\n\n$$U_A:=\\bigl\\langle E_i^{(r)},\\ F_i^{(r)},\\ K_h^{\\pm1},\\ T_{i,c,t}\\ \\colon\\ i\\in I,\\ r,t\\ge0,\\ c\\in\\mathbb Z,\\ h\\in P^{\\vee}\\bigr\\rangle\\ \\subseteq\\ U_q(\\mathfrak g),$$\n\nwhere $x^{(r)}=x^r/[r]_i!$ are the divided powers of\n[[def-quantum-integers-factorials-and-divided-powers-at-q-i]]. Write $U_A^\\pm$\nfor the $A$-subalgebras generated by the $E_i^{(r)}$ and by the $F_i^{(r)}$,\nand $U_A^0$ for the one generated by the $K_h^{\\pm1}$ and the $T_{i,c,t}$.\n\nThen:\n\n(i) $U_A$ contains $E_i=E_i^{(1)}$, $F_i=F_i^{(1)}$ and all $K_h$;\n\n(ii) $U_A$ is a root-graded $A$-subalgebra of the root-graded\n$\\mathbb Q(q)$-algebra $U_q(\\mathfrak g)$ ([[def-positive-negative-and-toral-quantum-subalgebras]]):\nwith $U_A[\\beta]:=U_A\\cap U_q(\\mathfrak g)[\\beta]$ one has\n$U_A=\\bigoplus_{\\beta\\in Q}U_A[\\beta]$, each $U_A[\\beta]$ is an $A$-submodule,\nand $U_A^\\pm,U_A^0$ are graded in the same way;\n\n(iii) $U_A\\otimes_A\\mathbb Q(q)\\cong U_q(\\mathfrak g)$ canonically, i.e. the\n$\\mathbb Q(q)$-span of $U_A$ is all of $U_q(\\mathfrak g)$.\n\nThe shifted binomials $T_{i,c,t}$ with $c\\ne0$ are included because the\ndivided-power reordering identity of\n[[lem-divided-power-and-toral-quantum-binomial-reordering-identities]] has\ncoefficients $T_{i,2t-a-b,t}$ with a nonconstant index; the specializations at\n$q=1$ of these elements are computed in\n[[lem-q-one-toral-specialization-identifies-the-classical-cartan-generators]],\nand the integral triangular decomposition and the specialization are treated\nonly after this definition.\n\nNo freeness of $U_A$ or of its parts over $A$, no independence of the listed\ngenerators, and no triangularity of the products of the three parts is asserted\nhere. In particular $A$ is not a principal ideal domain (Verification, step\n7.1), so no torsion-free-to-free inference over $A$ is permitted anywhere on\nthis page.",
