      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Work first over $R=\\mathbb C[v,v^{-1},(v-v^{-1})^{-1}]$ with $H_v=(K-K^{-1})/(v-v^{-1})$. Combine adjacent powers of $K$ as elements $K^b$ of the group algebra $R[K,K^{-1}]$, and rewrite $K^bF\\to v^{-2b}FK^b$, $EK^b\\to v^{-2b}K^bE$, and $EF\\to FE+H_v$. Count inversions in the order $F<K<E$, with a second measure equal to the number of $E$ and $F$ symbols. The first two rules decrease the inversion count; the $FE$ term of the third decreases it and its $H_v$ term lowers the second measure. Thus every word reduces after finitely many steps to an $R$-linear combination of the ordered monomials $F^aK^bE^c$. The same rules remain valid after $v=\\zeta$ by [F2].",
