      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "If $\\ell(ws_i)=\\ell(w)+1$, then $S_w(E_i)$ is positive. Prove this by induction on $\\ell(w)$. Choose a right descent $j$ of a nonidentity $w$; necessarily $j\\ne i$. Write $w=w'v$ with $w'$ the minimal right coset representative for $\\{i,j\\}$ and $v$ in that rank-two parabolic. Both $i,j$ are ascents of $w'$. Since $i$ is an ascent and $j$ a descent of $v$, its alternating reduced word has length at most $m_{ij}-1$. The rank-two calculations in [F1] therefore make $S_v(E_i)$ either a simple generator or one of the two neighboring positive polynomials $E_jE_i-qE_iE_j$ and $E_iE_j-qE_jE_i$. Induction makes both $S_{w'}(E_i),S_{w'}(E_j)$ positive, hence also $S_w(E_i)$. Its divided powers belong to $U_A$ by [F1], so [F2] puts them in $U_A^+$. Apply this to every prefix in the chosen reduced word.",
