          "quote": "Under [[def-root-of-unity-weyl-and-dual-weyl-module-families]], $\\Delta_\\zeta(\\lambda)$ is a nonzero finite dimensional integrable type-1 module, cyclic on a highest vector of label $\\lambda$ with one-dimensional highest space. Its formal character is the classical finite Weyl character $\\chi_\\lambda$. It is universal among finite dimensional highest-label modules generated by a vector of label $\\lambda$. It has a unique maximal proper submodule and unique simple head $L_\\zeta(\\lambda)$. The simple heads are pairwise nonisomorphic and exhaust finite dimensional simple type-1 modules. The dual Weyl module has the same character, unique simple socle $L_\\zeta(\\lambda)$, and weights at most $\\lambda$.\n\nThese assertions use the inherited Axiom of Choice. They do not assert root-specialized semisimplicity or that these Weyl modules are simple.",
