          "claim": "If a finite module $V$ has no label strictly greater than $\\lambda$, every surjection $V\\to\\Delta_\\zeta(\\lambda)$ splits: lift its highest vector to a label-$\\lambda$ vector $v\\in V$. All positive divided powers kill $v$ because they would increase its label strictly. The universal property in [F1] extends the highest-vector lift to a module map from $\\Delta_\\zeta(\\lambda)$, and its composite with the surjection fixes the highest generator, hence is the identity. This argument permits labels incomparable with $\\lambda$ in $V$.",
