          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the inherited Axiom of Choice ([[def-axiom-of-choice]]). For the actual root Weyl families of [[def-root-of-unity-weyl-and-dual-weyl-module-families]], Weyl-filtered and dual-Weyl-filtered modules are closed under direct summands. Hence tiltings are closed under direct summands, and each tilting is a finite direct sum of indecomposable tiltings. One has $\\operatorname{Hom}(\\Delta_\\zeta(\\lambda),\\nabla_\\zeta(\\mu))=\\delta_{\\lambda\\mu}\\mathbb C$ and every extension of a Weyl-filtered module by a dual-Weyl-filtered module splits. Every indecomposable tilting has a unique maximal label, of multiplicity one, and two indecomposable tiltings with the same maximal label are isomorphic. These assertions give uniqueness where the objects exist; they make no existence claim for an arbitrary prescribed label.",
