          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Write $\\zeta=\\exp(2\\pi i a/l)$ with $\\gcd(a,l)=1$. There is $b\\equiv a\\pmod l$ with $\\gcd(b,ld)=1$: for every prime dividing $d$ but not $l$ avoid the unique forbidden residue of the multiplier in $b=a+kl$, and apply the finite Chinese remainder theorem; primes dividing $l$ already do not divide $b$. Thus $t=\\exp(2\\pi i b/(ld))$ is a primitive $ld$-th root with $t^d=\\zeta$. Use [F3] with this auxiliary root. Replacing a previously selected $d$-th root by this one does not change the underlying module category or pivot; the ratio of the two Cartan phases is trivial whenever one label belongs to $Q$, hence is a bicharacter of $P/Q$. We use this auxiliary braiding only to construct natural module endomorphisms, with no nondegeneracy claim for either braiding.",
