amental-alcove]] (3).\n\n**(4) Comparison.** The finite root-system types are the standard crystallographic types $A_n,B_n,C_n,D_n,E_6,E_7,E_8,F_4,G_2$ (with the low-rank identifications in [[thm-classification-of-irreducible-reduced-crystallographic-root-systems]]). In that root-system normalization, $W_a=Q^\\vee\\rtimes W$ from [[lem-cg-affine-reflection-identities-and-local-finiteness]] is the standard affine Weyl group. This does not identify it with an untwisted Kac–Moody loop realization, and it does not assert that the extended group $P^\\vee\\rtimes W$ is a Coxeter group with the same simple system. No axiom of choice is used.",
