          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "lem-the-laurent-polynomial-ring-is-noetherian-and-a-unique-factorisation-domain",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "The Laurent polynomial ring $\\Lambda=\\mathbb Z[t^{\\pm1}]$ of\n[[def-the-laurent-polynomial-ring]] is Noetherian, hence every ideal of\n$\\Lambda$ is finitely generated, and $\\Lambda$ is a unique factorisation\ndomain; its units are $\\pm t^k$, $k\\in\\mathbb Z$, and $t$ is prime in $\\mathbb Z[t]$ but becomes a unit in $\\Lambda$.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "2.1",
            "3.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "thm-noetherian-ring-quotients-and-localisations",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $R$ be a Noetherian commutative ring. Then\n\n1. $R/I$ is Noetherian for every ideal $I$ of $R$\n   ([[def-quotient-ring]]), and\n2. $S^{-1}R$ is Noetherian for every multiplicative subset $S\\subseteq R$\n   ([[def-multiplicative-subset-and-localisation]]).\n\nBoth cases include their degenerate instances: $I=R$ makes $R/I$ the zero ring,\nand $0\\in S$ makes $S^{-1}R$ the zero ring, and the zero ring is Noetherian.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "2.1",
            "3.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "cor-polynomial-ring-over-a-field-is-a-pid",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For every field $F$, every ideal of $F[x]$ is generated by one polynomial; equivalently, $F[x]$ is a principal ideal domain.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "2.1",
            "3.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "thm-krull-height-theorem",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice ([[def-axiom-of-choice]]). Let $R$ be a Noetherian commutative ring, let\n$$ I=(x_1,\\ldots,x_n) $$\nbe an ideal generated by $n\\ge1$ elements, and let $\\mathfrak p$ be a prime ideal minimal over $I$. Then $\\operatorname{ht}(\\mathfrak p)\\le n$.",
          "uses": [
            "2.1",
            "3.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "thm-completion-of-a-noetherian-local-ring",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice.\n\nLet $(R,\\mathfrak m)$ be a Noetherian local ring, and let $\\widehat R$ be its\n$\\mathfrak m$-adic completion.\n\n1. $\\widehat R$ is a Noetherian local ring with maximal ideal\n   $\\mathfrak m\\widehat R$.\n2. The residue field is unchanged:\n   $$    \\widehat R/\\mathfrak m\\widehat R \\cong R/\\mathfrak m.    $$\n3. The completion map $R \\to \\widehat R$ is faithfully flat.",
          "uses": [
            "4.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "thm-completion-preserves-regular-local-rings",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice ([[def-axiom-of-choice]]). A nonzero Noetherian local ring $R$ is regular if and only if its maximal-adic completion $\\widehat R$ is regular.",
          "uses": [
            "4.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "thm-regular-local-rings-are-domains-and-cohen-macaulay",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice ([[def-axiom-of-choice]]). A regular local ring $R$ of dimension $d$ is a domain and Cohen–Macaulay. For every regular system $(x_1,\\ldots,x_d)$, the tuple is $R$-regular and $R/(x_1,\\ldots,x_c)$ is regular local of dimension $d-c$ for all $0\\le c\\le d$.",
          "uses": [
            "4.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F4",
          "source": "thm-nakayama-lemma",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice.\n\nLet $R$ be a commutative ring, let $I \\trianglelefteq R$ satisfy $I \\subseteq J(R)$, and let $M$ be a finitely generated left $R$-module. If $IM=M$, then $M=0$.",
          "uses": [
            "5.1",
