          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $(S,m)$ be a finite Coxeter matrix; let $W$ and $\\ell$ be the presented group and its length and let $\\sigma:W\\to\\mathrm{GL}_K(E)$ be the geometric representation, as in [[def-hh-coxeter-matrix-word-group-and-length]], [[def-hh-geometric-coxeter-representation-and-roots]] and [[lem-hh-dihedral-root-recurrence-and-root-sign]], with reflection set $T$ and sign-change sets $\\Phi(w)$ as in that lemma. Parts (1) and (2) hold for every finite $S$, including the empty and singleton cases; a distinct pair is required only for part (3).\n\n1. **Braid moves.** Call two words in $S$ *braid-equivalent* when one is obtained from the other by finitely many replacements of an alternating subword $s\\,t\\,s\\,t\\cdots$ of length $m(s,t)<\\infty$ by the alternating word $t\\,s\\,t\\,s\\cdots$ of the same length. Then any two reduced expressions of the same element $w\\in W$ are braid-equivalent.\n2. **M-reducedness.** A word is reduced if and only if no sequence of braid moves followed by cancellation of a consecutive equal pair can shorten it (M-reduced in the sense of [Davis, Definition 3.4.1]).\n3. **Singleton detection in dihedral subgroups.** Fix distinct $s,t\\in S$ and put $m:=m(s,t)$. The subgroup $\\langle s,t\\rangle\\le W$ is dihedral of order $2m$ when $m<\\infty$ and infinite dihedral when $m=\\infty$; every element of $\\langle s,t\\rangle$ acts on the quotient $E/\\operatorname{span}(\\alpha_s,\\alpha_t)$ as the identity, while for every $u\\in S\\setminus\\{s,t\\}$ one has $\\sigma_u(\\alpha_u)-\\alpha_u=-2\\alpha_u\\notin\\operatorname{span}(\\alpha_s,\\alpha_t)$ (no induced quotient map for $\\sigma_u$ is assumed). Consequently\n$$S\\cap\\langle s,t\\rangle=\\{s,t\\},$$\nand every element of $\\langle s,t\\rangle$ has a reduced expression with all letters in $\\{s,t\\}$ (so the alternating words of length $q\\le m$, and any $q$ when $m=\\infty$, are reduced in $W$).",
