        {
          "fact": "F5",
          "source": "thm-hh-generic-coxeter-hecke-standard-basis",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $(S,m)$, $W$, $\\ell$ be as in [[def-hh-coxeter-matrix-word-group-and-length]]; let $R$, $v_s$, $H$, $T_s$ be as in [[def-hh-universal-coxeter-hecke-parameters-and-presentation]]; let $T_w$ for $w\\in W$ and the spanning statement be as in [[lem-hh-reduced-word-independence-and-length-multiplication]]; and let $E$, $P_s$, $Q_s$ and $P_w$ be as in [[lem-hh-commuting-left-right-hecke-length-operators]].\n\n1. **The length-operator representation.** There is a unique unital $R$-algebra homomorphism $\\rho:H\\to\\operatorname{End}_R(E)$ with $\\rho(T_s)=P_s$ for all $s\\in S$; it satisfies $\\rho(T_w)=P_w$ and $\\rho(T_w)(e_1)=e_w$ for all $w\\in W$.\n2. **Standard basis.** $\\{T_w:w\\in W\\}$ is an $R$-basis of $H$: it spans by [[lem-hh-reduced-word-independence-and-length-multiplication]] and is $R$-linearly independent. Hence $H$ is free as an $R$-module and every element of $H$ has a unique expansion $\\sum_wa_wT_w$ with $a_w\\in R$ and all but finitely many $a_w$ zero.\n3. **Faithfulness.** $\\rho$ is injective.\n4. **Base change.** For every commutative ring $R'$ and every ring homomorphism $\\varphi:R\\to R'$, the scalar extension $R'\\otimes_RH$ is, as an $R'$-algebra, canonically isomorphic to the quotient of the free associative $R'$-algebra on $(T_s)_{s\\in S}$ by the two-sided ideal generated by the images under $\\varphi$ of the relations (Q) and (B) of [[def-hh-universal-coxeter-hecke-parameters-and-presentation]], and it is free as an $R'$-module with basis $(1\\otimes T_w)_{w\\in W}$. No flatness or freeness of $R'$ over $R$ is assumed, and no torsion-freeness or semisimplicity of $H$ or of its specialisations is claimed.",
