          "claim": "**Finite-support spanning.** Fix a finite $J\\subseteq S$. Its odd-edge components have a universal Laurent coefficient ring with one unit parameter for each component. By [F2], sending that parameter to $v^{L(s)}\\in A^\\times$ is independent of $s$ in the component, so it defines a coefficient-ring homomorphism. By [F4] and [F5], the finite Hecke algebra on $J$, after this base change, has basis $\\{T_u:u\\in W_J\\}$. Every word representing an element of the global presented algebra uses some finite $J$, so applying this finite spanning statement to that word shows that the global elements $T_w$ span $H_A(W,L)$.",
