          "id": "step-2-1",
          "step": "2.1",
          "claim": "Set $D_w=\\overline{T_w}-T_w$. By [F2], there are unique coefficients $a_y\\in A$ with $D_w=\\sum_{y<w}a_yC_y$. Since bar is an involution and each $C_y$ is bar invariant by induction, $\\overline{D_w}=-D_w$ implies $\\sum_{y<w}\\overline{a_y}C_y=-\\sum_{y<w}a_yC_y$. The basis property in step 1.1 gives $\\overline{a_y}=-a_y$ for each $y<w$.",
          "inputs": [
