          "id": "step-5-1",
          "step": "5.1",
          "claim": "For a simple generator $s$, write $C_s=T_s+p$ with $p\\in A_{<0}$. The bar formula in [F2] gives $\\overline{T_s}=T_s-v^{L(s)}+v^{-L(s)}$. Bar invariance is therefore equivalent to $p-\\overline p=v^{-L(s)}-v^{L(s)}$. Splitting into negative and positive exponents gives $p=v^{-L(s)}$ if $L(s)>0$, $p=0$ if $L(s)=0$, and $p=-v^{L(s)}$ if $L(s)<0$, proving the displayed normalization by uniqueness.",
