          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "thm-unequal-parameter-kazhdan-lusztig-basis",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $S$ be any set with Coxeter group $W$, let $L:W\\to\\Gamma$ be any weight function into a totally ordered abelian group, let $A=\\mathbb Z[\\Gamma]$, and let $H_A(W,L)$ and its bar involution be as above. For each $w\\in W$, there is a unique element $C_w\\in H_A(W,L)$ such that\n$$\n\\overline{C_w}=C_w,\\qquad C_w=T_w+\\sum_{y<w}p_{y,w}T_y,\\qquad p_{y,w}\\in A_{<0}.\n$$\nThe family $\\{C_w:w\\in W\\}$ is an $A$-basis. For a simple generator $s$ the normalization is\n$$C_s=\\begin{cases}T_s+v^{-L(s)},&L(s)>0,\\\\T_s,&L(s)=0,\\\\T_s-v^{L(s)},&L(s)<0.\\end{cases}$$",
