          "claim": "**The left spans are left ideals.** If $C_x$ occurs in $C_sC_y$, then $x\\leftarrow_L y$, hence $x\\le_L y$. Therefore, if $y\\le_L\\mathcal C$, every basis term in $C_sC_y$ also has index $\\le_L\\mathcal C$, proving closure of $I^L_{\\le\\mathcal C}$ under left multiplication by each $C_s$. If $y<_{L}\\mathcal C$, each such $x$ is also outside $\\mathcal C$: otherwise some $g\\in\\mathcal C$ satisfies $g\\le_L x\\le_L y\\le_L g$, forcing $y\\in\\mathcal C$, a contradiction. Thus $I^L_{<\\mathcal C}$ is also closed under left multiplication by each $C_s$. Since $T_s=C_s-\\eta_s$, the $C_s$ and scalars generate $H_A(W,L)$, so both spans are left ideals.",
