          "source": "lem-asymptotic-induction-identifies-leading-modular-simples",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "In the finite-Weyl setting of [[def-finite-weyl-lusztig-basic-set-data]], assume its specified Lusztig properties and let $\\theta:A\\to k$ have characteristic zero or satisfy $\\theta(f_E)\\ne0$ for every generic simple label $E$. Write $H=H_k$, and let $V_E$ be the corresponding simple module of the split asymptotic algebra $J_k$, supported in degree $\\alpha_E$. A star denotes restriction through $\\phi_k:H\\to J_k$.\n\nFor each simple $H$-module $M$, let $a_M=\\max\\{a(w):D_wM\\ne0\\}$, where $D_w=C_w^\\dagger$. There is an injective assignment $M\\mapsto E(M)$ such that $\\alpha_{E(M)}=a_M$, $M$ occurs once in $*V_{E(M)}$, and all its other simple factors have strictly smaller $a$-value. Moreover $H$ is split: every simple $H$-module remains simple over every field extension.",
