          "source": "thm-unequal-parameter-cell-quotients-are-modules",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For every Coxeter system and weight function of [[def-unequal-parameter-coxeter-hecke-algebra]], the spans $I^L_{\\le\\mathcal C}$ and $I^L_{<\\mathcal C}$ attached to a left cell are left ideals; the right-cell spans are right ideals; and the two-sided-cell spans are two-sided ideals. Therefore the quotients defined in [[def-unequal-parameter-cells-and-cell-quotients]] are left modules, right modules, or bimodules, respectively. Each quotient has an $A$-basis consisting exactly of the images of the KL basis elements indexed by its cell. No further cell property, semisimplicity, or irreducible-module classification is asserted.",
