          "source": "lem-complete-local-hecke-modular-systems-and-idempotent-lifting",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice. Let $A=\\mathbb Z[v,v^{-1}]$ and let $\\theta:A\\to k$ be a unital homomorphism to a field. Set $\\mathfrak p=\\ker\\theta$, $k_0=\\operatorname{Frac}(A/\\mathfrak p)\\subseteq k$, and let $R$ be the maximal-adic completion of $A_{\\mathfrak p}$. Then $R$ is a complete separated Noetherian local domain with residue field $k_0$, and $A\\to R$ is injective. Thus $\\mathbb Q(v)$ embeds in $F=\\operatorname{Frac}R$, and $A\\to R\\to k_0\\to k$ equals $\\theta$.\n\nEvery finite projective $R$-module is free, with equal fraction-field and residue-field dimensions. In every finite associative unital $R$-algebra $C$, every idempotent of $C/\\mathfrak m_R C$ lifts to an idempotent of $C$. For any right $C$-module, multiplication by such an idempotent is an exact projection commuting with scalar extension. In particular, a filtration with finite free layers remains exact on its projected layers after passing to $F$ or $k_0$. If $J_R=\\bigoplus_E M_{d_E}(R)$, every $R$-finite-free $J_R$-module has the same simple multiplicities in its generic and residue fibres.",
