          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice and the finite-Weyl data and Lusztig properties of [[def-finite-weyl-lusztig-basic-set-data]]. Let $\\theta:A\\to k$ have characteristic zero or $\\theta(f_E)\\ne0$ for every generic simple label $E$. Put $k_0=\\operatorname{Frac}(\\theta(A))\\subseteq k$, let $R=\\widehat{A_{\\ker\\theta}}$, and let $F=\\operatorname{Frac}R$. Take the explicit global free model $L_{E,A}=A\\otimes_{\\mathbb Z}\\Lambda_E$ of the Schur supplier, whose Hecke matrices are integral because the $J$-matrices and $\\phi_A$ are integral. Let $L_E=R\\otimes_A L_{E,A}$. This is the standard free module of the $E$-matrix block of $J_R$, restricted through $\\phi_R$; its freeness is by this construction, not an inference from torsion-freeness over $R$. Its fraction fibre is the generic simple $E_F$; its residue is the restricted asymptotic simple $*V_E$. Define\n$$\nd_{E,M}=[k\\otimes_{k_0}(L_E/\\mathfrak m_RL_E):M]\n$$\nfor simple $H_k$-modules $M$. These multiplicities agree with those of any other free stable $R$-models of the same generic simples. They are unchanged by extension from $k_0$ to $k$, using the simple-label bijection.\n\nFor a simple $H_k$-module $M$, choose an idempotent $e\\in H_k$ such that $H_ke$ is its projective cover. Regarding the layers $B_i=I_i/I_{i+1}$ as left $J_k$-modules and right $H_k$-modules, one has\n$$\n\\operatorname{mult}_{J_k}(V_E,B_ie)=\\begin{cases}d_{E,M},&i=\\alpha_E,\\\\0,&i\\ne\\alpha_E.\\end{cases}\n$$\nMoreover $d_{E,M}=[*V_E:M]$. No identification of the right action on $B_i$ with right multiplication by $\\phi_k$ is assumed.",
