          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $S$ be any set with Coxeter matrix $m$, let $(W,S)$ be the presented system of [[def-arbitrary-rank-coxeter-system-and-bruhat-order]], and let $\\Gamma$ be the ordered abelian group of [[def-unequal-parameter-weight-function-and-coefficient-order]]. Every weight function $L:W\\to\\Gamma$ has $L(s)=L(t)$ whenever $s\\ne t$, $m(s,t)<\\infty$, and $m(s,t)$ is odd. Conversely, every label map $\\lambda:S\\to\\Gamma$ satisfying these odd-edge equalities extends uniquely to a weight function with $L(s)=\\lambda(s)$.",
