          "quote": "Let $S$ be any set with Coxeter matrix $m$, and let $W,\\ell,T,\\le$ be as in [[def-arbitrary-rank-coxeter-system-and-bruhat-order]]. For a finite $J\\subseteq S$, let $W_J^*$ be the group presented by the restricted matrix $m|_J$, and let $\\phi_J:W_J^*\\to W$ send each generator to the same-named element.\n\n1. The map $\\phi_J$ is injective with image $\\langle J\\rangle$, and intrinsic length in $W_J^*$ equals ambient length in $W$ on this subgroup.\n2. For $y,w\\in W$, $y\\le w$ if and only if a reduced expression of $y$ occurs as a subword of any fixed reduced expression of $w$. In particular, the interval $\\{y:y\\le w\\}$ is finite and has at most $2^{\\ell(w)}$ elements.\n3. For every $s\\in S$ and $w\\in W$, $\\ell(sw)=\\ell(w)\\pm1$ and $\\ell(ws)=\\ell(w)\\pm1$.",
