          "source": "lem-hh-root-datum-affine-geometry-and-wall-parameters",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For the reduced based root datum and wall definitions of [[def-hh-affine-hecke-algebra-from-root-datum]], $W_{\\mathrm{aff}}=Q^\\vee\\rtimes W_0$ is the Coxeter group on the base alcove's wall reflections, acts simply transitively on alcoves, and has length equal to the number of separating walls. The extended group $Y\\rtimes W_0$ preserves the wall arrangement and equals $W_{\\mathrm{aff}}\\rtimes\\Omega$, where $\\Omega$ is the alcove stabilizer. These claims include empty roots and central lattice directions. Every affine wall reflection is conjugate to a simple affine wall reflection. If the positive parameters on simple walls are constant on extended conjugacy classes, they therefore give a well-defined parameter $v(H)>0$ on every wall. For simple $\\alpha$, put $v_\\alpha=v(H_{\\alpha,0})$. The parameter of $H_{\\alpha,j}$ is $v_\\alpha$ for even $j$ and $v'_\\alpha:=v(H_{\\alpha,1})$ for odd $j$; if $\\alpha\\notin2X$, these two values agree.",
