          "source": "def-cg-affine-root-hyperplane-reflection-and-alcove",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Let $E$ be a finite-dimensional real inner-product space with inner product $B$ ([[def-inner-product-space]]). Equip it with the induced norm $\\|x\\|_B=\\sqrt{B(x,x)}$ ([[def-inner-product-norm]], [[cor-inner-product-induces-a-norm]]) and metric $d_B(x,y)=\\|x-y\\|_B$ ([[def-norm-and-normed-space]]); $\\mathrm{Isom}(E)$ below means the isometry group for $d_B$ ([[def-isometry-and-metric-embedding]]). Let $\\Phi\\subseteq E$ be a supplied reduced crystallographic root system spanning $E$ ([[def-reduced-crystallographic-euclidean-root-system]]). For each $\\alpha\\in\\Phi$, put $\\alpha^\\vee=2\\alpha/B(\\alpha,\\alpha)$ ([[def-coroot-and-dual-root-system]]); write $s_\\alpha$ for the orthogonal reflection in the hyperplane $B(x,\\alpha)=0$ and $W=W(\\Phi)=\\langle s_\\alpha:\\alpha\\in\\Phi\\rangle$ for the Weyl group ([[def-weyl-group-of-a-root-system]]). Write $Q=\\sum_{\\alpha\\in\\Phi}\\mathbb Z\\alpha$ and $Q^\\vee=\\sum_{\\alpha\\in\\Phi}\\mathbb Z\\alpha^\\vee$ for the root and coroot lattices ([[def-root-lattice-coroot-lattice-weight-lattice-and-coweight-lattice]]), and fix a positive system with base $\\Delta=\\{\\alpha_s:s\\in S\\}$ ([[def-positive-system-and-base-of-simple-roots]]).\n\nFor $\\alpha\\in\\Phi$ and $k\\in\\mathbb Z$, define\n$$H_{\\alpha,k}:=\\{x\\in E:B(x,\\alpha)=k\\},\\qquad r_{\\alpha,k}(x):=x-\\bigl(B(x,\\alpha)-k\\bigr)\\alpha^\\vee.$$\nEach $H_{\\alpha,k}$ is an affine hyperplane: $B(-,\\alpha)$ is a nonzero linear functional, and $k\\alpha/B(\\alpha,\\alpha)$ lies in its level-$k$ set. The sets $H_{\\alpha,k}$ are the **affine root hyperplanes** or **walls**, and\n$$\\mathcal A_\\Phi:=\\{H_{\\alpha,k}:\\alpha\\in\\Phi,\\ k\\in\\mathbb Z\\}$$\nis their **affine wall arrangement**. An **alcove** is a connected component of $E\\setminus\\bigcup\\mathcal A_\\Phi$, with the subspace topology ([[def-subspace-topology-top]], [[def-connected-component-and-quasicomponent]]).\n\nThe **affine reflection group** $W_a$ is the subgroup of the Euclidean isometry group $\\mathrm{Isom}(E)$ generated by the maps $r_{\\alpha,k}$ ([[def-generated-subgroup]], [[def-isometry-and-metric-embedding]]). The well-definedness obligation for this subgroup is assigned to `lem-cg-affine-reflection-identities-and-local-finiteness`, which verifies that each generator is an isometry. The **coroot translation group** is the image of the homomorphism $Q^\\vee\\to\\mathrm{Isom}(E)$, $\\lambda\\mapsto t_\\lambda$, where $t_\\lambda(x)=x+\\lambda$.\n\nThe Weyl group acts on $Q^\\vee$ by $w\\cdot\\lambda:=w(\\lambda)$. This action is by automorphisms: $W$ permutes $\\Phi$, and for every root $\\alpha$,\n$$w(\\alpha^\\vee)=\\frac{2w\\alpha}{B(\\alpha,\\alpha)}=\\frac{2w\\alpha}{B(w\\alpha,w\\alpha)}=(w\\alpha)^\\vee,$$\nso $w(Q^\\vee)=Q^\\vee$ and the restriction has inverse $w^{-1}|_{Q^\\vee}$. These restrictions compose according to multiplication in $W$, giving the action required for the external semidirect product $Q^\\vee\\rtimes W$ ([[def-group-action]], [[def-action-by-automorphisms]], [[def-external-semidirect-product]]), whose multiplication is\n$$(\\lambda,w)(\\mu,v)=(\\lambda+w\\mu,wv).$$\n\nThis item fixes the definitions and conventions. It does not assert $W_a=Q^\\vee\\rtimes W$, local finiteness of the arrangement, that alcoves are simplices, or that any specified alcove is a fundamental domain. The root system is supplied; no crystallographic scaling for a Coxeter matrix is constructed, and non-crystallographic types are outside this definition. No choice principle is used.",
