          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "def-rational-cherednik-standard-module",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Fix a finite-dimensional representation $E$ of $W$. Regard $E$ as a module over the subalgebra $\\mathbb C[\\mathfrak h]\\rtimes\\mathbb C W$ of $H_{1,c}(W,\\mathfrak h)$ by letting $W$ act as given and every $y\\in\\mathfrak h$ act as zero. The **standard module** associated to $E$ is\n$$\\Delta_c(E)=H_{1,c}(W,\\mathfrak h)\\otimes_{\\mathbb C[\\mathfrak h]\\rtimes\\mathbb C W}E.$$\nBy the PBW theorem [[thm-rational-cherednik-pbw-theorem]], multiplication identifies its underlying vector space with $\\mathbb C[\\mathfrak h^*]\\otimes_{\\mathbb C}E$. This item defines the induced module and vector-space description; its membership in $\\mathcal O_c(W,\\mathfrak h)$ is proved in [[thm-rational-cherednik-standard-module-lies-in-category-o]].",
