          "quote": "Let $R=\\mathbb C[x_1,\\ldots,x_n][f^{-1}]$ with $0\\ne f$, and let $N$ be a finite $R$-module with operators $\\nabla_i$ satisfying $\\nabla_i(a v)=(\\partial_i a)v+a\\nabla_i(v)$. At every complex point $p$ with $f(p)\\ne0$, $N_p$ is free over $R_{\\mathfrak m_p}$, and this basis extends to an algebraic open neighborhood of $p$. Thus its coherent sheaf on the complex principal open is an algebraic vector bundle. A finite submodule stable under these operators, and its quotient, have the same property. Integrability is unnecessary for local freeness; if the operators commute, these bundles carry the induced integrable connections. Short exact sequences of such bundles give exact fiber sequences.",
