          "quote": "For every $n\\ge0$ the localized generalized standard family $G_{n,c}$ is a finite-rank trivial vector bundle with flat connection whose matrices depend polynomially on the parameter $c$. Its KZ monodromy matrices depend holomorphically on $c$, and for every finite complex reflection group and every parameter the exact defining meridian polynomials of $\\mathcal H_{q(c)}(W)$ annihilate $\\operatorname{KZ}(G_{n,c})$. Therefore these polynomials annihilate $\\operatorname{KZ}(M)$ for every $M\\in\\mathcal O_c$. This includes all resonant parameters and makes no claim that resonant meridian monodromy is diagonalizable.",
