          "claim": "Let $\\gamma\\in\\widehat{\\mathbb R^D}$. For the coordinate vectors $e_j$, each restriction $t\\mapsto\\gamma(te_j)$ is a continuous character, so [F2] gives unique $\\xi_j\\in\\mathbb R$ with $\\gamma(te_j)=e^{2\\pi i\\xi_jt}$. Since $a=\\sum_j a^je_j$ and $\\gamma$ is a homomorphism, $\\gamma(a)=\\prod_j e^{2\\pi i\\xi_ja^j}=\\chi_p(a)$ for $p^0=-2\\pi\\xi_0$ and $p^j=2\\pi\\xi_j$ for $j>0$. The same restrictions show uniqueness, so $p\\mapsto\\chi_p$ is a bijection.",
