          "quote": "For generic $q$, or whenever the quantum integers needed for $p_r,p_s,p_t$ are units, the unnormalized trivalent theta pairing satisfies\n\n$$\\Theta(r,s,t)=\\frac{[m]![n']![p]![m+n'+p+1]!}{[m+n']![n'+p]![m+p]!},$$\n\nwhere $m=(r+s-t)/2$, $n'=(s+t-r)/2$, $p=(t+r-s)/2$ are nonnegative integers. The vertices and exact unit domain are those of [[lem-temperley-lieb-general-theta-net-evaluation]]. At $q=e^{\\pi i/\\ell}$, $\\ell\\ge3$, and $0\\le r,s,t\\le\\ell-2$, the pairing is positive when the triangle/parity conditions hold and $r+s+t\\le2\\ell-4$; it is zero for a triangle/parity triple above that level. A triple requiring an undefined root JW projector is not implicitly included.\n\nPut $k=\\ell-2$ and quotient the diagram category by the tensor ideal generated by $p_{k+1}$. A retained path of length $n$ is $a=(a_0,\\ldots,a_n)$ with $a_0=0$, $0\\le a_i\\le k$ and $|a_i-a_{i-1}|=1$. There are inclusions $i_a:p_{a_n}\\to n$ and retractions $r_a:n\\to p_{a_n}$ such that $r_ai_b=0$ for distinct paths, $r_ai_a=p_{a_n}$, and $\\sum_a i_ar_a=1_n$. Consequently the $E_{a,b}=i_ar_b$ at a common endpoint form complete matrix units, with\n\n$$E_{a,b}E_{c,d}=\\delta_{b,c}E_{a,d},\\qquad \\operatorname{Tr}_n(E_{a,b})=\\delta_{a,b}[a_n+1]_q.$$\n\nTheir pairing is nondegenerate. The endpoint $p_{k+1}$ is deleted before normalization; no denominator $[\\ell]$ is used.",
