          "claim": "For an integer $r$ with $0<|r|<2\\ell$, put $C_r=\\sum_{m=1}^{\\ell-1}\\cos(rm\\pi/\\ell)$. If $r$ is even, then $z=e^{2\\pi i(r/2)/\\ell}$ is a nontrivial $\\ell$-th root of unity; the geometric sum $\\sum_{m=0}^{\\ell-1}z^m=0$ has real part $1+C_r$, so $C_r=-1$. If $r$ is odd, the geometric sum of $e^{i\\pi rm/\\ell}$ for $0\\le m<2\\ell$ is zero. Pairing terms at $m$ and $2\\ell-m$ for $1\\le m\\le\\ell-1$ leaves twice $C_r$; the two unpaired real terms are $1+\\cos(r\\pi)=0$, so $C_r=0$. Also $C_0=\\ell-1$.",
