    "lem-lagrangian-relation-sends-lagrangian-to-lagrangian": {
      "citations": [
        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "def-isotropic-coisotropic-symplectic-and-lagrangian-subspaces",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Let $W$ be a subspace of a symplectic vector space $(V,\\omega)$, with\n[[def-symplectic-orthogonal-complement|symplectic orthogonal]] $W^\\omega$.\nThen $W$ is\n\n- **isotropic** when $W\\subseteq W^\\omega$, equivalently $\\omega|_{W\\times W}=0$;\n- **coisotropic** when $W^\\omega\\subseteq W$;\n- **symplectic** when $\\omega|_{W\\times W}$ is nondegenerate, equivalently\n  $W\\cap W^\\omega=0$; and\n- **Lagrangian** when $W=W^\\omega$.\n\nThe zero subspace is isotropic (and Lagrangian only when $V=0$), while $V$ is\ncoisotropic and symplectic.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "2.1",
            "3.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "thm-rank-nullity",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $T:V\\to W$ be a linear map of vector spaces over $F$, with $V$\nfinite-dimensional. Then\n\n$$\\dim_F V=\\operatorname{nullity}T+\\operatorname{rank}T.$$\n\nEquivalently,\n\n$$\\dim_F V=\\dim_F(\\ker T)+\\dim_F(\\operatorname{im}T).$$",
          "uses": [
            "2.1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "step": "1.1",
          "claim": "Let $K=\\Lambda\\cap(L\\oplus W)$. Projection $p_W:K\\to W$ has image $R_\\Lambda(L)$ and kernel $T=\\{x\\in L:(x,0)\\in\\Lambda\\}$. For $(x,y),(x',y')\\in K$, isotropy of $\\Lambda$ gives $-\\omega_V(x,x')+\\omega_W(y,y')=0$; isotropy of $L$ makes the first term zero. Hence $R_\\Lambda(L)$ is isotropic.",
          "inputs": [
            "F1",
            "given",
            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-2-1",
          "step": "2.1",
          "claim": "In $\\overline V\\oplus W$, the orthogonal complement of $L\\oplus W$ is $L\\oplus0$, because $L^\\perp=L$. Since $\\Lambda=\\Lambda^\\perp$, the orthogonal complement of $\\Lambda+(L\\oplus W)$ is $\\Lambda\\cap(L\\oplus0)$, of dimension $\\dim T$. For any subspace $U$ of a finite-dimensional symplectic space, the map $v\\mapsto\\omega(v,-)|_U$ onto $U^*$ is surjective: extend a functional from a basis of $U$ to the ambient space and use the isomorphism defined by the nondegenerate form. Its kernel is $U^\\perp$, so $\\dim U^\\perp=\\dim V-\\dim U$. Rank-nullity and [F2] therefore give\n$\\dim K=(n+m)+(n+2m)-(2n+2m-\\dim T)=m+\\dim T.$\nThe kernel of $p_W|_K$ has dimension $\\dim T$, so $\\dim R_\\Lambda(L)=m$.",
          "inputs": [
            "F1",
            "F2",
            "step 1.1",
            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-3-1",
          "step": "3.1",
          "claim": "The isotropic subspace $R_\\Lambda(L)$ has dimension $m$. The formula proved in step 2.1 gives $\\dim R_\\Lambda(L)^\\perp=2m-m=m$. Since isotropy gives $R_\\Lambda(L)\\subseteq R_\\Lambda(L)^\\perp$, equality follows; this is the definition of Lagrangian in [F1].",
          "inputs": [
            "F1",
            "step 1.1",
            "step 2.1"
          ]
        }
      ],
