        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "def-rigid-object-and-rigid-monoidal-category",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "An object of a monoidal category is **rigid** if it has both a left dual and a\nright dual in the sense of [[def-left-dual-and-right-dual-object]].\n\nA monoidal category is **rigid** if every object in it is rigid.\n\nMuger's notes also use the word **autonomous** for the same condition, and\nJoyal-Street use **compact** in the non-symmetric setting.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "def-fusion-and-multifusion-category",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "A **multifusion category** is a finite semisimple multitensor category. A\n**fusion category** is a finite semisimple tensor category. In particular the\nunit of a fusion category is simple, whereas a multifusion unit may split.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "def-the-categorical-trace-of-a-morphism-into-the-double-dual",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Fix a rigid monoidal category with chosen left duals. For a morphism\n$a:X\\to X^{\\vee\\vee}$, the **left categorical trace** of $a$ is the endomorphism\nof the unit\n\n$$\\operatorname{Tr}_L(a):\\mathbf 1\\xrightarrow{\\operatorname{coev}_X}X\\otimes X^\\vee\\xrightarrow{a\\otimes1_{X^\\vee}}X^{\\vee\\vee}\\otimes X^\\vee\\xrightarrow{\\operatorname{ev}_{X^\\vee}}\\mathbf 1.$$\n\nFor a morphism $b:X^{\\vee\\vee}\\to X$, the **right categorical trace** of $b$ is\n\n$$\\operatorname{Tr}_R(b):\\mathbf 1\\xrightarrow{\\operatorname{coev}_{X^\\vee}}X^\\vee\\otimes X^{\\vee\\vee}\\xrightarrow{1_{X^\\vee}\\otimes b}X^\\vee\\otimes X\\xrightarrow{\\operatorname{ev}_X}\\mathbf 1.$$\n\nSo a bare endomorphism $X\\to X$ is not yet an input to categorical trace; one\nfirst needs a comparison between $X$ and a double dual.",
          "uses": [
            "2.1"
          ]
        }
      ],
