          "source": "lem-kirby-color-full-band-slide-and-coupon-identity",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $\\mathcal C$ be a complex finite semisimple spherical ribbon category with simple unit and finite simple-label set $I$, with every $d_i\\ne0$. Put $\\Omega=\\sum_i d_i i$ and use the multicolored arbitrary-coupon evaluator of [[lem-multicolored-ribbon-coupon-evaluation]]. The entire graph evaluation is unchanged under a framed band slide of one $\\Omega$-colored surgery component over another. It is also unchanged under sliding an open strand of any fixed color, or a strand of an arbitrary coupon-bearing colored graph, over an $\\Omega$-colored surgery component, keeping every original color and coupon morphism fixed. All exterior crossings, open boundary factors and coupons are included, not merely a meridian scalar or closed trace. Orientations may be reversed with dual labels; no positivity or unitarity is assumed.\n\nHere is the exact algebraic contract. Let $B=\\bigoplus_i i^*\\otimes i$ with inclusions $\\iota_i$. Define $\\iota_X,\\Delta,\\varepsilon,m$ by the finite formulas in the proof, and put $\\Lambda=\\sum_i d_i\\iota_i b_i^R$. Then\n\n$$m(1_B\\otimes\\Lambda)=\\Lambda\\varepsilon,\\qquad\\Gamma=(1_B\\otimes m)(\\Delta\\otimes1_B),\\qquad\\Gamma(1_B\\otimes\\Lambda)=1_B\\otimes\\Lambda,\\qquad\\Gamma(\\Lambda\\otimes\\Lambda)=\\Lambda\\otimes\\Lambda.$$\n\nFor a fixed object $Y$ the lifted open-strand operator, retaining its entire first tensor factor, is\n\n$$\\widehat\\Gamma_Y=(1_{Y^*\\otimes Y}\\otimes m)(1_{Y^*\\otimes Y}\\otimes\\iota_Y\\otimes1_B)(1_{Y^*}\\otimes b_Y\\otimes1_Y\\otimes1_B),$$\n\nand it satisfies $\\widehat\\Gamma_Y(1_{Y^*\\otimes Y}\\otimes\\Lambda)=1_{Y^*\\otimes Y}\\otimes\\Lambda$. Its exterior requires dinaturality only in the surgery-component variable; there is no naturality assumption on an arbitrary family of graph coupons indexed by $Y$. This lemma has no Gauss-sum, Fenn–Rourke, surgery normalization or topological move-completeness premise.",
