          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Let $G$ be a finite abelian group, written additively. A normalized **abelian 3-cocycle** is a pair of functions $\\omega:G^3\\to\\mathbb C^\\times$ and $r:G^2\\to\\mathbb C^\\times$, equal to $1$ whenever one of their arguments is $0$, satisfying the pentagon equation\n\n$$\\omega(a,b,c)\\omega(a,b+c,d)\\omega(b,c,d)=\\omega(a+b,c,d)\\omega(a,b,c+d)$$\n\nand the two braided hexagon equations\n\n$$\\omega(b,c,a)\\omega(a,b,c)r(a,b+c)=r(a,b)r(a,c)\\omega(b,a,c),$$\n\n$$r(a+b,c)=\\omega(a,b,c)\\omega(c,a,b)\\omega(a,c,b)^{-1}r(a,c)r(b,c).$$\n\nThe associated pointed category has one simple object $g$ in each grade $g\\in G$, tensor product $g\\otimes h=g+h$, associator $\\alpha_{g,h,k}:(g\\otimes h)\\otimes k\\to g\\otimes(h\\otimes k)$ given by scalar $\\omega(g,h,k)$, and braiding $c_{g,h}:g\\otimes h\\to h\\otimes g$ given by scalar $r(g,h)$. For the left dual $g^\\vee=-g$, take evaluation $g^\\vee\\otimes g\\to0$ to have scalar $1$ and coevaluation $0\\to g\\otimes g^\\vee$ to have scalar $\\omega(g,-g,g)^{-1}$. The first snake is the identity by this choice; the second is the identity because the normalized pentagon at $(g,-g,g,-g)$ gives $\\omega(g,-g,g)\\omega(-g,g,-g)=1$. A ribbon twist is a function $q:G\\to\\mathbb C^\\times$ with $q(0)=1$, $q(-g)=q(g)$, and\n\n$$q(g+h)=r(g,h)r(h,g)q(g)q(h).$$\n\nWrite $b(g,h)=r(g,h)r(h,g)$ for the double-braiding scalar. The pointed ribbon category data include a compatible pivotal structure whose twist is $q$ and whose simple dimensions are $1$; this convention is an explicit input, not a consequence of the quadratic function alone. [[thm-pointed-metric-group-is-modular-iff-radical-trivial]] proves from the two hexagons that $b$ is a symmetric bicharacter and that the Hopf-link matrix has entries $s_{gh}=b(g,h)$. A quadratic function alone is not the category data: the associator, both hexagons, duality maps, and the stated pivotal convention are part of the definition.",
