          "id": "derivation-1.1",
          "step": "1.1",
          "claim": "Apply [F2] to the actual state space from [F3]. Its separating inverse resolves every simple summand and multiplicity, and its nonseparating inverse resolves $H$; hence it identifies the geometrically factored space with exactly the Hom space used in [F2]'s dimension calculation. The displayed formula holds for all $g,n$, including the exceptional spheres by [F2]. At $g=1,n=0$ every summand is $1$, giving $|I|$. The summand $\\operatorname{Hom}(\\mathbf1,i\\otimes i^*)$ has basis $b_i$ by rigidity and simplicity, so these are a basis of the unmarked torus space.",
