        {
          "id": "derivation-3.1",
          "step": "3.1",
          "claim": "Put $A=s_+t=\\left[\\begin{smallmatrix}0&1\\\\-1&-1\\end{smallmatrix}\\right]$. Direct multiplication gives $A^3=I$ and $s_+^2=-I$. Composing the weight-zero $s_+,t$ lifts introduces no weight because $t^{-1}\\alpha=\\alpha$, so its Maslov triple has a repeated argument. Thus $ST$ is the weight-zero lift of $A$. For its square the middle triple is $(A\\alpha,\\alpha,A^{-1}\\alpha)=(\\mathbb Rl,\\mathbb Rm,\\mathbb R(l-m))$. A sum-zero vector is $(-c l,c m,c(l-m))$, and its Walker form is $\\omega(-c l,c'm)=cc'$, so this Maslov index is $+1$. For its third power the first and third lines coincide: $A^2\\alpha=A^{-1}\\alpha$. The next correction is zero. Therefore the cubed weighted lift is $(I,1)$ and [F4]'s positive weight action gives $(ST)^3=\\kappa I$. Similarly the correction in $s_+s_+$ is $\\mu(l,m,l)=0$, so its operator is the weight-zero $-I$ lift, equal to $S^2=C$ by [F1]. These are geometric weighted relations, not an appeal to the desired modular matrix identity.",
