          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $(V,\\omega_V)$ and $(W,\\omega_W)$ be finite-dimensional real symplectic vector spaces of dimensions $2n$ and $2m$. Give $\\overline V\\oplus W$ the form $-\\omega_V\\oplus\\omega_W$. If $\\Lambda\\subseteq\\overline V\\oplus W$ is Lagrangian and $L\\subseteq V$ is Lagrangian, then\n\n$$R_\\Lambda(L)=\\{y\\in W:\\text{there is }x\\in L\\text{ with }(x,y)\\in\\Lambda\\}$$\n\nis Lagrangian in $W$.",
