        },
        {
          "id": "derivation-4.1",
          "step": "4.1",
          "claim": "For arbitrary $L,P$ and $N$ containing $K$, the four-Lagrangian identity gives $\\mu(L,P,N)-\\mu(L,P,N_0)=\\mu(L,N_0,N)-\\mu(P,N_0,N)$. Reduce the two right-hand terms by step 3.1 and apply that same identity in $K^\\perp/K$. Thus $\\mu_V(L,P,N)=\\mu_{K^\\perp/K}(L_K,P_K,N/K)+\\eta_K(L,P)$, where $\\eta_K(L,P)=\\mu_V(L,P,N_0)-\\mu_{K^\\perp/K}(L_K,P_K,N_0/K)$. In particular the defect is independent of $N$. The auxiliary $N_0$ disappears from the differences used below.",
