          "quote": "Assume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ ([[def-countable-choice]]). For every compact collared triad $(W;M_0,M_1)$ there are an adapted excellent Morse function $f:W\\to[0,1]$ and an adapted complete downward gradient-like field $X$, both agreeing with the product model on smaller neighborhoods in the fixed collars: $f=t_0/3$ near $M_0$, $f=1-t_1/3$ near $M_1$, and $X$ is its negative Riemannian gradient for a metric that is a product metric there. Here **adapted complete** has the collar-extension meaning of [[def-morse-function-adapted-to-a-cobordism]]: $X$ is the restriction of a complete smooth field on a boundaryless collar extension of $W$; a trajectory is followed in $W$ only until it exits a face.",
