          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Every continuous $f:X\\to Y$ factors as $f=p_fj_f$, where $j_f:X\\to E_f$ is a homotopy equivalence and $p_f:E_f\\to Y$ is a Hurewicz fibration. This holds for all ordinary spaces and, with the specified kified constructions, in CGWH. No surjectivity onto components disjoint from $f(X)$ is asserted. The result is choice-free.",
