          "fact": "F7",
          "source": "thm-signature-is-an-oriented-cobordism-invariant",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume AC, inherited from Poincare-Lefschetz duality. Let $W$ be a compact\noriented smooth $(4k+1)$-manifold with boundary $M=\\partial W$ carrying the\ninduced orientation and inclusion $i:M\\hookrightarrow W$. Then $\\sigma(M)=0$.\nConsequently, if $M_0,M_1$ are closed oriented $4k$-manifolds that are oriented\ncobordant ([[def-oriented-smooth-cobordism]]), then\n$\\sigma(M_0)=\\sigma(M_1)$: by [[def-oriented-smooth-cobordism]],\n$\\partial V=(-M_0)\\sqcup M_1$; reversing the orientation of $V$ gives\n$\\partial(-V)=M_0\\sqcup(-M_1)$ as an oriented boundary, so\n$0=\\sigma(M_0\\sqcup(-M_1))=\\sigma(M_0)-\\sigma(M_1)$ by\n[[lem-signature-is-additive-under-disjoint-union-and-orientation-reversal]].\nHence $\\sigma$ descends to a well-defined additive map on oriented bordism\nclasses $\\Omega_{4k}^{SO}\\to\\mathbb Z$ and vanishes on null-cobordant classes\n([[def-null-cobordant-closed-manifold]]).",
