      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "derivation-1.1",
          "step": "1.1",
          "claim": "Fix $q\\ge8$. The determinant-line sphere bundle over $BO(q)$ is its orientation double cover $BSO(q)$. Its mod-two Gysin sequence has multiplication by $w_1$ as its Euler map. This multiplication is injective in the polynomial ring of [F3], so pullback gives $H^*(BSO(q);\\mathbb F_2)=\\mathbb F_2[w_2,\\ldots,w_q]$. This uses the canonical mod-two orientation of the line bundle, rather than assuming it is integrally oriented. The same space has degreewise finitely generated integral homology by its lifted Schubert cells. It is simply connected: the universal oriented-frame bundle has contractible total space and connected fiber $SO(q)$, so its component sequence gives $\\pi_1BSO(q)=0$. The frame-bundle description and connectedness also follow from the actual sphere-bundle induction starting with the contractible $BSO(1)$.",
