        },
        {
          "id": "derivation-2.1",
          "step": "2.1",
          "claim": "With mod-two splitting roots $t_j$ of degree one, $Sq^1t_j=t_j^2$ and Cartan makes $Sq^1$ a derivation. Expand the elementary symmetric functions: in $w_1w_k$, the terms in which the extra root lies in the chosen $k$-subset are precisely $Sq^1w_k$; every $(k+1)$-subset occurs $k+1$ times among the other terms. Hence $Sq^1w_k=w_1w_k+(k-1)w_{k+1}$. On $BSO(q)$ this gives $Sq^1w_2=w_3$ and $Sq^1w_4=w_5$, both nonzero by step 1.1.",
