          "step": "2.2",
          "claim": "Freudenthal applies to the $(q-1)$-connected Thom CW space and gives $\\pi_{q+i}(T_q)\\cong\\pi_{q+i+1}(\\Sigma T_q)$ when $q+i\\le2q-2$. The unreduced suspension convention of [F5] agrees with the reduced Thom suspension after collapsing the contractible basepoint meridian; that CW collapse is a homotopy equivalence and respects the represented suspension map. For $i\\le4$, $q\\ge8$ satisfies both this range and step 1.2's range. Iteration identifies the actual finite-rank groups with the stable colimit. Thus [F1] gives $\\pi_{q+i}(T_q)=0$ for $1\\le i\\le3$ and $\\pi_{q+4}(T_q)=\\Omega^{SO}_4$. The bottom group $\\pi_q(T_q)=\\mathbb Z$ is supplied by the first Hurewicz theorem and step 1.2.",
