        {
          "id": "derivation-3.1",
          "step": "3.1",
          "claim": "The rational and odd-field calculations of [F3], with the coefficient UCT, give ranks zero for $H_2,H_3$, rank one for $H_4$, and no odd-primary torsion in these groups. Here $H_1=0$ by simple connectivity. Since $H^2(-;\\mathbb F_2)$ has dimension one, $H_2$ has exactly one two-primary cyclic summand. The nonzero $Sq^1w_2$ forces this summand to have order exactly two. Explicitly, for $\\mathbb Z/2^a$ the integral Bockstein of its nonzero $\\mathbb F_2$-valued homomorphism is $2^{a-1}$ in $\\operatorname{Ext}(\\mathbb Z/2^a,\\mathbb Z)=\\mathbb Z/2^a$, whose mod-two reduction is nonzero exactly when $a=1$; a free summand has zero Bockstein. Thus $H_2=\\mathbb Z/2$. The dimension-one group $H^3(-;\\mathbb F_2)$ is already accounted for by $\\operatorname{Ext}(H_2,\\mathbb F_2)$, so $H_3/2=0$ and $H_3=0$.",
