          "claim": "Represent the integral Thom class by $f:T_q\\to K(\\mathbb Z,q)$. It induces an isomorphism on $\\pi_q$: evaluation of the normalized class sends the bottom fiber sphere generator to one, and the first Hurewicz isomorphisms identify both groups with $\\mathbb Z$. Replace $f$ by its mapping-path fibration and let $F$ be its strict fiber. Its homotopy exact sequence, the sole nonzero homotopy group of $K(\\mathbb Z,q)$, and step 2.2 make $F$ $(q+3)$-connected and identify $\\pi_{q+4}F$ with $\\Omega^{SO}_4$. Apply the ordinary Hurewicz theorem to a CW approximation of $F$; the weak approximation induces both homotopy and integral singular-homology isomorphisms by [F6]. Consequently $\\Omega^{SO}_4\\cong H_{q+4}(F;\\mathbb Z)$ naturally under inclusion into $T_q$.",
