losed condition. Every relevant connecting segment eventually satisfies it, since its endpoints and its compact finite-time image lie in the interior. Only zeros satisfying this condition require the shears above; their neighborhoods can be chosen in the interior of $W$. Compactness controls all such zeros for nearby fields too. Possible ambient trajectories outside $W$ are not included and acquire no genericity claim. This resolves domain changes during the successive small perturbations. For the resulting family, dimension gives no index-increasing ordinary trajectory and locally isolated equal-index incidences. It also excludes simultaneous distinct equal-index trajectories, including pairs joined end-to-end at the same parameter. The derivative at an equal-index incidence is an isomorphism after quotienting the flow direction. On an incoming stable section this says exactly that its $i-1$ source-sphere directions and its one parameter direction span the $i$ normal unstable directions. This is the transversality hypothesis of the local framed-passage comparison, not full slice-wise Morse–Smale transversality.",
