          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "On the real vector space with orthonormal basis $b_i=[X_i]$, rigidity gives Frobenius reciprocity $N_{ij}^k=N_{i^*k}^j=N_{kj^*}^i$, and $N_{ij}^0=\\delta_{j,i^*}$. Indeed the adjunctions $\\operatorname{Hom}(X_i\\otimes X_j,X_k)\\cong\\operatorname{Hom}(X_j,X_i^*\\otimes X_k)$ and $\\operatorname{Hom}(X_i\\otimes X_j,X_k)\\cong\\operatorname{Hom}(X_i,X_k\\otimes X_j^*)$ give the first equalities by dimensions; simplicity of the unit gives the second. Left and right multiplication matrices $L_i,R_i$ therefore have transposes $L_{i^*},R_{i^*}$, respectively, and $L_iR_j=R_jL_i$ by associativity. The matrix $S=\\sum_i L_i$ is real symmetric and strictly positive entrywise: for any $a,b$, the nonzero object $X_b\\otimes X_a^*$ has a simple summand $X_i$, and reciprocity then gives $N_{ia}^b>0$. The object is nonzero because tensoring by a nonzero rigid object is faithful: the unit is a summand of its dual times itself, so a zero tensor product would force the other factor to be zero.",
