        },
        {
          "id": "step-3-1",
          "claim": "Since $R_i$ commutes with $S$, $R_iv=d_iv$ for a scalar $d_i$; it is positive because $R_i$ is nonzero and nonnegative and $v$ is strictly positive. Transposition and the scalar product give $d_i\\langle v,v\\rangle=\\langle v,R_iv\\rangle=\\langle R_{i^*}v,v\\rangle=d_{i^*}\\langle v,v\\rangle$. The coefficient of $b_0$ in $v b_i$ is $v_{i^*}$, so $d_i=v_{i^*}=v_i$. Right multiplication by a product now gives $d_id_j=\\sum_kN_{ij}^kd_k$, and $R_0=1$ gives $d_0=1$. These numbers are fixed by the fusion data, since $S$ and the normalization of its unique positive top eigenvector are fixed. Writing $\\Omega=\\sum_i d_i b_i=v$, we have $\\Omega b_i=d_i\\Omega$ and therefore $\\Omega^2=D\\Omega$ for $D=\\sum_i d_i^2$.",
