      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Choose representatives $a$ of the finitely many simple objects of $\\mathcal M$. Put $R(n)=\\bigoplus_a\\operatorname{Hom}_{\\mathcal N}(F(a),n)\\otimes_k a$ and $L(n)=\\bigoplus_a\\operatorname{Hom}_{\\mathcal N}(n,F(a))^*\\otimes_k a$. Since $\\operatorname{End}(a)=k$, decomposition into these simples gives natural bijections $\\operatorname{Hom}_{\\mathcal M}(m,Rn)=\\operatorname{Hom}_{\\mathcal N}(Fm,n)$ and $\\operatorname{Hom}_{\\mathcal M}(Ln,m)=\\operatorname{Hom}_{\\mathcal N}(n,Fm)$. Define the units and counits to represent the identity maps under these bijections. The two triangle identities follow by applying either bijection: in each case the composite corresponds to the original identity. Thus these are actual ordinary adjunctions, with no exactness or representability assumption left implicit.",
