          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $\\mathcal C$ be a fusion category over an algebraically closed field. Write $\\mathcal D=\\mathcal C\\boxtimes\\mathcal C^{\\mathrm{rev}}$, acting on $\\mathcal C$ by $(X\\boxtimes Y)\\cdot V=X\\otimes V\\otimes Y$. Choose duals with $\\operatorname{ev}_i:i\\otimes i^*\\to\\mathbf1$ and $\\operatorname{coev}_i:\\mathbf1\\to i^*\\otimes i$. The canonical algebra $K=\\underline{\\operatorname{End}}_{\\mathcal D}(\\mathbf1)$ is $\\bigoplus_i i\\boxtimes i^*$, with multiplication induced by composition of evaluations and unit the inclusion of the unit summand. Projection $\\lambda:K\\to\\mathbf1\\boxtimes\\mathbf1$ to that summand makes $\\beta=\\lambda\\mu$ a nondegenerate pairing. Its inverse $c:\\mathbf1\\to K\\otimes K$ defines a Frobenius comultiplication\n$$\\Delta=(\\mu\\otimes\\mathrm{id})(\\mathrm{id}\\otimes c)=(\\mathrm{id}\\otimes\\mu)(c\\otimes\\mathrm{id}).$$\nThis comultiplication is coassociative, is a $K$-bimodule morphism, and has counit $\\lambda$, with $\\lambda\\eta=1$. No nonvanishing dimension or pivotal structure is assumed.",
