          "quote": "Use the canonical algebra $K$ in $\\mathcal D=\\mathcal C\\boxtimes\\mathcal C^{\\mathrm{rev}}$ from [[lem-canonical-fusion-category-algebra-is-frobenius]]. Without a separability or characteristic-zero assumption, the functor $J:\\mathcal C\\to\\operatorname{Mod}_{\\mathcal D}(K)$ given by $J(V)=(V\\boxtimes\\mathbf1)\\otimes K$ is an equivalence. There are natural right $K$-module isomorphisms\n$$\\rho_V:(V\\boxtimes\\mathbf1)K\\longrightarrow(\\mathbf1\\boxtimes V)K.$$\nThey obey $\\rho_{\\mathbf1}=\\mathrm{id}$ and the sliding equation: $\\rho_{V\\otimes W}$ is the composite of $\\mathrm{id}_{V\\boxtimes\\mathbf1}\\otimes\\rho_W$, the interchange of the two separate Deligne factors, and $\\mathrm{id}_{\\mathbf1\\boxtimes W}\\otimes\\rho_V$. In particular any right $K$-linear map $J(V)\\to J(W)$ uniquely equals $f\\otimes\\mathrm{id}_K$ for $f:V\\to W$.",
