      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Left and right duals of a simple $i$ are isomorphic. Indeed, rigidity identifies the unique simple $j$ with $\\operatorname{Hom}(\\mathbf1,i\\otimes j)\\ne0$ as one dual, and the unique simple $j$ with $\\operatorname{Hom}(i\\otimes j,\\mathbf1)\\ne0$ as the other; semisimplicity makes both dimensions the multiplicity of the unit in $i\\otimes j$, so these simple labels coincide. Thus $i\\cong i^{**}$. Each of the two loops defining $d_i,e_i$ is nonzero: it is a nonzero inclusion of the multiplicity-one unit summand in a product of dual simples followed by a nonzero projection to that summand. Multiplicity one follows from $\\operatorname{End}(i)=k$ and rigidity. Any two $a_i$ differ by a scalar $t\\ne0$; this multiplies $d_i$ by $t$ and $e_i$ by $t^{-1}$. Hence $|i|^2$ is well-defined and nonzero.",
