        {
          "id": "step-1-2",
          "claim": "Put $\\mathcal D=\\mathcal C\\boxtimes\\mathcal C^{\\mathrm{rev}}$. The object $\\mathbf1\\in\\mathcal C$ is a generator for its regular left $\\mathcal D$-module action, since $(V\\boxtimes\\mathbf1)\\cdot\\mathbf1=V$. By F2, $H(V)=\\underline{\\operatorname{Hom}}(\\mathbf1,V)$ is an equivalence from $\\mathcal C$ to right $K$-modules. Rigidity and representability identify both $L_V=(V\\boxtimes\\mathbf1)K$ and $R_V=(\\mathbf1\\boxtimes V)K$ with $H(V)$: applying $\\operatorname{Hom}_{\\mathcal D}(X\\boxtimes Y,-)$ in each case gives $\\operatorname{Hom}_{\\mathcal C}(X\\otimes Y,V)$, by moving $V$ across the Hom using the appropriate dual. These identifications preserve the right action because both actions are composition of the representing evaluations. Thus $J:V\\mapsto L_V$ is fully faithful, and the identity on the represented Hom functor defines a right $K$-linear natural isomorphism $\\rho_V:L_V\\to R_V$.",
