          "id": "step-1-3",
          "claim": "We prove the algebraic mate calculation needed to dualize sliding. In any rigid category, let $A$ be a Frobenius algebra with $b=\\epsilon m$, and let $\\ell:A\\to A^\\vee$ be its perfect right-curried pairing, so $b=\\operatorname{ev}_A(\\ell\\otimes\\mathrm{id})$. Put $F=(-)^{\\vee\\vee}$, $q=(\\ell^{-1})^\\vee\\ell:A\\to F(A)$ and $b_R=\\operatorname{ev}_{A^\\vee}(\\mathrm{id}_{F(A)}\\otimes\\ell)$. Then $\\ell^\\vee q=\\ell$, hence $b_R(q\\otimes\\mathrm{id})=b$. For $t:U\\otimes V\\to\\mathbf1$ define its cyclic transpose, of source $F(V)\\otimes U$, by $R_{U,V}(t)=\\operatorname{ev}_{V^\\vee}\\bigl(\\mathrm{id}_{F(V)}\\otimes[(t\\otimes\\mathrm{id}_{V^\\vee})(\\mathrm{id}_U\\otimes\\operatorname{coev}_V)]\\bigr).$ The two snake identities make this operation invertible. Direct substitution proves naturality in $U$ and the rule $R_{U,W}(t(\\mathrm{id}_U\\otimes h))=R_{U,V}(t)(F(h)\\otimes\\mathrm{id}_U)$ for $h:W\\to V$. It also proves that two successive last-factor rotations equal rotation of their last-two-factor block: substitute the nested coevaluation formula for $V\\otimes W$ and the reverse-order evaluation formula, obtaining the same nested composite.",
