          "id": "step-2-1",
          "claim": "The sliding equation for $\\rho$ says that on $(V\\boxtimes\\mathbf1)(W\\boxtimes\\mathbf1)K$, sliding $W$ and then $V$, commuting the distinct exterior factors between these operations, equals sliding $V\\otimes W$. To verify it without a diagram, apply $\\operatorname{Hom}_{\\mathcal D}(X\\boxtimes Y,-)$ and the identifications of step 1.2. In either order the two adjunctions represent the same map $X\\otimes Y\\to V\\otimes W$. If intermediate simple decompositions are inserted, their inclusion/projection sum is $\\sum q_ap_a=\\mathrm{id}$, so erasing these sums gives the original map in both orders. The reverse-order tensor-dual evaluation is exactly the composite of the two evaluations, and the module associator equation identifies their parentheses. The unit case is evaluation against $\\mathbf1$. Yoneda proves the sliding and unit equations.",
