          "quote": "A **fusion 2-category** is a finite semisimple linear 2-category with a weak monoidal structure, a simple monoidal unit, and left and right duals for every object. For a right dual $A^\\#$ of $A$, the duality data include 1-morphisms\n$$e_A:A\\otimes A^\\#\\to I,\\qquad i_A:I\\to A^\\#\\otimes A,$$\nand invertible cusp 2-morphisms from $(e_A\\otimes A)\\circ(A\\otimes i_A)$ to $1_A$ and from $(A^\\#\\otimes e_A)\\circ(i_A\\otimes A^\\#)$ to $1_{A^\\#}$, with the associator and unitors inserted at the indicated sources and targets.\n\nFor a left dual ${}^\\#A$ of $A$, the data separately include 1-morphisms\n$$e_A^\\ell:{}^\\#A\\otimes A\\to I,\\qquad i_A^\\ell:I\\to A\\otimes{}^\\#A,$$\nand invertible cusp 2-morphisms from $(A\\otimes e_A^\\ell)\\circ(i_A^\\ell\\otimes A)$ to $1_A$ and from $(e_A^\\ell\\otimes{}^\\#A)\\circ({}^\\#A\\otimes i_A^\\ell)$ to $1_{{}^\\#A}$. The associator and unitors are inserted at these sources and targets as well. No identification of the chosen left and right duals is required.\n\nHere “simple unit” means that $1_I$ is a simple 1-morphism. A pivotal or spherical enhancement is extra structure: it requires its own duality coherence and trace axioms. Neither such enhancement nor a spherical trace is included in “fusion 2-category.”",
