          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "lem-canonical-fusion-category-algebra-is-separable",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $\\mathcal C$ be a fusion category over an algebraically closed field of characteristic zero. For the canonical Frobenius algebra $(K,\\mu,\\eta,\\Delta,\\lambda)$ constructed in [[lem-canonical-fusion-category-algebra-is-frobenius]], set $t=\\lambda\\mu\\Delta\\eta$. Then $t\\ne0$ and $s=t^{-1}\\Delta$ is a $K$-bimodule section of multiplication. In particular $K$ is separable, and $e=s\\eta$ satisfies\n$$\\mu e=\\eta,\\qquad(\\mu\\otimes\\mathrm{id})(\\mathrm{id}\\otimes e)=(\\mathrm{id}\\otimes\\mu)(e\\otimes\\mathrm{id}).$$",
          "uses": [
