        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "lem-separability-contracts-normalized-categorical-hochschild-complex",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $A$ be an algebra object in a $k$-linear monoidal category and $B$ an $A$-bimodule. Suppose $e:\\mathbf1\\to A\\otimes A$ satisfies\n$$\\mu e=\\eta,\\qquad (\\mu\\otimes\\mathrm{id})(\\mathrm{id}\\otimes e)=(\\mathrm{id}\\otimes\\mu)(e\\otimes\\mathrm{id}).$$\nSet $C^n=\\operatorname{Hom}(A^{\\otimes n},B)$, with the Hochschild differential given by the alternating sum of the left action, adjacent multiplications, and the right action. Its normalized subcomplex consists of maps vanishing whenever any input is the unit $\\eta$. For every $n\\geq1$, define\n$$h_n(f)=\\lambda_B(\\mathrm{id}_A\\otimes f)(e\\otimes\\mathrm{id}_{A^{\\otimes(n-1)}}),$$\nwhere $\\lambda_B$ denotes the left $A$-action. Then $h$ preserves the normalized subcomplex and $dh+hd=\\mathrm{id}$ in every positive degree.",
          "uses": [
