      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Put $\\mathcal E=\\operatorname{Fun}_k(\\mathcal M,\\mathcal N)$ and $\\mathcal Q=\\operatorname{End}_k(\\mathcal N)\\boxtimes\\operatorname{End}_k(\\mathcal M)^{\\mathrm{rev}}$. The action $(U\\boxtimes V)\\cdot S=USV$ makes $\\mathcal E$ a $\\mathcal Q$-module category. These underlying categories are finite semisimple: after choosing their finitely many simple objects, linear functors and transformations are finite matrices of vector spaces and linear maps. The two action functors give a tensor functor $\\mathcal C\\boxtimes\\mathcal C^{\\mathrm{rev}}\\to\\mathcal Q$. Let $A$ be the image of $K$ and $e_A$ the image of $e$; tensor functors preserve the two separability identities. The comparisons $\\gamma$ give an action $\\rho_T:A\\cdot T\\to T$: on a simple summand it is the adjoint of $\\gamma_i:N_iT\\to TM_i$, namely $N_iTM_{i^*}\\to T$. The product and unit equations for this action are exactly the module-functor equations, as one sees by inserting $\\sum q_a^rp_a^r=\\mathrm{id}_{i\\otimes j}$ in the displayed multiplication of $K$.",
          "step": "1.1",
          "inputs": [
            "given",
            "F1",
            "construct",
            "algebra"
          ]
