          "id": "step-4-1",
          "claim": "Denote this complex isomorphism by $\\Phi_n:C_T^n\\to\\operatorname{Hom}_{\\mathcal Q}(A^{\\otimes n},B_T)$. For $n\\geq1$ define the required homotopy by $$h_n(f)=\\Phi_{n-1}^{-1}\\bigl(\\lambda_{B_T}(\\mathrm{id}_A\\otimes\\Phi_n(f))(e_A\\otimes\\mathrm{id}_{A^{\\otimes(n-1)}})\\bigr).$$ All maps in this formula have been specified in the preceding steps. Fact [F2] and the complex isomorphism give $d h_n+h_{n+1}d=\\mathrm{id}_{C_T^n}$ and preservation of normalization. The same proof with $T=\\mathrm{id}_{\\mathcal M}$ gives the action complex; replacing $\\mathcal C$ by its tensor reversal gives the prescribed right-action convention. Thus every positive-degree cocycle is a coboundary, in particular every degree-two cocycle.",
