          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For a fixed fusion category $\\mathcal C$ over an algebraically closed field of characteristic zero, there is a finite integer $R(\\mathcal C)$ such that every indecomposable finite semisimple right $\\mathcal C$-module category has at most $R(\\mathcal C)$ isomorphism classes of simple objects. More explicitly, write $I$ for its simple labels, $0$ for the unit, and $N_{ij}^k$ for its fusion coefficients. There are positive real numbers $d_i=d_{i^*}$, determined by these coefficients, with $d_0=1$ and $d_id_j=\\sum_kN_{ij}^kd_k$. Put $D=\\sum_i d_i^2$. One may take $R(\\mathcal C)=\\lfloor D\\rfloor$. For every finite semisimple right module category, indecomposable or otherwise, the multiplicity $n_{ai}^b=[m_a\\odot X_i:m_b]$ satisfies $n_{ai}^b\\le D/d_i$. Consequently there are finitely many possible action multiplicity arrays at any specified rank, and finitely many indecomposable arrays at all ranks.\n\nThe real numbers used here concern the fusion ring, and are not categorical traces. No pivotal structure or positivity of categorical dimensions is assumed.",
