          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "A **complex associative algebra with involution** is a unital associative\nalgebra over $\\mathbb C$ as in [[def-algebra-over-a-commutative-ring]], equipped\nwith a conjugate-linear map $a\\mapsto a^*$ using complex conjugation from\n[[def-complex-conjugate-real-imaginary-part-and-modulus]] such that\n$(a^*)^*=a$, $(ab)^*=b^*a^*$, and $1^*=1$. Its **self-adjoint part** is\n\n$$ A_{\\rm sa}:=\\{a\\in A:a^*=a\\}. $$\n\nThe theorem [[thm-associative-symmetrization-satisfies-jordan-identity]] proves\nthat this subset is a real vector subspace closed under the symmetrized\nproduct.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "thm-associative-symmetrization-satisfies-jordan-identity",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $k$ be a field with $\\operatorname{char}(k)\\ne2$ and $A$ a unital\nassociative $k$-algebra. The product $a\\circ b=(ab+ba)/2$ makes $A^+$ of\n[[def-associative-jordan-product]] a Jordan algebra. If $A$ is a complex\nassociative algebra with involution as in\n[[def-involutive-complex-associative-algebra]], then its self-adjoint part\n$A_{\\rm sa}$ is a real vector subspace closed under $\\circ$, hence a real\nJordan subalgebra of $A^+$.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "2.1"
          ]
        }
      ],
