          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "lem-elementary-surface-sewing-relations",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "In the category $\\mathsf{Cob}^{\\mathrm{oc}}_2(S)$ of [[def-oriented-open-closed-surface-category]], the ten generator surfaces obey the boundary-relative equalities whose images under a strong symmetric monoidal functor are precisely equations 1–7 in [[def-frobenius-object-and-knowledgeable-sewing-data]]. Thus the closed pair of pants, disk, and reversed pair of pants give a commutative Frobenius object; the open pair of pants, disk, and reversed pair of pants give the indexed open algebra/coalgebra/Frobenius equations and cyclic trace; the zipper and cozipper give the central unital algebra map, pairing adjunction, and colored Cardy equality. Each equality preserves every black parametrization, corner endpoint color, and free-boundary label. This lemma proves the listed relations; it does not assert that they present all surface morphisms.\n\nFor the singleton color set, write $A=A_{**}$ and $i=i_*$, $i^*=i^*_*$; then the open pairing is symmetric, while commutativity is required only of $C$.",
