        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "lem-frobenius-sewing-derived-moves",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For S-colored knowledgeable data of [[def-frobenius-object-and-knowledgeable-sewing-data]], all of the following identities follow from its typed equations: open and closed evaluation/coevaluation snakes; symmetry and cyclic invariance of the pairings and their adjoint copairings; both zipper/cozipper pairing and copairing transports; coalgebra and counit preservation by each cozipper; sliding of closed-window and handle operators; the Cardy reduction of an open handle through the closed sector; and cyclic rotation of an open product followed by a cozipper. In particular, define\n$$\nb_{ab}:=\\epsilon_a\\mu_{aba}:A_{ab}\\otimes A_{ba}\\to k, \\qquad d_{ab}:=\\Delta_{aba}\\eta_a:k\\to A_{ab}\\otimes A_{ba}.\n$$\nBoth maps to algebraic duals induced by $b_{ab}$ and $b_{ba}$ are isomorphisms. With $b_C=\\epsilon_C\\mu_C$, $d_C=\\Delta_C\\eta_C$, $W_a=i_a^*i_a:C\\to C$, $H=\\mu_C\\Delta_C:C\\to C$, and $O_a=\\mu_{aaa}\\Delta_{aaa}:A_{aa}\\to A_{aa}$, the typed consequences include\n$$\n\\Delta_Ci_a^*=(i_a^*\\otimes i_a^*)\\Delta_{aaa},\\qquad \\epsilon_Ci_a^*=\\epsilon_a,\\qquad i_a^*O_a=W_ai_a^*.\n$$\nThe same map identities hold in the formal symmetric monoidal presentation generated by the ten typed elementary surfaces and their equations in [[lem-elementary-surface-sewing-relations]]. Here the tensor unit replaces $k$, and finite-dimensional dual-isomorphism statements are confined to the vector-space specialization. Thus the identities may be used as surface rewrites before classification. This formal assertion is proved by faithful bending in step 1.5; equality of vector-space evaluations alone is not used to infer a surface equality.",
          "uses": [
